{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm","id":1552676,"title":"What lore changes did you hate that was added to VTM?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-27T17:37:46-07:00","id":1552676,"title":"What lore changes did you hate that was added to VTM?","content":"As someone who is still learning about the lore of the setting, there has to be stuff that you thought didn't add much to the game and you thought what were they thinking when it was introduced and you decided to ignore the changes in your game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":".  For greater clarity. 08-04-2025, 02:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-27T19:15:13-07:00","id":1552681,"title":"","content":"This thread will most probably devolve into edition warring, because most of the things V5 detractors didn't like were lore-related.<br /> <br /> But trying to avoid that... I would say the <b>Week of Nightmares</b> as it was done. It was definitely a fun reading by itself, but its effects in the setting run from poorly thought out to outright harmful. On one hand, thinking that no one noticed three nukes in Bangladesh is just completely ridiculous. On the other hand, however one felt about the Ravnos clan, all but whipping them out was an asshole move for the player community.<br /> <br /> Another problem lore change was the awakening of Ur-Shulgi. The character is insufferable, and that's not even because he's &quot;so evil&quot;, but he's simply bland as Hell. Most of the changes brought with him to the setting were actually good, and even necessary, but they could and should be implemented in a better way, from a better story behind the end of the Tremere Curse (instead of &quot;humorless mummy breaks the curse with his pinky) to a better development for the Web of Knifes (instead of &quot;most of the clan decides to follow the child with the personality of a spoon&quot;). And definitely the way the Banu-Haqim who were Sabbat members switched places was not a good thing at all, as it put unnecessary pressure on players wanting to play Banu-Haqim in the Sabbat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-27T20:58:48-07:00","id":1552683,"title":"","content":"I think we can avoid it getting into edition warring... but yeah V5 has a lot of lore-change related things people dislike. A big problem with V5's lore is that it's very inconsistent on when it explains things as an in-universe change, and when a change is just there an has to be treated as effectively a retcon in order to make any sense. There's plenty of good ideas in the changes V5 made, but a lot of them are also just shoved in (explained or not) that it interferes with using the changes effectively. An example here for me is the Hecata. I don't actually mind the idea of having the death themed groups reconnect and join forces, but the centuries of antagonism between some of them just feel weakly hand-waved away; esp. for the WoD and its themes it's kinda jarring for a bunch of lethally antagonistic vampires to suddenly all work together as a functional social unit.<br /> <br /> Kindred of the East and Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom have massive problems with how their introductions interacted with the existing lore; not helped by how much they didn't respect the cultures being focused on. KotE's &quot;entirely different kind of vampire&quot; has its advantages but it's also pretty unnecessary and makes running games where they are gaining power (mirroring the rise of south east Asia's power on the global scale) much more difficult as they're not just a new faction of vampires fighting for control, but a &quot;race&quot; of non-white vampires invading white vampire territories with the glaring issues that faces as a framework for exploring issues in a game.<br /> <br /> KotEK's &quot;we're the same kinda vampire, but also just a bit different,&quot; wasn't an improvement in helping make setting games in Africa easier, or handling clashes between African vampires and vampires from other places as imperialism and colonialism have faded only to be replaced by globalization. I appreciate the intent to show that vampires can have a completely functional non-Noddist mythology, it's so late in the game for such a big push to finally explore the topic in depth that too many people just react to the African myths as wrong instead of different because different wasn't represented well enough in the older books.<br /> <br /> The Revised crossover event between the Tremere and the Hermetics was also the worst kind of &quot;big event in the books that actually acknowledge it, but somehow it didn't actually change anything in the rest of the books,&quot; was just annoying as it messed with the lores of VtM and MtA with basically no payoff; and is largely ignored anyway.<br /> <br /> There's also a whole category of lore stuff that you can technically say doesn't count for this topic (as it's stuff from non-VtM books), but if you want to include other games (esp. the games introduced in Revised like Demon and Hunter) you're adding in a lot of weird changes that exemplify what WoD crossover is hard beyond just mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-27T22:07:40-07:00","id":1552686,"title":"","content":"At least the Hecata has Augustus being made into a sacrifice to seal the deal, which makes some sense as most of their enmity comes from him screwing everyone else. But it sure would pay off for this to be more carefully done and less effective than it seems to have been.<br /> <br /> KotE has more problems than KotEK, in my opinion, but it was sure as hell late for the introduction of alternative mythology. I always thought Noddism was too unnecessarily heavy in the setting. Anyway, both had the flaws of the time: attempts at representation by people without any real contact with the ones being represented. I have to re-read KotEK, by the way, I never quite understood their Morality system. And I never had the interest on reading KotE, precisely because it isn't the Vampires of Asia and their culture, it is another splat entirely.<br /> <br /> I'm not going into other splats lore for now, that way lies madness. The best way to handle any crossover that won't be completely bonkers (which isn't a bad idea for a game in itself) is to take a single splat's lore and everything else be just for mechanics. This is doable as long as everyone agrees with the main splat for the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-27T22:35:52-07:00","id":1552687,"title":"","content":"Werewolves being the reason that Kindred don't move around a lot in older V:tM probably caused a lot more cascade issues than it solved as a form of verisimilitude. Especially since there's probably a much more pressing limiter of &quot;you won't find blood anywhere as easily as your established herd zones&quot; combined with &quot;the vampires in other places already laid out their claims, and do not appreciate their stocks being poached&quot; with a side of &quot;too many strange murders in a rural town brings in more attention than you want to deal with from the human authorities&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not that it matters now, no matter how much V5 and VV5 insist &quot;no, Kindred like, totally don't have a metaphysical sign of corruption emanating from them, they're totally cool to Garou&quot; when there are zero indications that Kindred act any better than they used to. The nod to kegare was there to show cause and effect in the particular animistic setup of W:tA, not be detect evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T00:59:55-07:00","id":1552689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552687#post1552687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves being the reason that Kindred don't move around a lot in older V:tM probably caused a lot more cascade issues than it solved as a form of verisimilitude. Especially since there's probably a much more pressing limiter of &quot;you won't find blood anywhere as easily as your established herd zones&quot; combined with &quot;the vampires in other places already laid out their claims, and do not appreciate their stocks being poached&quot; with a side of &quot;too many strange murders in a rural town brings in more attention than you want to deal with from the human authorities&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not that it matters now, no matter how much V5 and VV5 insist &quot;no, Kindred like, totally don't have a metaphysical sign of corruption emanating from them, they're totally cool to Garou&quot; when there are zero indications that Kindred act any better than they used to. The nod to kegare was there to show cause and effect in the particular animistic setup of W:tA, not be detect evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was always intriguing to be honest<br /> Even if you take the story of the <b>Bloody Man</b> (the Silver Records spoke of a a man who the Weaver &quot;stole&quot; and wove her webs around him, snuffing out the Wyld spark, making him immortal; intrusion angered the - still uncorrupted - Wyrm, who swallowed the Man to return him to the cycle of being. But the Man was still immortal and within the Wyrm's belly, he began to feed on the blood of the Great Devourer. The Wyrm, howling in pain, spat out the blood-soaked Man, whom all of creation abhorred. Helios then cast his angry gaze upon him, and the Bloody Man was forced to flee beneath the earth. Gaia herself cursed him to hunger forever for blood, to enter age-lasting sleep without dreams and to be unable to conceive and only able to corrupt. Helios warned the Bloody Man that if he or his progeny would ever show his face to him again, he would burn them to cinders.) the vampires are not actually the creation of the Wyrm, but more of the Weaver and even their own stories tell the Hunger and to reproduce with corruption was Gaia's curse (for some unfathomable reason) while Helios added the sunlight and fire sensitivity<br /> Even a well conditioned and brainwashed cub hearing this age old sacred story would scrathy their head and blink &quot;wait what... dafaq, why the Earth Mother made these abominations, we had enough problem already!&quot;<br /> Vampires - especially elder Cainites and those deep into the Jyhad - were seen by the Garou as Wyrm-tainted because: They manipulate, corrupt, feed on the living, and create stagnation.<br /> Many vampires are city-dwellers who promote urbanization and that means destruction of wilderness and on the long term (or short actually) pollution<br /> But here comes the catch: the vampires... not really do these things on purpose<br /> They are dead, that is an undeniable fact, they should be in their graves quietly decomposing feeding the erath part of the Cycle but to be dead and still effecting the world of the living not restig in peace is something basically is an essential part of the the Garou with ther Past Lives and Ancestor Spirits medling left and right, not to mention the Silent Striders whole connection to the Dark Umbra and the Wraiths and the Ivory Priesthood of the Silver Fangs who are basically court necormancers. Necromancy in its core was never a &quot;bad&quot; thing, could be used bad things, but a necromancer basically soemone who help the dead find rest, deliver their warning the living and help them uncovering hidden truths, enslaving the dead or disrupting natural cycle is just a possibility many necromancer do, but in essence Necormancy and dealing with the dread is the oldest form of ancestor worship<br /> Nonetheless, we are back to the main problem the Vampires are not &quot;stuck&quot; in immortality because of the Wyrm, but because of the Weaver, no matter what Garou or Vampire myth you take and th whole blood drinking and reproducing with a curse is rooted either in Gaia's de facto &quot;Decree&quot;/Curse or the Weaver - along the line Eater-of-Souls, the Wyrm of Consumption, embodiment of the gnawing hungers of greed, lust, and gluttony took the oportunity since they more or less fell under their domain but to say the Vampires are under the sway and controll of Eater-of-Souls is like saying the Garou are under the sway and controll of Beast-of-War, the Wyrm of Calamity, a monster of senseless rage, eager to destroy anything in its path and calling Frenzy and Rage the Wyrm's &quot;blessings&quot; (in a sense they are sure, but Luna and Gaia had their hand in that...)<br /> Vampires are just as unwlilling pawns of the Wyrm as the Garou - the Wyrm is opportunistic, but the Vampire don't even know they serve the Wyrm's great plan, if there any such plan, and they are actually again unwillingly and unknowingly help the Weaver<br /> The Garou sense something deeply wrong or unnatural about Cainites - but that is more often than not is because of ther static Essence<br /> The Vampires are the agents and children of the Weaver, never changing (or really really hard and slowly changing) ,static, never aging, never dying, repoducing by trapping others in the Stasis, if they would change, even with a tattoo or cutting their hair... they simply resets to their original &quot;stucked and Embrace&quot; form\u200b and they indeed create stagnation - once a Cainite settled in, they want to keep things unchanged. No progression, no evolution. No change. Everything should stay the same and VERY organized, static, basically in stasis.<br /> The Cainites ebodied on a micro scale what according the Ananasi the Weaver did with Luna, and even if you dismiss that Fera tale, what the Weaver wants the world to become. <br /> The Vampires <i>need</i> to feed, but that is what it is a need, what they <i>want</i> consciously or unconsciously or eve subconsciously is to never change and the world to stay the same, to have their System, their Order, their static, unchanging everlasting life. This is the most Weaver-thing you can think of and their every action, the urbanization, the spreading of technology (in this case, every progeny is like an upgrade to the previous version, more adept to use and understand technology, but that is hardly a &quot;change&quot;\u200b, and the older ones distaste of the modenr is more like a side effect of the static nature)<br /> <br /> This is the only one thing I actually agreed with V5, removing the Garou auto-triggered hate and sense corruption from a vampire, because it never really made sense in the first place, especially when your Sense Wyrm flares up even on a human (or pack mate) who ate too much junk food... Using Sense Wyrm in a city basically fries your senses anyway but never really made much sense to single out a vampires who are usually <i>less </i>wyrm-tainted than your everage human who works in a factory to feed his kids. <br /> But sense Weaver? Despite they were cleary the child of the Weaver, ebodied Stasis and static unchanging, their every deed basically furthered the Weaver's goals and they are walking web-covered unchanging corpses and even your own sacred texts/legends talk about them to be the result of the Weaver&quot;s actions... nope. Or very rarely.<br /> <br /> That addition and thus the whole Garou-Vampire enmity never made any sense<br /> IF you treat the Weerewolves as Lupine not Garou and ignore the whole Werewolf, it still not made much sense to have a war between two spuernatural races who not really had any reason to have a war behind the scenes - if anything they should have been allies, subjugating Humanity, beat them back to the stone age, let the vampires have their small little cities where they rule the Humans as Blood Gods (and if two such ruler want to go to war, even better, let them kill each other), the Wolves can have 80% of the world, the wilderness and if they really want to mate with humans in the name of the good relationship and diplomacy let them pick a few they want to have their own &quot;noble savage&quot; living in the wild humans... <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T02:06:02-07:00","id":1552690,"title":"","content":"2nd edition<br /> <br /> -the secret masters and the ventrue was pretty dumb<br /> <br /> Revised<br /> <br /> -didn't like revised turning the giovanni into mafia<br /> <br /> -ive never liked how the embrace destroys the avatar of a mage. If you can't use spheres to cure the curse it seems wrong the opposite applies.<br /> <br /> -how much they shovelled on 'elders bad and unassailable' got tiresome.<br /> <br /> v20<br /> <br /> -not simply having the harbingers as surviving cappadocians was pointless and convoluted<br /> <br /> V5<br /> <br /> -the lasombra defection was pointless and badly written.<br /> -the anarch ressurgance is nonsensical and doesn't do much for the game.<br /> -The casualty and exodus rates of vampires make trying to reset the game to the 90's weird.<br /> -collapsing the sabbat into orcs was just bad<br /> -the carmarilla tech ban is just clumsy railroading<br /> <br /> <br /> Kindred of the east<br /> <br /> -while the write was aged and behind the times it was as problematic making everyone everywhere american pop culture vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-30-2025, 06:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T02:14:24-07:00","id":1552691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552687#post1552687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not that it matters now, no matter how much V5 and VV5 insist &quot;no, Kindred like, totally don't have a metaphysical sign of corruption emanating from them, they're totally cool to Garou&quot; when there are zero indications that Kindred act any better than they used to. The nod to kegare was there to show cause and effect in the particular animistic setup of W:tA, not be detect evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with them not showing up as 'wrong' was all you're really doing is delaying how long before you correctly identify them as repulsive and an existential threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T02:18:25-07:00","id":1552692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552690#post1552690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2nd edition<br /> <br /> -the secret masters and the ventrue was pretty dumb<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>That line went anywhere?<br /> I kinda lost notice after in their clanbook story about Caine himself talking with their Antediluvian and more or less giving him the imperative of stopping the Secret Masters, after he had witnessed the coming of great destruction for mankind from their hands. What he revealed scared Vaddertha so much he turned his palace in to a Fortress and gathered artifacts like Fenris's fang, the Rainbow Birdge, the Tapestry of Blood ,etc... but that plot line never went anywhere right?<br /> And never truly it was relvelaed who the hell were the Secret Masters?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T02:21:42-07:00","id":1552693,"title":"","content":"I didn't care for any of the &quot;lore&quot; that was written for Demon: The Fallen. <br /> <br /> I also did not care for Orpheus. Didn't read it, but I definitely remember rolling eyes at when I heard about the whole &quot;Grandmaw&quot; aspect of it. I also did not like the whole &quot;Spectre Hives&quot; across the Shroud thing... in general, I just didn't like Orpheus because you could tell it was made with the intent of being actual humans, than ghosts like Wraith was supposed to be and represent (but I understand why it was done, since they were probably trying to gain <i>ANY </i>interest on such a niche but masterfully written game.. it's a shame it wasn't more popular).<br /> <br /> Also (and probably expected this of me to mention), basically all released 5th edition corebooks, supplements, and so-called &quot;side stories&quot; at this point. V5 was an unmitigated disaster among multiple reasons that I've mentioned in the past years before (the most egregious being the removal of Bloodlines for the awful &quot;bloodbook&quot; or whatever its called &quot;lore mechanic&quot;). H5 was nothing more than a blatant lazy cash grab, capitalizing on the name of Reckoning alone but without the actual Imbued present. I didn't bother really engaging with anything W5 put out after the subsequent barrage of 5th failures, but I do remember something along the lines of &quot;Fianna just being a word&quot;... <br /> <br /> More-than-half of the appeal of oWoD for me was the Lore and how interesting it was... and if it I didn't like something about a particular metaplot, I would just homebrew; modifying it to my liking or just removing it for something of my own. But for whatever reason, it seems a particular group holding ironclad platitudial few of anything &quot;lore-heavy&quot; or &quot;metaplot&quot; that took up the mantle for writing 5th took the notion that the former couldn't be the case, and essentially retconned nuked vast portions of the setting to be so-called &quot;beginner friendly&quot; for new audiences.. which have yet to really materialize (and ironic too, from my own personal standpoint, since I only get into oWoD in 2019.. I am the &quot;new audience&quot;, only arriving on-scene in the most inopportune time lol). <br /> <br /> And all-of-the-above is just some of my (albeit, not in-depth as I've done in past, as my overall care for this franchise has dimmed to a pinprick at this point) opinions on the writing/lore they have done to World of Darkness so far. Don't even get me started on what I find mechanically awful about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T02:34:48-07:00","id":1552694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552692#post1552692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That line went anywhere?<br /> I kinda lost notice after in their clanbook story about Caine himself talking with their Antediluvian and more or less giving him the imperative of stopping the Secret Masters, after he had witnessed the coming of great destruction for mankind from their hands. What he revealed scared Vaddertha so much he turned his palace in to a Fortress and gathered artifacts like Fenris's fang, the Rainbow Birdge, the Tapestry of Blood ,etc... but that plot line never went anywhere right?<br /> And never truly it was relvelaed who the hell were the Secret Masters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Forum tend to eat my edits, better this way<br /> It hink the Secret Masters-plot/concept ended up in a Lore-limbo, like the Malkavian's &quot;Thousand Voices&quot;<br /> Tho' that was more or less re-worked to be the Madness Network and Malkav<br /> BUT on the other hand they left enough wriggle room for interpretation and I think the original concept suggested the Thousand Voices were not metaphorical but actual beings, either echoes from a previous universe, or sentient remnants of some pre-Creation state or more likely Beings outside time that became aware of Malkav when he \u201clooked too deeply into the Abyss.\u201d, Pre-reality entities, akin to Lovecraftian Outer Gods or outside reality akin to the Lords and Ladies, the True Fae of the Changeling the Lost<br /> <br /> Anyway in that form it not really made much sense either","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T06:10:46-07:00","id":1552698,"title":"","content":"In general, I don't enjoy lore changes whenever the authors tried to out-extreme themselves, and the self-inflicted confusion on cross-over elements.<br /> <br /> The first one for me was the Sabbat, which as written is completely dysfunctional as an organisation - not as much in terms of philosophical background, but execution. I don't know how to put it any other way than &quot;too edgy to work&quot;. That pattern repeats throughout many Vampire elements (Tzimisce, Baali, Bahari, Black Hand, True Black Hand...) and as a narrative element of parody it is fine, until this lore stops being parody and starts to take itself seriously enough to imply if you're not on board with it then you're playing the game wrong.<br /> There also is an annoying amount of Flanderization of both individual lore NPCs and groups.<br /> <br /> The cross-over stuff has been mentioned by others, it didn't help that WW couldn't decide whether they themselves liked it or not.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T18:38:16-07:00","id":1552710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552689#post1552689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Garou auto-triggered hate and sense corruption from a vampire, because it never really made sense in the first place, especially when your Sense Wyrm flares up even on a human (or pack mate) who ate too much junk food... Using Sense Wyrm in a city basically fries your senses anyway but never really made much sense to single out a vampires who are usually <i>less </i>wyrm-tainted than your everage human who works in a factory to feed his kids.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if that was the problem, self-awareness and free will have nothing to do with this. Many Fomori don't have a clue about what they're representing, either. But that's a backwards rationale to begin with. There was no &quot;Triat&quot; or &quot;Gaia&quot; or kegare-sensing werewolves when it was established that <i><b>the reason for Vampires not traveling out of the cities is the presence of werewolves</b></i>. And the problem is this whole concept and everything it entails, not simply Vampires being hated by Garou (although that's kind of awkward, too).<br /> <br /> I mean, sure, I do think under WtA's cosmology it was unnecessary. While Vampire society in general will be a problem for most Garou because they're assholes who are a problem for everyone, as a standard it's easier to state Vampires are simply supernatural predators (micro-predators to be biologically precise). Being a predator is natural, most Vampires won't be as destructive to the environment as Wyrm minions, and it isn't a part of Werewolf cosmology to have the level of moral judgement (or preocupation with being moral towards humans) seen in Vampire.<br /> <br /> But beyond that, this rationale put an over-the-top pressure for both groups to be always at odds, and made it hard to justify any travel by Vampires, as if Werewolves were waiting in ambush everywhere. At a WtA game you have to think about how any Garou is able to enter a city without becoming a target for the entire Vampire society, as they're basically a pack of ravenous wild beasts from the Leech perspective and the Vampires have no reason to not eliminate the existential threat. It affects stories you can tell both about Garou and Kindred, because you &quot;have&quot; to always assume they're bitter enemies in perpetual war. If not, then you're left with the taste of a main plot point not being true. It gets in the way far more than it builds stories, as whole aspects of their lives are defined by that single phrase.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552690#post1552690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-while the write was aged and behind the times it was as problematic making everyone everywhere american pop culture vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I beg to disagree, and as far as I heard, many Asian players do, too.<br /> <br /> The game is about &quot;western&quot; Vampires (which is by itself a problematic concept). People come to the game to play those Vampires. They exist in a fictional space where they're real and everywhere.<br /> <br /> Something was the problem here, it was making them so heavily attached to a Christian mythology that you couldn't make a character based on another concept without looking as a naive idiot, but even that is less so than we think. It's a big problem for non-Christian players in places with a Christian majority, that have to relive in the game the religious pressure and prejudice they (we) live in real life. For players in actual Asia it seems to not be a problem at all, as Noddism simply sounds as fantasy religion.<br /> <br /> KotE presents a splat that's interesting by itself (as far as I heard, anyway), but &quot;regular&quot; Kindred should be the norm everywhere, save when it's a plot point. Heck, here in Brazil we have a big problem among Werewolf players precisely because in canon we don't have Werewolves, only Cats and Spiders. No one uses the Canon, and few people want to play in the Amazon just because the canon says so. Creatures like the Hungry Dead (the name Kuei-Jin is incredibly stupid orientalism) would be a welcome addition to the setting, if in their own terms and less &quot;culture-specific&quot; (not really).\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552693#post1552693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also did not care for Orpheus. Didn't read it, but I definitely remember rolling eyes at when I heard about the whole &quot;Grandmaw&quot; aspect of it. I also did not like the whole &quot;Spectre Hives&quot; across the Shroud thing... in general, I just didn't like Orpheus because you could tell it was made with the intent of being actual humans, than ghosts like Wraith was supposed to be and represent (but I understand why it was done, since they were probably trying to gain <i>ANY </i>interest on such a niche but masterfully written game.. it's a shame it wasn't more popular).</div> </div> </div> </div>While I can't say much, as I didn't read it either, I think this is a tad unfair with Orpheus.<br /> <br /> Revised killed Wraith. Like in, almost literally killed it. In-character, the Maelstrom destroyed the whole of Wraith's setting. However we feel about this decision, it is what it is, WW wouldn't ever make another Wraith book or assume Wraith society existed anymore. And it wasn't a quiet end, the Shadowlands were heavily used for the metaplots of everyone else, the ends of the Necropolises was an undeniable fact.<br /> <br /> Orpheus was made against that background as a love-letter and goodbye to Wraith. It is not the same game, nor does it pretends to be, it is a memorial, a funerary rite in itself.<br /> <br /> And a good one, as far as everyone I know that read it says.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T19:07:39-07:00","id":1552712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552689#post1552689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was always intriguing to be honest<br /> Even if you take the story of the <b>Bloody Man</b> (the Silver Records spoke of a a man who the Weaver &quot;stole&quot; and wove her webs around him, snuffing out the Wyld spark, making him immortal; intrusion angered the - still uncorrupted - Wyrm, who swallowed the Man to return him to the cycle of being. But the Man was still immortal and within the Wyrm's belly, he began to feed on the blood of the Great Devourer. The Wyrm, howling in pain, spat out the blood-soaked Man, whom all of creation abhorred. Helios then cast his angry gaze upon him, and the Bloody Man was forced to flee beneath the earth. Gaia herself cursed him to hunger forever for blood, to enter age-lasting sleep without dreams and to be unable to conceive and only able to corrupt. Helios warned the Bloody Man that if he or his progeny would ever show his face to him again, he would burn them to cinders.) the vampires are not actually the creation of the Wyrm, but more of the Weaver and even their own stories tell the Hunger and to reproduce with corruption was Gaia's curse (for some unfathomable reason)</div> </div> </div> </div>I call metatextual issues on that one. Vampires and stories about them invite curses as explanations even when it wouldn't make sense. Their collective angst is so far off the charts that the Sasuke Limit cannot contain it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> while Helios added the sunlight and fire sensitivity<br /> Even a well conditioned and brainwashed cub hearing this age old sacred story would scrathy their head and blink &quot;wait what... dafaq, why the Earth Mother made these abominations, we had enough problem already!&quot;<br /> Vampires - especially elder Cainites and those deep into the Jyhad - were seen by the Garou as Wyrm-tainted because: They manipulate, corrupt, feed on the living, and create stagnation.<br /> Many vampires are city-dwellers who promote urbanization and that means destruction of wilderness and on the long term (or short actually) pollution<br /> But here comes the catch: the vampires... not really do these things on purpose </div> </div> </div>I mean that only really flies so many times. After about a dozen, it's so far beyond a reasonable presumption of malice that you can't even see a simple &quot;Enemy Action&quot; from here.<br /> <br /> [quote]<br /> They are dead, that is an undeniable fact, they should be in their graves quietly decomposing feeding the erath part of the Cycle but to be dead and still effecting the world of the living not restig in peace is something basically is an essential part of the the Garou with ther Past Lives and Ancestor Spirits medling left and right[quote]<br /> <br /> No. Ancestor-spirits are living beings of the Middle Umbra who happen to have jumped from being half-flesh and half-spirit to being pretty much all spirit (you go through the same result if you spend too long in the Umbra). They also technically share the flesh of their descendants and can return through it to aid them. Vampires, meanwhile, panned out as spiritual roach motels that will keep a bane lodged in there indefinitely (and no one else is likely to try).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> not to mention the Silent Striders whole connection to the Dark Umbra and the Wraiths and the Ivory Priesthood of the Silver Fangs who are basically court necormancers. Necromancy in its core was never a &quot;bad&quot; thing, could be used bad things, but a necromancer basically soemone who help the dead find rest, deliver their warning the living and help them uncovering hidden truths, enslaving the dead or disrupting natural cycle is just a possibility many necromancer do, but in essence Necormancy and dealing with the dread is the oldest form of ancestor worship </div> </div> </div>A big part of the Striders' connection to it was thrust upon them by a vampire. Also, the Ivory Priesthood is more about being the keepers of the Secret of Death that Wolf received from Gaia, with study of the Dark Umbra being more of an ancillary part of that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nonetheless, we are back to the main problem the Vampires are not &quot;stuck&quot; in immortality because of the Wyrm, but because of the Weaver, no matter what Garou or Vampire myth you take and th whole blood drinking and reproducing with a curse is rooted either in Gaia's de facto &quot;Decree&quot;/Curse or the Weaver - along the line Eater-of-Souls, the Wyrm of Consumption, embodiment of the gnawing hungers of greed, lust, and gluttony took the oportunity since they more or less fell under their domain but to say the Vampires are under the sway and controll of Eater-of-Souls is like saying the Garou are under the sway and controll of Beast-of-War, the Wyrm of Calamity, a monster of senseless rage, eager to destroy anything in its path and calling Frenzy and Rage the Wyrm's &quot;blessings&quot; (in a sense they are sure, but Luna and Gaia had their hand in that...)<br /> Vampires are just as unwlilling pawns of the Wyrm as the Garou - the Wyrm is opportunistic, but the Vampire don't even know they serve the Wyrm's great plan, if there any such plan, and they are actually again unwillingly and unknowingly help the Weaver<br /> The Garou sense something deeply wrong or unnatural about Cainites - but that is more often than not is because of ther static Essence </div> </div> </div>Nah. It's because they're walking factories for making an addictive drug that they frequently feed to others to spread their condition in one way or another. And also because, per the W20 Book of the Wyrm, their general night to night activities are highly reminiscent of what the majority of Black Spiral Dancers get up to. They're self-indulgent consumers of those that they hold beneath them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Vampires are the agents and children of the Weaver, never changing (or really really hard and slowly changing) ,static, never aging, never dying, repoducing by trapping others in the Stasis, if they would change, even with a tattoo or cutting their hair... they simply resets to their original &quot;stucked and Embrace&quot; form and they indeed create stagnation - once a Cainite settled in, they want to keep things unchanged. No progression, no evolution. No change. Everything should stay the same and VERY organized, static, basically in stasis.<br /> The Cainites ebodied on a micro scale what according the Ananasi the Weaver did with Luna, and even if you dismiss that Fera tale, what the Weaver wants the world to become.<br /> The Vampires <i>need</i> to feed, but that is what it is a need, what they <i>want</i> consciously or unconsciously or eve subconsciously is to never change and the world to stay the same, to have their System, their Order, their static, unchanging everlasting life. This is the most Weaver-thing you can think of and their every action, the urbanization, the spreading of technology (in this case, every progeny is like an upgrade to the previous version, more adept to use and understand technology, but that is hardly a &quot;change&quot;\u200b, and the older ones distaste of the modenr is more like a side effect of the static nature) </div> </div> </div>And where the Weaver sets up shop, the corrupter always follows. It's really easy, like riding down a spiral slide or rappelling down from height.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is the only one thing I actually agreed with V5, removing the Garou auto-triggered hate and sense corruption from a vampire, because it never really made sense in the first place, especially when your Sense Wyrm flares up even on a human (or pack mate) who ate too much junk food... Using Sense Wyrm in a city basically fries your senses anyway but never really made much sense to single out a vampires who are usually <i>less </i>wyrm-tainted than your everage human who works in a factory to feed his kids. </div> </div> </div>No, most of them don't drink each others' blood and turn each other into drugged-out thralls, so there's that. Rarely, there are fomori that result from these tasks, but for the most part the people who work these jobs mostly just feel bad about it and get apathetic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But sense Weaver? Despite they were cleary the child of the Weaver, ebodied Stasis and static unchanging, their every deed basically furthered the Weaver's goals and they are walking web-covered unchanging corpses and even your own sacred texts/legends talk about them to be the result of the Weaver&quot;s actions... nope. Or very rarely. </div> </div> </div>Book of the Weaver mentions that they have to go a long time (centuries) before they ping strongly on it. Conversely, one that decides to go wild with blood drinking and making life worse around them will smack much more of the burnt tires and trash kegare than they probably ever will of the eye-stinging sterile bleach kegare.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That addition and thus the whole Garou-Vampire enmity never made any sense<br /> IF you treat the Weerewolves as Lupine not Garou and ignore the whole Werewolf, it still not made much sense to have a war between two spuernatural races who not really had any reason to have a war behind the scenes - if anything they should have been allies, subjugating Humanity, beat them back to the stone age, let the vampires have their small little cities where they rule the Humans as Blood Gods (and if two such ruler want to go to war, even better, let them kill each other), the Wolves can have 80% of the world, the wilderness and if they really want to mate with humans in the name of the good relationship and diplomacy let them pick a few they want to have their own &quot;noble savage&quot; living in the wild humans... </div> </div> </div>Subjugating humanity was what they did during the Impergium. It didn't work out well and they swore not to do it again (that was what the Concord and the Litany was all about). So, again, for the werewolves to see the vampires acting as they did at their worst... no sympathy, no questions, no quarter asked or given.<br /> <br /> Again, the relationship, by now, how soured more than the worst failure of yogurt production, and there's really no going back. Retcons won't help as long as vampires still act like vampires. You'd have to be a vampion instead, and V5 definitely isn't going to do that; it's the edition's very definition of wrongbad fun... not that it wants you to have fun; it's purely looking to instill a catharsis, but to be quite frank, I have Anohana and similar series for experiencing that kind of Best Worst Times, and I don't need Vampire to try and measure up to it, because it can't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T22:26:00-07:00","id":1552715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552712#post1552712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Book of the Weaver mentions that they have to go a long time (centuries) before they ping strongly on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What doesn't make a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> One of the problems with Book of the Weaver is that it generally has a far higher bar for signs of Bleach Kegare than the rest of WtA has for Trash Kegare, and that depiction is the most extreme of this.<br /> <br /> Vampires are supernatural stasis more than anything else. Their corruption tends to follow from them living a shitty life, but their stasis is abnormal from the get go, with a body that stubbornly goes back to their initial state of death, rejecting absolutely any change to it, mundane or preternatural, superficial or invasive.<br /> <br /> That isn't just the Vampires, though. Drones take a lot more to form, for example, than Fomori. More extreme conditions, more time dedicated to dysfunctional behavior, more everything.<br /> <br /> It makes sense from a design perspective because the game isn't meant to focus too much on the Weaver like that, but it doesn't really follow from a setting where, regardless of the Wyrm's tactical advantage, the assumption is that the Weaver basically covered the world. And with Vampires it makes especially little sense.<br /> <br /> But that's that, anyway. No few ancient vampires would stink of the Wyrm royally, especially in the later versions of the setting (as Vampire gets more Grimm-Dark-Kick-the-Pup-Evil as editions go).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-29T00:16:47-07:00","id":1552716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552715#post1552715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What doesn't make a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> One of the problems with Book of the Weaver is that it generally has a far higher bar for signs of Bleach Kegare than the rest of WtA has for Trash Kegare, and that depiction is the most extreme of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably to keep some degree of plausibility with the Glass Walkers not thinking that the Weaver was as bad as the Wyrm. To keep them from looking like total idiots and dupes, or to make the Weaver seem much subtler and cunning (which it kind of is compared to the Wyrm, seeing as how it's not trapped and biting itself trying to get free).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires are supernatural stasis more than anything else. Their corruption tends to follow from them living a shitty life, but their stasis is abnormal from the get go, with a body that stubbornly goes back to their initial state of death, rejecting absolutely any change to it, mundane or preternatural, superficial or invasive. </div> </div> </div>But the things that their body does to the blood they consume could be considered an incredibly horrid corruption. Normal fluid connective tissue goes in, a horribly-addicting animating force that chains others to the holder comes out. The blood bond is a true thing of horror, and even if it instills some degree of stasis to turn a living being unaging, the psychological corruption it can produce from repeated drinks is far more noticeable in an immediate sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That isn't just the Vampires, though. Drones take a lot more to form, for example, than Fomori. More extreme conditions, more time dedicated to dysfunctional behavior, more everything. </div> </div> </div>That's because whatever force was behind it saw fomori, realized that they were kind of slap dash, and developed an alternative that thoroughly binds spirit and flesh together much more deeply. It's why Drones also cannot be exorcised easily, read by any force that most characters have access to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It makes sense from a design perspective because the game isn't meant to focus too much on the Weaver like that, but it doesn't really follow from a setting where, regardless of the Wyrm's tactical advantage, the assumption is that the Weaver basically covered the world. And with Vampires it makes especially little sense.<br /> <br /> But that's that, anyway. No few ancient vampires would stink of the Wyrm royally, especially in the later versions of the setting (as Vampire gets more Grimm-Dark-Kick-the-Pup-Evil as editions go). </div> </div> </div>Well, the Gauntlet was spun by the Weaver, so there might be some acclimation going on.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-29T01:11:05-07:00","id":1552717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552716#post1552716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the things that their body does to the blood they consume could be considered an incredibly horrid corruption. Normal fluid connective tissue goes in, a horribly-addicting animating force that chains others to the holder comes out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still think the emotional conditioning looks more like a Weaver than a Wyrm thing, but here I do agree that it at the very least becomes blurry and arguable.<br /> <br /> And to be clear, I don't think Book of the Weaver should be much different. Whatever the in-game explanation, generally dialing down the &quot;strength&quot; of Weaver-Taint was a design necessity.<br /> <br /> My personal point is more that in the case of Vampires, specifically, I think they should by all means reek of the Weaver. It should be easier to find a &quot;regular&quot; Vampire through Weaver-Taint than Wyrm-Taint, especially Neonates or others with less Wyrm-related behaviors. And of course, it would be doubly so if they didn't had made Vampires and Werewolves into obligatory nemeses, but even without this.<br /> <br /> Was there somewhere a rule that the three &quot;Taints&quot; somehow cancelled each other? AFAIR it was perfectly possible for someone to ping as both high Wyrm and high Weaver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-29T02:24:18-07:00","id":1552718,"title":"","content":"There have been Sense Weaver and Sense Wyld, as well as other Gifts, for the Garou to pick up other imbalances. That said, the books between 2e and W20 usually do describe most vampires as a mix of Wyrm and Weaver, with some more Wyrmy than others (usually in crossover this is pegged to Humanity ratings or being on a Path).<br /> <br /> That said, since this is a thread about VtM lore... VtM tends to describe vampires as cursed and tainted in various negative ways. Very few VtM books treat the idea that most other supernaturals find the undead - including vampires - distasteful as fairly self-evident even if vampires don't like it or have any idea as to the specific metaphysical stories most other splats use to justify hatred of them simply existing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-29T07:40:18-07:00","id":1552719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552710#post1552710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I beg to disagree, and as far as I heard, many Asian players do, too.<br /> <br /> The game is about &quot;western&quot; Vampires (which is by itself a problematic concept). People come to the game to play those Vampires. They exist in a fictional space where they're real and everywhere.<br /> <br /> Something was the problem here, it was making them so heavily attached to a Christian mythology that you couldn't make a character based on another concept without looking as a naive idiot, but even that is less so than we think. It's a big problem for non-Christian players in places with a Christian majority, that have to relive in the game the religious pressure and prejudice they (we) live in real life. For players in actual Asia it seems to not be a problem at all, as Noddism simply sounds as fantasy religion.<br /> <br /> KotE presents a splat that's interesting by itself (as far as I heard, anyway), but &quot;regular&quot; Kindred should be the norm everywhere, save when it's a plot point. Heck, here in Brazil we have a big problem among Werewolf players precisely because in canon we don't have Werewolves, only Cats and Spiders. No one uses the Canon, and few people want to play in the Amazon just because the canon says so. Creatures like the Hungry Dead (the name Kuei-Jin is incredibly stupid orientalism) would be a welcome addition to the setting, if in their own terms and less &quot;culture-specific&quot; (not really).<br /> <br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I've spoken with asian players with mixed or opposite views but I sort of agree, a setting should have allowances to run non-localized supernaturals in regions which are distinct. It isnt even that hard with the western supernaturals considering the early modern period expansion. I also think vice versa should be permissible and we do a deeper dive on what was present before. A write of for something based of the Nagual and other shape shifters and how the they adapt (or not) to post columbian Garou presence and how they differ from western Fera could be really good, for example.<br /> At the same time we should explore an emerging presence of said groups in WoD in traditional kindred territories like they were doing in revised and western vampires are not hard to justify in asia.<br /> Although I'd still comment kindred of the east needs updating in a lot of ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-29T09:33:43-07:00","id":1552720,"title":"","content":"I've rarely liked nor hated Metaplot or Lore advancements - I've never been a big fan of WoD &quot;canon characters&quot; or novels anyway. But I do dislike when those changes make the world smaller, with less options. Such as killing off the Ravnos on WoN, or deciding to devastate all off-world realms of mages on the Avatar Storm<br /> <br /> I didn't like the choice to make Elders go away with the Beckoning on V5. But it's the choice to collapse the structure of the Sabbat, with a lot &quot;going East&quot;, and the rest becoming a monster rabble labeled as &quot;unplayable&quot; for no reason, what single handedly collapsed any hope I may have had to play on that edition.<br /> <br /> So I guess you could say I hate it. The whole &quot;off to the middle east&quot; arc.<br /> <br /> The explicit intention was to collapse the power structures of vampires to force change, so it's the &quot;put on a bus&quot; trope ... but isn't it weird to send the social structure of Vampire to some place?, why would all Elders go to one place?, what's going on there?...<br /> <br /> From the perspective of someone that plays Vampire on the Middle East, it must've been pretty wild - like, suddenly the place HAS to be full of Elders figthing some strange magical war between Super-Elders?. And the core book had 0 support for that kind of game.<br /> <br /> Personaly, I think that choice was much more related with the whole conflict betweeen USA and Afganistan, that was a pretty hot topic at the time V5 was written and released, than any other reason (much like how comic books often send the heroes to fight wars on places that are strangely similar to countries that are at odds with USA at the time). Ultimately, WoD games are set in USA, are supposed to be played there, and the setting<i> &quot;looks at the world&quot;,</i> so to speak, from that perspective. This one was just a pretty noticeable example of something that happens all the time, really, if you think about it.<br /> <br /> To me, the exclusive location and the lack of support at the moment made that metaplot fell like everyone that's someone going to a party you're not really invited to. I guess part of the intent was to return some &quot;mistery&quot; to WoD, and that's allright - I can dig that &quot;gehenna vive&quot;. That's one thing I can say I <b>like </b>about the whole things as a concept.<br /> <br /> But it really didn't seemed that V5 was trying to engage players with that mistery - rather it seems the idea was to play the game everywhere <i>else</i>, and to give Anarchs more relevance while shoving the Sabbat out of the players hand and more into the STs hand. As it was on 1e. Felt like them trying to take a toy from my hands and then giving me another toy, saying I should like the new toy more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-29-2025, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-29T12:01:55-07:00","id":1552725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552717#post1552717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I still think the emotional conditioning looks more like a Weaver than a Wyrm thing, but here I do agree that it at the very least becomes blurry and arguable.<br /> <br /> And to be clear, I don't think Book of the Weaver should be much different. Whatever the in-game explanation, generally dialing down the &quot;strength&quot; of Weaver-Taint was a design necessity.<br /> <br /> My personal point is more that in the case of Vampires, specifically, I think they should by all means reek of the Weaver. It should be easier to find a &quot;regular&quot; Vampire through Weaver-Taint than Wyrm-Taint, especially Neonates or others with less Wyrm-related behaviors. And of course, it would be doubly so if they didn't had made Vampires and Werewolves into obligatory nemeses, but even without this.<br /> <br /> Was there somewhere a rule that the three &quot;Taints&quot; somehow cancelled each other? AFAIR it was perfectly possible for someone to ping as both high Wyrm and high Weaver.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Weaver and Wyrm are probably special cases on account of ganging up on the Wyld, and how the Triatic Defiler Wyrm is said to be very, very good at fitting between and down the Weaver's webs, enabling corruption by one and then the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-29T17:08:34-07:00","id":1552736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552698#post1552698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, I don't enjoy lore changes whenever the authors tried to out-extreme themselves, and the self-inflicted confusion on cross-over elements.<br /> <br /> The first one for me was the Sabbat, which as written is completely dysfunctional as an organisation - not as much in terms of philosophical background, but execution. I don't know how to put it any other way than &quot;too edgy to work&quot;. That pattern repeats throughout many Vampire elements (Tzimisce, Baali, Bahari, Black Hand, True Black Hand...) and as a narrative element of parody it is fine, until this lore stops being parody and starts to take itself seriously enough to imply if you're not on board with it then you're playing the game wrong.<br /> There also is an annoying amount of Flanderization of both individual lore NPCs and groups.<br /> <br /> The cross-over stuff has been mentioned by others, it didn't help that WW couldn't decide whether they themselves liked it or not.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>While I mostly agree with the sentiment, I have to admit one thing: many of those changes added elements to the game that someone greatly enjoyed, while their impact on my games was minimal. The Sabbat added a whole play style a lot of people like. Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand was shock full of ideas and concepts you could rip out from the given context and use, including things like the Old Clan Tzimisce that I really like. Either as antagonists or player options, there's a lot of uses for Baali and Bahari, whether using their given lore directly or adapting.<br /> <br /> In the long run, the wonky ideas and super-edgy concepts added to the game more frequently than they took from it, even when the lore itself given wasn't interesting for me. There are lots of takes and pieces on the setting that I don't like, but I much prefer to save my &quot;hatred&quot; for things that made the game smaller rather than bigger, that took toys out of the hands of people instead of adding new ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552720#post1552720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the perspective of someone that plays Vampire on the Middle East, it must've been pretty wild - like, suddenly the place HAS to be full of Elders figthing some strange magical war between Super-Elders?. And the core book had 0 support for that kind of game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll really try to not talk too much about V5 lore, but here's one of the worst of it in my opinion.<br /> <br /> The problem with the Beckoning is that it completely ignored that there are people that play Vampire in the Middle East. Both in the sense that they play chronicles taking place there, and in the sense that there are players that live there. It was presented as a &quot;they went to a far away land no one has contact with&quot;, except it isn't a particular far away place and definitely a lot of people has contact with.<br /> <br /> Orientalism at its finest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-29T22:38:38-07:00","id":1552742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552736#post1552736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with the Beckoning is that it completely ignored that there are people that play Vampire in the Middle East. Both in the sense that they play chronicles taking place there, and in the sense that there are players that live there</div> </div> </div> </div>As you pointed out the Week if Nightmares, this one was one of its major problems... Zapathasura rampaged across India to Bangladesh for two days... then on the third day was attacked by three of the eldest Kuei-jin Bodhisattvas, the Devil-Tiger Eight Thunders Sage, the Thrashing Dragon Black Earth Boy and the Resplendent Crane Rising Majestically to the Western Sun, powerhouses on their own right<br /> Since Baba Yaga and her Armies casually swept away Spets and anything that stood in Her way the world not really seen such display of power... but Bangladesh was and is - and no offense to russia and where Baba Yaga rose and ruled - is the eighth-most populous country in the world and among the most densely populated with a population of over 171 million within an area of 148,460 square kilometres... the death toll was above the charts and after that others joined the fray - swath of territory stretching from Calcutta to Dhaka was almost entirely depopulated.<br /> From storyteller point of view the Week of Nightmares was a logistical nightmare say the least and you had to be pretty clever to explain how on earth this not broke the Masquarade to pieces and more importantly what happened to the locals? And those who played there...<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 07-30-2025, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-30T00:11:14-07:00","id":1552744,"title":"","content":"Speaking of the Week of Nightmares I was not really keen about the idea - lore - it introduced.<br /> Increased tension between Ravnos and Kuei-Jin in South Asia (especially India) erupted into open conflict - it is okay, they are age old enemies, for one reason or another - but the Week of Nightmares basically happened becuse the Ravnos began Embracing more neonates to fight this growing battle and the barely trained, highly unstable neonates and then fledgelings sent into suicidal confrontations against the Kuei-Jin.<br /> Their quick deaths created a psychic backlash through the Ravnos Antediluvian\u2019s bloodline, this death echo resonated upward.<br /> More elder Ravnos awoke from torpor, sensing the threat or being disturbed by the vitae's turmoil.<br /> These elders also Embraced more childer<br /> The new childer were sent into battle, dying just as quickly \u2014 feeding the cycle.<br /> Each death was like a bell rung in the blood, reverberating louder and louder through the clan\u2019s Blood<br /> The psychic pressure built to a climax, culminating in the awakening of Zapathasura himself.<br /> <br /> So the Ravnos began Embracing rapidly, sending young to die, which psychically echoed through the bloodline and progressively awoke more powerful elders, culminating in Zapathasura\u2019s awakening\u2026<br /> But this presented two possibilites:<br /> A, the Ravnos were unique, their blood was uniquely &quot;resonant&quot; and/or their own legends about they were not Cainite at all, but Zapathasura was created to combat the Kuei Jin by the gods were true after all\u2026<br /> B, this was not an unique thing, every Clan could end up like them<br /> <br /> While I am personally always was fond of the multiple vampire-&quot;races&quot;, both presented a headscratching problem<br /> Why now?<br /> The Ravnos and the Kuei-jin battled for Ages, literally, and they fought even bigger battles and the older Ravnos bent reality left and right in those ancient bloody battles, the number of deaths were even higher, whole cities of vampires were destroyed to the point lot of Zapathasura's direct children had enough and left, like Hazimel or Ravana (who may or may not become the Yama King of the same name)<br /> And the ther fact is, vampires did this all the time they died en-masse, be it vampire wars, Week of the Midnight Sun (that did a number on the Followers of Set on a grand scale) the anarch revolt, the flood, inqusition or just a prolonged Sabbat siege\u2026<br /> Mass embrace and Mass Death was not something new\u2026 yet no other Elder or Ancient or Antediluvian woke - or at least no one told us (tho' porbably most of the Antediluvians are around and awake just staying out of sight)<br /> So this lore addition and explanation never really made any sense to me or liked it that much","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-30T16:03:24-07:00","id":1552754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552742#post1552742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the death toll was above the charts and after that others joined the fray - swath of territory stretching from Calcutta to Dhaka was almost entirely depopulated.<br /> From storyteller point of view the Week of Nightmares was a logistical nightmare say the least and you had to be pretty clever to explain how on earth this not broke the Masquarade to pieces and more importantly what happened to the locals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost 1,5 million people died in total in accordance with the official lore, most from the astounding colateral damage of the many battles raging there (Zapathasura plus a bunch of Ravnos plus a lot of stranded spirits, vs everyone else), but 110.000+ from the floods and 60.000+ from the nukes.<br /> <br /> This is more than the annual deaths in the entire country for most of the last century. In fact, unless no one else died that year, it's enough to make 1999 almost as lethal as 1971, the year of the Bangladeshi Liberation War, which was one of the biggest mass deaths events after WWII, and more lethal than the entire year of 1970, when Bangladesh was hit by the Bhola Cyclone, the most lethal storm of its history (the Bhola killed at most half a million people).<br /> <br /> Concentrated, so it doesn't mean a lot of extra deaths spread through the country through time, it was a lot of areas being wiped out at once. There's a lot of physical damage in the area's landscape that couldn't possibly be caused by a storm, not to say that the three nukes were nukes, they left radiation behind, so we have huge swaths of uninhabitable land, and a lot of the people who died from them didn't die immediately, but up to weeks after.<br /> <br /> Sure, the Technocracy covered it up. No one was thinking about it anymore a month later. That definitely makes sense...\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552744#post1552744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of the Week of Nightmares I was not really keen about the idea - lore - it introduced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing about it makes sense, and the more you think about it, the less it makes sense.<br /> <br /> Why did the mass embrace caused those effects? Why did the Ravnos resorted to mass embrace right now? Why the Fledglings even went to fight? Mass embraces in the area where a battle will happen are one thing. &quot;mass embraces&quot; that aren't really massive are also a thing. But anything expecting a huge mass of Fledlings to act as an actual army, I don't see it working, and that seems to have been the case.<br /> <br /> And why did the awakening of Zapathasura caused murderous rage through the entire clan?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-30T16:52:45-07:00","id":1552755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552710#post1552710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">KotE presents a splat that's interesting by itself (as far as I heard, anyway), but &quot;regular&quot; Kindred should be the norm everywhere, save when it's a plot point. <b>Heck, here in Brazil we have a big problem among Werewolf players precisely because in canon we don't have Werewolves, only Cats and Spiders. </b>No one uses the Canon, and few people want to play in the Amazon just because the canon says so. Creatures like the Hungry Dead (the name Kuei-Jin is incredibly stupid orientalism) would be a welcome addition to the setting, if in their own terms and less &quot;culture-specific&quot; (not really).</div> </div> </div> </div>Bolded the most stupid part of the lore I could remember. Brasil in particular has a well documented folkore about the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lobisomem\" target=\"_blank\">Lobisomem</a> which is nothing but a werewolf! Copying nearly all european myths.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is due of course to the writers not knowing anything about the places they wrote about. Far more egregious examples on the Kuei-Jin side, but it comes again to bad game design, we forget the original writers were a bunch of semi-amateurs, that had great passion, but almost zero knowledge of game design or even cultural knowledge that today we take for granted easy access (I still remember the first years of the internet, wikipedia is a great invention).<br /> <br /> <br /> I know collectively we the fans glorify old editions, but they were bad. Bad as in badly-designed-lore, bad as in culturally-insensitive-USA-centric, bad as in dumb-mechanics-that-are-not-consistent-among-the-same-splat-even.<br /> <br /> <br /> One of the great things that Chronicles did, was using a system that was playtested, and tweaked to be internally consistent: everyone is a baseline human, then templates on top, same dice mechanics for the same things, baseline merits/flaws (then conditions with 2ed) definitions for everyone. We are benefiting there from several years of game design professionalisation that not only includes mechanics but also setting creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-31T04:33:13-07:00","id":1552765,"title":"","content":"<img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1928_1753961338621_188\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1928\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1928\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1928&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> FYI, the property damage and radioactive area is only localized to a small area.<br /> <br /> For the second issue, of why the Ravnos Ante waking up effected its bloodline like that. It was a master of Animalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","user":"Aydoo","date":". 07-31-2025, 07:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-31T05:23:34-07:00","id":1552766,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy deployed &quot;magical neutron bombs&quot; as the part of <b>Operation Ragnar\u00f6k</b><br /> The Technocracy viewed the situation as a <b>Class Omega Scenario</b><br /> They dropped it on Karachi, Pakistan (the most recent census data indicates Karachi's population is 20.3 million, according to Wikipedia, back then a bit smaller.)<br /> The <b>neutron bombs</b> used by them were designed to maximize lethal radiation with minimal blast damage. - it is true, but they were three Hypertech-enhanced, Prime-infused, Chimerical-piercing bombs, Type Theta-R Suppression Devices with 100\u2013200 kilotons radiation, equivalent to 10\u2013100 megaton bombs on superanturals, just for fun with a 3.6 kilotons (blast) with a 188 kilotons (neutron release),\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200bThe blast covered all of Karachi (~12M people) - 3,527 square kilometers\u200b<br /> It was devastating say the least and wouldn't really call it a &quot;small&quot; area and this was just the Technocracy's bombs... and the rampaging Antediluvian and his enemies did a number on the rest<br /> I mean it is &quot;canon&quot; most of the territory stretching from Calcutta to Dhaka was almost entirely depopulated and destroyed...<br /> Not really a backyard squabble<br /> And totally - again - headache to explain as a ST why the Masquarade is still intact, Baba Yaga at least &quot;hid&quot; her domain behind the Shadow Courtain (but that one was again a logistical nightmare...)<br /> Zapatahasura and the Bodishatvas and everyone else? They were not really &quot;discrete&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 07-31-2025, 08:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-31T17:52:11-07:00","id":1552784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552765#post1552765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1928_1753961338621_188\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1928\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1928\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1928&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> FYI, the property damage and radioactive area is only localized to a small area.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not, because it was a moving battle from Calcutta to Dhaka. Most of the damage was on low-density population areas, but not in a small area.<br /> <br /> And Neutron Bombs aren't subtle. They do have smaller blast area, but they have larger radiation spread for their yield.<br /> <br /> This simply isn't something you can throw without attracting attention. Nuclear blasts are powerful enough to be detected by seismographers, and the signal is easily distinguished from an earthquake. And they were three, in populated enough areas to kill more than 60 thousand people. While seismographers can't distinguish if a blast was caused by a nuclear or a regular (if damn powerful) bomb, there are planes made to de<br /> <br /> Even if the affected area were indeed &quot;small&quot;, it isn't negligible, and the effects are quite strong. It's impossible that no one noticed three nuclear blasts and fallout areas.<br /> <br /> Zapathasura being a master of <b>Animalism</b> only explains half of a small part of what happened. It make some sense that he has this power, but the whole debacle remains a lot contrived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-31T22:57:57-07:00","id":1552791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552765#post1552765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the second issue, of why the Ravnos Ante waking up effected its bloodline like that. It was a master of Animalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except not his awaking caused the bloodlust but his death<br /> While he was awake Chimerstry grew stronger, though harder to control.<br /> When Zapathasura &quot;died&quot; - and this part was always a bit of a source of debate because while most of the time editions mentioned his death, others even V5 and the whole lore not really supported that idea and probably he was not <i>that dead</i> as you can see in V5 there are hints (on the lorsheet, Blood of Zapatashura) Like how Malkav was tore apart, yet his children consumed his blood to shiled it from the sun, so he survived as the Cobweb/Madnes network, lot of his life blood remained... if that trick worked with Malkav, Zapatashura may survived too, since the sun not destroyed his lifeblood.... or it was just a reality alteration. Sources saying well he died is not really reliable, considering they also say the Venture antediluvian died too around the Second City (or First, depending the source), yet he was Embraced left and right till 60 BC when he embraced Antonius and Erik Eigermann/Ueruic and Danava believe themselves to be the guardians of their Antediluvian (pitri, or &quot;father&quot;), whom they call Veddhartha. - so when he &quot;died&quot; every Ravnos on Earth felt an uncontrollable bloodlust, compelled to destroy or diablerize other members of their clan for four days<br /> This was never explained<br /> And effecting the Bloodline was never an Animailsm power but a Dominate one<br /> The Clans whose progenitor suposedly &quot;died&quot; never really consumed themselves in a fit of rage, even the Salubri - and Saulot was just played a long con - only experienced their third eye opened and shone hard to hide, but not mass destruction by their own hands<br /> And the Cappadoicans were fine, and their Progenitor really &quot;died&quot; - well as much as was possible for him; Sargon<b>, t</b>he Cappadocian Antediluvan bacame a Wraith after Augustus tried to eat him, then In Giovanni Chronicles IV: Nuova Malattia, the Children of Isaac tried to put him to rest with a ritual from Marianna. Partially worked. During Gehenna, his soul was consumed when the Sixth Great Maelstrom hit the Shadowlands and became a Specter, a de-facto part of Oblivion. - they not ended up like the Ravnos either...<br /> Also the Master of Animanilsm was the main reason many belived he never Frenzied at all, considering even its low level powers are exactly to avoid that...<br /> ...and if he was sane and in controll or was a controlled Frenzy?<br /> We are back to square one with the problems with him<br /> So all and all the whole &quot;Lore&quot; the Week of Nightmares presented gave nothing but a headache and a tons of problems","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 08-01-2025, 04:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-01T08:28:56-07:00","id":1552803,"title":"","content":"First bit. Bombs: Doesn't matter what bombs do in real life, and the real world. These were magical techno-magic made up fantasy bombs. They were powered by magic, and shat out magic radiation that mainly harmed supernaturals. I pasted the literal explanation that is straight from the book. You don't have to like it, but according to the narrative, the damage from the bombs wasn't a huge deal and was easily covered up by the typhoon. If you can suspend disbelief enough that vampires and other supernatural shit exists, it shouldn't be hard to do the same for magical bombs. Now whether you use the information or not, that's between you and the storyteller. Golden rule and all, if you don't like it change it.<br /> <br /> On top of that there is this nugget (from &quot;WtA: A World of Rage&quot;) as stupid as it is:<br /> <img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1929_1754058176751_36\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1929\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1929\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1929&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> All the supernaturals covered it up, changed information, and because its the World of Darkness, the masses just don't care. Apathy and all that.<br /> <br /> Is it kinda dumb? Yeah very. Is it inline with the stupid gonzo stuff that happens in WoD? Totally.<br /> <br /> <br /> Second bit. Ravnos:<br /> <br /> The narrative (Graverobber's Coterie) in Clanbook Ravnos Revised, show how their Chimerstry flew out of control, and then how after they all started turning on each other, trying to cannibalize each other. This hunger to eat each other lasted four days, and lines up with the time that the Antedeluvian was fighting.<br /> <br /> Quite frankly in my opinion Dracien/Zapathasura was a wight. From his awakening in the book where it actually happens, &quot;Time of Thin Blood,&quot; he acts and speaks like a wight, only wanting to feed. He is pegged at being a super selfish person, who was made even more selfish by becoming kindred. His curse was to never know satisfaction, which is why he went East. He was trying to learn what Saulot did in the East since when Saulot returns he seems at peace. From there he ends up in his own little war with the Kuei-jin, and is abandoned by his childer. The Path of Paradox is wholy a product of Chandraputra trying to control the disparate elements of the errant clan. Nothing about Dracien/Zapathasura is ever shown that he had -any- self control, and it pushes more that he has degenerated fully by the time he wakes in '99.<br /> <br /> While low level Animalism is about staving off the Beast and trying to control it, all the high level powers that aren't about animals specifically, are mostly about moving your Beast elsewhere, or using it to attack and letting it run free.<br /> <br /> Specifically:<br /> Animalism 5: <b>Drawing Out the Beast</b>: When about to Frenzy, send your Beast into another person.\u200b<br /> Animalism 7:<b> Beast Shard</b>: Split up your Beast and instill shards in others, making them more prone to Frenzy and making them more susceptible to your Disciplines.<br /> <br /> I could easily see a flailing dying demi-god master of Animalism, trying to stave off Rotschreck from the light of <i>four suns</i> by sending it's Beast into all its progeny.<br /> <br /> Third bit. Other Antedeluvians.<br /> <br /> You're going to hate this one but, it has to be said. <b>NO</b> other Antedeluvians have been shown to have been out right destroyed. It either happened in antiquity (Brujah, Ventru, Malkav) and thus there is no real evidence, or was a play by them to transcend their form.<br /> <br /> <br /> For the ones we see in the game lines :<br /> <br /> Saulot submitted to the diablerie and allowed his soul to be subsumed by Tremere because he was literally the master of the Soul Manipulation discipline Valeren. He exists still within Tremere. All of the Salubri are shown to have felt the diablerie of Saulot.<br /> <br /> Cappadocius, the master of the Bodily Death discipline (Mortis before Necromancy...) allowed his body to be consumed by Augustus, and continued to exist as a special Wraith until the Maelstrom drove him into Spectre-hood. He again did not die as an Antedeluvian but transcended and passed his mantle onto Augustus. (Augustus mind you who I still believe was originally intended to be a backup body..) By the time he is destroyed he is a Spectre and has no ties to his clan anymore, and Augustus is the one who holds that mantle.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce faked his death with Visscitude, taking Lugoj's place. He's also everything, everyone, everywhere etc. Be a good lad.<br /> <br /> Lasombra fucked off to the the abyss, leaving a simulacrum of himself. This was not an unknown thing he could do (waw Obtenebration, so cool, much blood magic, so Abyss Mysticism,) seeing as he did it for Gratiano when he embraced him.<br /> <br /> Malkav causes the events of Fountains of Bright Crimson, as he transcends into the Madness Network, which is an advanced version of Dementation 9:Brother's Gift imo, which was described as:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This power baffles those few who\u2019ve heard of it, for it seems totally at odds with Dementation. Brother\u2019s Gift frees the subject from all Derangements, granting total lucidity. The ancient Malkavians know the truth; Brother\u2019s Gift was a trick Malkav himself learned while studying with his brother Saulot. Malkav could not heal his own pain like Saulot could, but he could shunt it elsewhere, a task that became easier as his brood grew. Malkav poured his madness into the blood, which now carries his madness in the veins of all Malkavians. </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Brujah's and Ventru's fates are both in antiquity and are conjecture. Was Brujah diablerized by Troile? Is Brujah stuck traveling through time? Is Brujah and Troile stuck in a time loop? Were Brujah and Troile both Agatha all along? Who the fuck knows. Ventru is the same type of fuckery. Was he killed in the Second City? Did he &quot;I lived bitch&quot; and continue to embrace over the ages, or are all the Ventrue elders a bunch of lying diablerists? Who the fuck knows.<br /> <br /> Toreador is MIA. Nos fucks around with nukes. Set is MIA. Haqim is a sleeping pool of blood.<br /> <br /> Reverberations through the blood -are- a common thread among powerful kindred either being killed or changing, but what happened to the Ravnos was unique to their situation, and the death of their founder. The closest thing would be what happened with Malkav, but that situation was unique in itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-01T10:16:28-07:00","id":1552806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552803#post1552803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First bit. Bombs: Doesn't matter what bombs do in real life, and the real world. These were magical techno-magic made up fantasy bombs.</div> </div> </div> </div>True to a certain extend. But as Technocratic artifacts it is expected within the fiction that they work as the real thing whenever it isn't clearly stated they don't.<br /> <br /> In this regard, the explanation is seriously lacking.<br /> <br /> Suspension of disbelief is a matter of balance, and the main problem here is that the end result is inconsistent with the setup. The setup thoroughly states how huge the decision was, it makes clear that using those nukes isn't a light decision and that there will be consequences.<br /> <br /> And then it procedes to have no consequences. <b>That</b> is the problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552803#post1552803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as stupid as it is</div> </div> </div> </div>Our point is precisely that it is stupid. No one is arguing it isn't the canon, just that it is a stupid canon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552803#post1552803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and because its the World of Darkness, the masses just don't care. Apathy and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>One and a half million people dying at once?<br /> <br /> You see, the problem here is that this only makes sense from an exclusively <b>AMERICAN</b> POV, and that's one of the recurrent problems with WoD, and the biggest problem with the Week of Nightmares.<br /> <br /> The 2002's Los Angeles Earthquake and Devil's Night Riots was an event with less than a tenth of the magnitude of the Week of Nightmares, yet it was the talk of the year and the following year, because of course it was, it was in the US. This is pure bullshit.<br /> <br /> It isn't too wild to think that no one <b>in the US</b> would be talking about the events in Bangladesh after long, except for the military (those wouldn't ever let a nuclear detonation go unnoticed and non-investigated). But what about people in India, Bhutan, Myanmar, Nepal, China, and Bangladesh itself, just to name a few nearby countries that together had 1,5 <b>billion</b> inhabitants even back then (now India has almost that many alone)?<br /> <br /> An organization like the Technocracy can't be as blind to the opinions of the masses all around the world as the typical American is. Their place in the setting requires that they care about more than what Fox News has to say. It makes no sense whatsoever that this hasn't attracted major attention in the region where it happened.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552803#post1552803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second bit. Ravnos</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole setup for Zapathasura to awaken is ludicrous, so the problem begins way before that.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552803#post1552803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The narrative (Graverobber's Coterie) in Clanbook Ravnos Revised, show how their Chimerstry flew out of control, and then how after they all started turning on each other, trying to cannibalize each other. This hunger to eat each other lasted four days, and lines up with the time that the Antedeluvian was fighting.</div> </div> </div> </div>What doesn't align with that is the clan being almost wiped out in the process.<br /> <br /> Vampires don't live in huge clusters, and the Ravnos are no exception. Most can go weeks at a time without seeing another Kindred, much less another clan mate. The few that live with or near other members of the clan, live with one or two at most. And once aware of the problem, it's even more likely that they would avoid the risk of contact with each other.<br /> <br /> The idea that 4 days of rampage was enough to decimate the clan is completely ludicrous.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552803#post1552803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reverberations through the blood -are- a common thread among powerful kindred either being killed or changing</div> </div> </div> </div>Which doesn't makes <b>this</b> particular reverberation particularly believable. It's contrived.<br /> <br /> But more importantly than it being contrived, the problem is the effect it was made to have. Because while in Whatsonian terms the Ravnos fought to death because the Antediluvian went nuts, in a Doylist perspective it was the other way around: the Antediluvian went nuts in that particular way for the authors to wipe out the Ravnos. And that was a stupid and asshole move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-01T12:49:29-07:00","id":1552812,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> I wish I could up vote more your message.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26219\" data-vbnamecard=\"26219\">Aydoo</a> totally serious question, are you arguing in good faith here or just trolling? Because it seems you are not reading anything the previous posters mention, you just reply to say (more or less) <i>&quot;yeah, but you are wrong&quot; </i>it seems you are commenting on a whole different thread, or bad faith replying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-01T17:59:11-07:00","id":1552817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552806#post1552806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But more importantly than it being contrived, the problem is the effect it was made to have. Because while in Whatsonian terms the Ravnos fought to death because the Antediluvian went nuts, in a Doylist perspective it was the other way around: the Antediluvian went nuts in that particular way for the authors to wipe out the Ravnos. And that was a stupid and asshole move.</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost all of the Revised era's setting changes can fit into two buckets.<br /> <br /> The first bucket is &quot;I think this idea is quite stupid so I'm getting rid of it, and replacing it with my own, much better, idea.&quot;<br /> <br /> The second bucket is &quot;We are actually going to run a Gehenna storyline, and we need to do things to showcase that the End Times are happening now.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Ravnos Week of Nightmares is in that second category. As such that event - and similar &quot;countdown&quot; events like the destruction of the Tremere anti-tribu - should just be ignored if you didn't want the world to end in 2004 or whenever it was. It's a storyline driven event. And if you are not telling a Gehenna story, there's no reason to include it in your game. (And personally if I was to run an actual Gehenna chronicle, I probably wouldn't use the metaplot story as laid out although I might steal a few ideas.)<br /> <br /> Other setting changes in Revised were not of this &quot;countdown to Gehenna&quot; variety. It was just because the new developers and writers didn't like certain aspects of the old setting and just got rid of it. Getting rid of the entire Tal'mahe'Ra and eliminating the Souleaters is of that nature of change. They just didn't like it as a setting element so they dumped it. This is more like a DC Comics &quot;Earth-One&quot; and &quot;Earth-Two&quot; scenario in which there is no story need for these changes. It's just an indication that they are two different settings, reusing a lot of the same names and tropes while detailing a different &quot;world&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-01T21:27:17-07:00","id":1552822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552817#post1552817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Ravnos Week of Nightmares is in that second category.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really not that sure, not entirely at least.<br /> <br /> The Ravnos had been a problem for a time by then. It was a mostly badly written clan, full of racist tropes, and a lot of players at the time were heavily critics of them.<br /> <br /> Overall the Week of Nightmares was a Countdown to Gehenna thing, that's for sure. In fact, it was meant as the very first &quot;Sign of Judgement&quot; in the setting, the starting point of the whole Revised metaplot.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't change that some details in it could have other goals, and I'm pretty sure wiping out the Ravnos wasn't just a way to convey the apocalyptic mood, but a convenient means to get rid of a problem they simply didn't want to solve anymore, if they even saw it as something to solve instead of just getting rid of regardless.<br /> <br /> Just look how the Banu-Haqim and Gangrel also had major setbacks at the time, but they didn't simply say they're dead almost to the last, to the point of their society crumbling. The way they made it clear that surviving Ravnos are the rarest of rare exceptions is quite telling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-02T01:54:06-07:00","id":1552825,"title":"","content":"I also don't really think the &quot;bucket&quot; analogy holds. Too many elements of Revised are clearly written with multiple goals.<br /> <br /> To move away from VtM for a moment: the Avatar Storm in Mage. The Avatar Storm served to both be an in-universe rationale for instituting major changes to the setting to help replace elements deemed negatives for the game according to the developers of the time (the Mage team - and with far less animus than many fans seem to want to acknowledge - felt late Mage 2e had gone far too epic in scope and need to be returned to a more grounded point where the huge conflicts between archwizards and fleets of voidships weren't something for normal games to get into), as well as setting off the Time of Judgement metaplot for Mage by breaking the stalemate between the Traditions and Technocracy so they and other factions would start to make their big moves.<br /> <br /> I think it's easier to just think of Revised's changes as having some mixture of two overarching goals: do what the developers at the time felt was best for making the setting better, and moving the metaplot forward. While it's certainly simple to point to individual examples that are heavily biased towards one goal or the other, it doesn't seem to serve much purpose when editions aren't bound to only following one design goal at a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-02T07:26:58-07:00","id":1552831,"title":"","content":"To start out:<br /> @Ibeaumanior My answer to you question is, &quot;No.&quot; Lets stick to talking about the game and not each other.<br /> <br /> Next:<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> I'll use numbers to signify for your replies, it'll be easier this way instead of quoting everything if that's ok. Starting from the top.<br /> <br /> 1. Absolutely agree with this assessment. It is a problem and one that stems from the company setting up to end game lines. There were well aware at this point that they were going to shutter the WoD for months and months for what became known as WoD 2.0 so everything the company presented was moving towards that front. It lead to a lot of inconsistent and sloppy writing.<br /> <br /> 2. My argument in the first place is that the context and facts were being misconstrued, which is why I posted the actual fiction. I will admit on my part this a bit of &quot;well ackshully&quot; but it is what it is at this point. The fiction says &quot;<i>the bomb air-bursts caused serious property damage and death only in the immediate vicinity of the blast, while slaughtering the supernatural creatures many kilometers distant.&quot;</i> While you can disagree that it should be different based on real world physics, that its a stupid inclusion, that its tone deaf, that it makes no sense, that you just don't like it, or that bombs just don't work that way; in this case, in this situation, in this fiction, it did and does work that way. This was in reply to specifically the comment of:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a lot of physical damage in the area's landscape that couldn't possibly be caused by a storm, not to say that the three nukes were nukes, they left radiation behind, so we have huge swaths of uninhabitable land, and a lot of the people who died from them didn't die immediately, but up to weeks after. </div> </div> </div>3. The company that makes the books is American, and everything in them is written from an American POV. Originally the books were written for specifically an American audience, and over time it has become a globally recognized brand. There has been and was always a bias towards tone deaf Americanism in the writing. It is also a product of its time and the experiences and foibles of the people who developed it. While we may be old enough to have lived through the time period in which all this was written, there has no doubt been a cultural shift from the time of publication till now. &quot;Time of Thin Blood&quot; the publication that first mentions the Week of Nightmares, is dated as being copyright 1999, that was <b>TWENTY-SIX</b> years ago.<br /> <br /> In fiction, from the point of view of the world population, they were either extremely apathetic (hey its a World of Darkness and terrible atrocities happen all the time, or everyone is eating O'Tolley burgers and are under Wyrm corruption or something else hand wavy,) they believed that it was just all the massive typhoon, or as the last fiction I posted showed the cover up was just that good, because apparently the whole supernatural community got in on it together, not just the Technocracy. Its dumb, but that's ok. By being fiction, its allowed to be dumb, by its very nature because its not real, and doesn't have to conform to what is.<br /> <br /> 4. I disagree with this opinion, vehemently. There were many hints that this type of thing (not necessarily the Ravnos specifically) would happen over the years of publication in various books. If you would like to request it, I would be glad to share examples.<br /> <br /> 5. This goes back to the way that the author's were trying to portray the Ravnos themselves. In earlier editions (where the Ravnos were being tied to Gypsies/Rroma) and even so in Revised (where they moved their roots to the India subcontinent,) the Ravnos were shown to be a more social group of Kindred. The Ravnos over the editions are depicted as being mainly ostracized by every other faction, run out of most domains, and so due this, they became a very insular clan, mainly making coteries of just Ravnos. If the Ravnos, a clan that might have had 1000 members world wide, were mainly lots of clustered coteries, it stands to reason that yeah, many would get wiped out. Originally in &quot;Time of Thin Blood&quot; they declared that perhaps only 100 survived, but by the time of &quot;Clanbook: Ravnos Revised&quot; they would walk that back to perhaps up to 300, and then in the same breath say &quot;Well you know what, who the fuck cares, if you want Ravnos, they're still around at full power.&quot; This smacks of editorial meddling. Someone didn't like the clan (my guess Achille) and mandated that they be gotten rid of, and over the years of publication it went back and forth. Revised was a turbulent time.<br /> <br /> 6. For the first bit, I agree with the assessment that its contrived, and refer back to my statement in point 1. For the second bit all I can think of is this image<br /> <br /> <img title=\"why-not-both-why-not.gif\" data-tempid=\"temp_1930_1754143249374_22\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1930\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1930\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1930&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"why-not-both-why-not.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> Furthermore, I agree with both <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24802-blackfox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24802\" data-vbnamecard=\"24802\">Blackfox</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> comments. It <b>was</b> in service of moving the plot lines to an end point and shuttering the World of Darkness line, but at the same time each individual writer had their own ideas and motivations being presented. Sometimes these differing points of view did not line up in a way that was cohesive for the entire line. You can see that many of the books were being written simultaneously and without cross input from other teams so there is quite a bit of inconsistency in tone and direction. Add to what seems apparent mandates to meet certain social shifting trends of the time period, the movement of the narrative of the game line towards ending said game line, and some of the more vocal dev's personal feelings on the content, you get what Revised ended up turning into, for better or worse.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the over arching topic here anyway. Your relationship with and to the lore changes over the years of the World of Darkness really breaks down into your personal relationship to the IP itself. What I mean by this is, there are many posters here I have seen that have a much different relationship to it than I personally do.<br /> <br /> For many people its just a game that they play, they don't care for the story, the meta plot, or anything outside the strict mechanics and some of the most basic world building that the game presents. This of course is a valid way to enjoy the IP. It is a game after all and is meant to be played however you want. We'll call this group A.<br /> <br /> On the other hand you have those like me, who frankly only care about the meta plot, story and world building of the game. While I've played the game as a game over the years, its not the part that hooked me into the IP. The stories presented, the lore, and the mysteries that the authors hinted at is all what I find intriguing. We'll call this group B.<br /> <br /> Now there's various shades of gray in between these two group's extremes, and probably other factors I'm not considering. The problem with lore and the narrative really stems from how closely you align with one of these groups really. If the lore and narrative gets in the way of the mechanical aspect of the game (changes in Revised,) its usually to the displeasure of group A, and the reverse is usually true when mechanical rules suddenly upend the flow of the narrative (changes in 5th edition,) to the displeasure of group B.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-02T10:46:48-07:00","id":1552836,"title":"","content":"The next question I should ask is what metaplot lore did you completely ignore in your game?<br /> <br /> In ours the Sabbat sect fell apart as they learned that Lasombra and Tzismce never fell and learning that their battles against the 3rd generation was meaningless as most of them have moved onto more important things<br /> <br /> We kept the Beckoning but changed it to a sort of judgment by the antivulieans on which clan members were worthy of survival or final death and some coming back more powerful or much weaker.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThere are others but I don't think people would want a essay on it.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-02T18:12:18-07:00","id":1552845,"title":"","content":"The thing with the Avatar Storm is that it felt like it clashed a bit with the inherent conceits of the supernatural at hand when one already had sorcerers for lower-stakes games. Making the difficulty of Umbra access an environmental thing rather than one of Awakened power was on the one hand the only way they could have handled the matter given how they were not going for a retcon, but on the other hand it meant that there was always going to be a dissonance between what players were effectively allowed to do by the circumstances of the setting and the broader perspective naturally invited by their powers. With Masquerade it was not really like what the players were actually able to do was affected; nothing happened to elder powers either narratively or mechanically, and it was not like player's were actually expected to attain them in the same way that a mage could be expected to reach 5 dot Spheres. Arguably, apart from those players who had their character options essentially cut out of the picture through stuff like the Ravnos getting annihilated, the metaplot changes didn't the Masquerade's player main play experience as it did the Ascension player (although arguably, one could also say that Ascension players were not focused on cosmic shenanigans anyway, but determining what the table demographics were really like back at that time is obviously a difficult task).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-03T22:01:03-07:00","id":1552865,"title":"","content":"First of all, I'm not seeing the image. I'm seeing the code in the quote edition, but nothing visible, and there's no url in the code.<br /> <br /> I'll keep using quotes merely because I'll lose myself if I don't, no prob using numbers, I like the system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552831#post1552831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Absolutely agree with this assessment. It is a problem and one that stems from the company setting up to end game lines. There were well aware at this point that they were going to shutter the WoD for months and months for what became known as WoD 2.0 so everything the company presented was moving towards that front. It lead to a lot of inconsistent and sloppy writing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Explains, but doesn't justifies. I'm not saying that keeping consistency is easy under such conditions, but at that point they had 8 years of experience with WoD alone, and many had previous works, so they had no excuses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552831#post1552831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. My argument in the first place is that the context and facts were being misconstrued</div> </div> </div> </div>A few things, here.<br /> <br /> 1- Here's a thread about changes in lore that we hated. At no point my argument was meant to say things couldn't happen the way they did. It was to say I hated it (and with the caveat that I hated the aftermath as a game element. The story itself was a very fun read, gonzo and all);<br /> <br /> 2- Sorry if I wasn't clear. I didn't meant the structural damage was specifically caused by the nukes. What the nukes brought (and as far as I know it was never stated to not be present) was radiation. The damage was caused by the whole thing, and probably by the battle on the ground (that killed 1,2 million people) more than by anything else;<br /> <br /> 3- Even with a limited size explosion, the nukes are still detectable. Not that it isn't something they could work around, but they didn't. The more egregious part was still the setup of high stakes that ended up being really low stakes, and that's regardless of any explanation on why the cover-up worked. It was like characters dying in Naruto because a Jutsu was dangerous to use;<br /> <br /> 4- The bombs still killed 60k+ people. Not supernaturals (even because that would be almost the entire Vampire population of the world at the time), but common people. That's almost the same as the immediate deaths of Hiroshima, which was a nuke in a major population center. So the problem with the nukes specifically isn't just the description of the blast, but a death toll that can't be easily dismissed (at least not when it's a single, localized event).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552831#post1552831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. The company that makes the books is American, and everything in them is written from an American POV.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not so simple, for several reasons. For one, the company was already licensing translations all over the world. Here in Brazil Vampire arrived in 1994, for example. So the company had been aware for years that their audience wasn't only American, or even European.<br /> <br /> And while it wasn't nearly like today, by 1999 awareness about other countries was already a thing. Not common by any means, but enough for White Wolf specifically to be expected to do better (because it was their thing, plus because they already had a history of backlash with this sort of thing, and of doing better after the backlash).<br /> <br /> More on point, though, given that the point of the thread is to say what we hate. Well, I hate this. And I hated this at the time. Yes, I've read Time of Thin Blood when it was a recent thing, so I'm well aware of how things were at the time. And I'm Brazilian, so this kind of thing is personal to me, their American roots be damned.<br /> <br /> It's also important to keep in mind that regardless of the time those things were written, we're talking about our <i><b>current</b></i> opinions. So it's perfectly valid to think badly today about something that was an error only in hindsight (arguably). No one is being asked to say what we thought about it at the time, or if we think it was a reasonable take back them.<br /> <br /> So, while this argument of yours here is true, it doesn't has any weight on my current opinion about the whole thing.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552831#post1552831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they believed that it was just all the massive typhoon</div> </div> </div> </div>So, here's the thing:<br /> <br /> The 1970's Bhola Cyclone was <b>the deadliest storm in recorded history</b>, yet it killed <u>between 300k and 450k people</u>. It's a historical event talked about even today.<br /> <br /> My point being, a storm that killed 3 to 5 times more people simply wouldn't be forgotten. And that's a big part of why their description is lacking. However good the cover-up ended up being, the storm itself would have been a major event people and media would talk about for several months, rescue missions, recovery efforts and preliminary investigations would take maybe years, and people in the meteorology field would study intensely for more than a decade (and not so intensely forever).<br /> <br /> If the aftermath were that the cover-up was successful, but it's an ongoing effort because there's a lot of people there looking into the storm for its own sake, that would be a hugely better option. As &quot;after a month no one cared about&quot; it's simply stupid.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552831#post1552831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its dumb, but that's ok. By being fiction, its allowed to be dumb, by its very nature because its not real, and doesn't have to conform to what is.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's simply a debate-killer argument, saying no criticism should be levied because it's fiction.<br /> <br /> We're here to discuss the fiction, to state our opinions about this fiction, and we definitely have a right to do so, and to apply whatever reasoning and criteria we want (as long as we argue why we think it's relevant, of course), because fiction isn't excused from being dissected and evaluated just for being fiction. And there is such a thing as quality in fiction, being dumb isn't a crime, but isn't irrelevant, either.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552831#post1552831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. I disagree with this opinion, vehemently. There were many hints that this type of thing (not necessarily the Ravnos specifically) would happen over the years of publication in various books. If you would like to request it, I would be glad to share examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>At no moment did I say that this was the only time something ridiculous happened in the game's lore. It wasn't even particularly egregious. The end result (eliminating the clan as an existing faction) was the important part, the setup being ludicrous is merely a side note.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552831#post1552831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Ravnos were shown to be a more social group of Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but not like that.<br /> <br /> Just as Vampires in general, most Ravnos didn't live in Coteries, at least not to the point of sharing havens or even seeing each other every night.<br /> <br /> Most Ravnos travel alone, and spend most of their time traveling. They do keep in contact with each other more than most clans, but we're talking a situation were their <b><i>average</i></b> organization would mean staying in groups of 10 or more for most of the time. Keeping in mind that I'm referring to the original depiction of their decimation, I don't hate how they backed down as time went on.<br /> <br /> Nine in ten Ravnos being killed by their clan-mates in the space of <u>four days</u> is too much, just too much.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552831#post1552831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your relationship with and to the lore changes over the years of the World of Darkness really breaks down into your personal relationship to the IP itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not, it isn't so simple.<br /> <br /> While the relationship with the IP is relevant, the opinion of each person with any particular lore change can hinge in a huge variety of reasons.<br /> <br /> You're invalidating any argument by reducing it to a single, generic characteristic and shifting responsibility exclusively back to the person, when that's not how fiction and art work at all, game or other type.<br /> <br /> People don't disagree with you just because they don't have the same relationship with the IP. Nor are they impacted differently by a given thing just because of that.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552831#post1552831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For many people its just a game that they play, they don't care for the story, the meta plot, or anything outside the strict mechanics and some of the most basic world building that the game presents. This of course is a valid way to enjoy the IP. It is a game after all and is meant to be played however you want. We'll call this group A.<br /> <br /> On the other hand you have those like me, who frankly only care about the meta plot, story and world building of the game. While I've played the game as a game over the years, its not the part that hooked me into the IP. The stories presented, the lore, and the mysteries that the authors hinted at is all what I find intriguing. We'll call this group B.\u200b<br /> <br /> Now there's various shades of gray in between these two group's extremes, and probably other factors I'm not considering. The problem with lore and the narrative really stems from how closely you align with one of these groups really.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even assuming this as a sliding scale, this is a gross simplification.<br /> <br /> People may have a plethora of positions and reactions to either aspect of the setting, and how deeply they're invested in one has no bearing on how much they're invested in the other. The way people relate to the game has a far greater variety and reasons behind it than this oversimplified view opposing &quot;game vs lore&quot;.<br /> <br /> By the way, if you didn't notice so far, everyone here is talking exclusively about lore, which is itself an example of how wrong this take is. How much a given lore piece enriches or impoverishes the setting is purely a lore analysis. How much it facilitates different stories is purely a lore analysis. How it impacts the potential fiction of specific games isn't just a game analysis, it is still primarily a lore analysis, if lore within a specific context.<br /> <br /> And analysis within specific contexts is still perfectly valid. Analysis in any context is valid in its own right.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552831#post1552831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the lore and narrative gets in the way of the mechanical aspect of the game (changes in Revised,) its usually to the displeasure of group A, and the reverse is usually true when mechanical rules suddenly upend the flow of the narrative (changes in 5th edition,) to the displeasure of group B.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, an oversimplification that completely ignores why people like or dislike something, and with a result that is blatantly false.<br /> <br /> Changes don't pleasure one group in lieu of the other, those are unrelated things. Even because for people who only care about mechanics the changes in lore have no impact whatsoever. What we're discussing here is something that exclusively affects people who are invested in the lore, and to the extent they're invested in the lore.<br /> <br /> There are many reasons why I don't like the Week of Nightmares, and many among those reasons are precisely because I think it upends the flow of the narrative to achieve an unrelated goal, as nothing in the narrative made the end of the Ravnos either likely, necessary or preferable. Even because they still had a write-up and stats in <i>Revised</i>, so from a purely mechanical standpoint there was nothing to complain about.<br /> <br /> Likewise I didn't like most of the changes in 5th Edition, but they have nothing to do with mechanics. Most of the mechanical changes didn't need a change in lore, most of the changes in lore didn't affect mechanics, and even when they were related that has no bearing on the quality of the changes, or if they were the better or worse particular changes. The bombing of Vienna, the new stance of the Camarilla on the Ancients, the Ministry and the Hecata, the Beckoning, the Sabbat abandoning territories to go to war, the changes in Sect of the Lasombra and the Tzimisce, none of those were primarily mechanical changes, yet they're the things many people didn't like. And other people did like.<br /> <br /> Even changes in mechanics frequently are liked or disliked more because of their effects in the lore than in actual playability. Sure, some players hated that the Avatar Storm changed how easy it is to cross the Gauntlet, but most don't really care because in practice it was a minor increase in difficulty. Many more disliked it because it destroyed huge swaths of Mage's setting and they liked to explore the Horizon Realms and interact with their NPCs, and the changes in how the Avatar Storm works mostly affected the setting itself and the viability of Realms.<br /> <br /> People don't dislike the Week of Nightmares, or any other particular piece of lore, just because they belong to group A or B. They have actual complex reasons and arguments behind it. And they don't agree or disagree with your opinions just because they're less invested in the metaplot than you are, nor are they more or less invested in the metaplot because of how much they're invested in the setting's lore in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-03T22:28:18-07:00","id":1552868,"title":"","content":"This sounds like what this thread would turn into Monteparnas. Suspension of disbelief can only go so far in a game setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-03T23:20:26-07:00","id":1552874,"title":"","content":"The inane thing about Ravnos is that Revised did in fact destroy another previously playable faction in a way that didn't do away with the entire concept of the Masquerade: the disappearance of the Tremere <i>antitribu</i>. Striking the most densely populated country on Earth with the equivalent of the bomb that levelled Hiroshima was a deliberate choice; I happen to think it was a really bad one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28177-gamiem","name":"gamiem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T02:56:26-07:00","id":1552876,"title":"","content":"I used the week of nightmares to make lemonade when made the ravnos a full fledged sabbat clan shifting them to the antitribu away from previous issues. <br /> <br /> I also used a week of nightmares style scenario for a technocratic game when something became active in the apalatians. So its not a writting dead end.<br /> <br /> Imo the issue is its one of the early phases of metaplot as railroading which have become increasingly prevailing in 5th.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T10:07:07-07:00","id":1552881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavyArms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To move away from VtM for a moment: the Avatar Storm in Mage. The Avatar Storm served to both be an in-universe rationale for instituting major changes to the setting <b>to help replace elements deemed negatives for the game according to the developers of the time </b></div> </div> </div> </div>See, this is what I don't like.<br /> <br /> And it can be said the same about very much every change I end hating on WoD. &quot;the developers of the time&quot; deemed negative the way Ravnos, the Sabbat, the Imbued Hunters, the Garou Nation ... were as previously understood ... for whatever narrative they were wanting to push foward at the moment.<br /> <br /> So, instead of creating options, they choose to nuke such &quot;bad&quot; narratives out. Naturally, the gamers using them would hate that choice.<br /> <br /> In the case of the Avatar Storm. It was never necessary to make ground-level games: A fleet of Void Ships wasn't going to barge into your street level game on Earth due to how the cosmology of mage it's built arround the assumption those things can only happen on other worlds far away from the Consensus (regardless if the rules are a bit wibbly-wobbly).<br /> <br /> A mage needed to invest in Spirit, and/or have Backgrounds (such as having a powerful Chantry or Mentors) that would led them to those &quot;epic fantasy&quot; places for those high-level plots to matter at all. It's not something that would intrude if it wasn't seeked by the players.<br /> <br /> As a tool to change the status-quo, it was incredibly heay-handed (a rock falls, everyone dies, but with more metaphisics to it).<br /> <br /> Destroying the realms that they sold in previous books it's already taking toys away from you. But it wouldn't have caused so much controversy if it hadn't <i>remained</i> to threaten and punish players that wanted to engage with the &quot;elements deemed negative&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the Mage team - and with far less animus than many fans seem to want to acknowledge - felt late Mage 2e had gone far too epic in scope and need to be returned to a more grounded point </div> </div> </div>&quot;returned&quot; it's an interesting word, because I'm not sure 1e can be said to be much more grounded than 2e (<s>wasn't the dyson sphere part of 1e?, el vivo? MECHA?</s> - nvm. I've found out, the dyson sphere - the COP - was on 2e, MECHA it's from 1e.). But I'm pretty sure Mage was never AS grounded as Revised was intended to be, in any case.<br /> <br /> As an example of how much they wanted to &quot;ground&quot; Mages on Revised: The Bitter Road does spend a lot of pages stressing out how you should get a real job, and talking about mages in their grounded, mundane, lives.<br /> <br /> I took that as vaguely insulting when I read it at the time, really. But I get it wasn't done with animosity.<br /> <br /> It shows the authors are trying to institute out the tendency of players to use magick to skip all the <s>mundanity</s> drama of real life, and to teach better ways to STs that let them get away with it... <hr /><br /> In any case, the backlash Revised caused should be a good proof that the oppinion of the developpers of the time about what was negative for the game wasn't shared by a large portion of the fanbase.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't be surprised in the slightest if Mage v5 keeps trying to push the square on the ground hole by cutting corners and taking options away ... and I'm probably not gona like it either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-04-2025, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T14:43:17-07:00","id":1552890,"title":"","content":"First of all I've never said you couldn't like or dislike something, nor was I refuting your feeling on it, hell I agree with a lot of them. At the same time, its supposed to be a discussion and I'm trying (no matter how badly) to express why I feel in opposition to your opinion. Neither of our opinions are infallibly correct, but there are -facts- that the publication did present, and even if you don't like them, doesn't change what happened.<br /> <br /> If you couldn't see the images I'll help you out here and describe them, the first two images in the first posts were snippets from the books themselves. One is from Time of Thin Blood and the description by the Technocratic Agent of the events, and what happened. He lists the death toll, the property damage, the armaments used, and other various information. The second image was from World of Rage, and is a cheeky description of who was covering up the events (EG: Everyone.) It talks about how in one instance a werewolf, two mages, two vampires and a wraith all met in the same building while covering up the event, and parted ways, as an example of every faction being responsible for the cover up. The third image was the meme of the little Mexican girl saying &quot;Why not both?&quot; from an American Taco commercial.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552865#post1552865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Likewise I didn't like most of the changes in 5th Edition, but they have nothing to do with mechanics. Most of the mechanical changes didn't need a change in lore, most of the changes in lore didn't affect mechanics, and even when they were related that has no bearing on the quality of the changes, or if they were the better or worse particular changes. The bombing of Vienna, the new stance of the Camarilla on the Ancients, the Ministry and the Hecata, the Beckoning, the Sabbat abandoning territories to go to war, the changes in Sect of the Lasombra and the Tzimisce, none of those were primarily mechanical changes, yet they're the things many people didn't like. And other people did like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to keep this short, that you aren't seeing how these things you mention are Lore that affects Mechanics.<br /> <br /> Lore wise Tremere does a ritual in the Transylvania Chronicles Book to regain power after losing his body, killing the Tremere Antitribu.<br /> Mechanical: You can't play Tremere Antitribu. (Well you can do whatever the fuck you want, but its -discouraged- by the game, and no longer officially supported.)<br /> <br /> Other examples: Gangrel leaving the Camarilla, Week of Nightmares, Malkavians losing Dominate for Dementation, Visscitude changes and rechanges and changes again into nonexistance, the destruction of the True Black Hand, and many many other things. These all had both mechanical effects and lore effects by changing and making the world smaller.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552865#post1552865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> At no moment did I say that this was the only time something ridiculous happened in the game's lore. It wasn't even particularly egregious. The end result (eliminating the clan as an existing faction) was the important part, the setup being ludicrous is merely a side note.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're not even talking about the same thing at this point. I was saying there were major hints throughout the publication that a mass killing of a clan would awaken its founder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552865#post1552865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ravnos</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel you need to probably re-read the Clan books, because your idea of the Ravnos is quite at odds from the published material.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> hits the nail on the head with that post and put things much better than I could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T19:01:02-07:00","id":1552896,"title":"","content":"V5, many but the main issue is Oblivion and the Lasombra. If the Lasombra had that since the beginning they had access to everything the Cappadocian and Giovanni had, that would change the entire Cainite history. Their curse would also be pointless since Caine cursing them for a thing that would be an issue millennia into the future is really pointless.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T19:26:59-07:00","id":1552898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552890#post1552890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all I've never said you couldn't like or dislike something</div> </div> </div> </div>You didn't invalidate feelings, you invalidated arguments instead of engaging with them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552890#post1552890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there are -facts- that the publication did present, and even if you don't like them, doesn't change what happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>A total of zero people said they would change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552890#post1552890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you couldn't see the images I'll help you out here and describe them</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. Anyway, it doesn't seems to change anything relevant in the exchange, but it's certainly a shame that I couldn't see it.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552890#post1552890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to keep this short, that you aren't seeing how these things you mention are Lore that affects Mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every lore affects mechanics. You missed my point that the distinction itself is a fallacy.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552890#post1552890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Well you can do whatever the fuck you want, but its -discouraged- by the game, and no longer officially supported.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is a point relevant only to people that care about the lore, as others will simply ignore it.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552890#post1552890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're not even talking about the same thing at this point. I was saying there were major hints throughout the publication that a mass killing of a clan would awaken its founder.</div> </div> </div> </div>We are, you just didn't understood.<br /> <br /> I don't think killing a helluva lot of Ravnos wouldn't awaken their Ante. This is, by itself, ok.<br /> <br /> But the reasons, the mass embraces, the war, everything was contrived and illogical.<br /> <br /> So, my problem isn't with the basic idea of a mass killing of Ravnos awakening Zapathasura, my problem is with the setup for this mass killing.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552890#post1552890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel you need to probably re-read the Clan books, because your idea of the Ravnos is quite at odds from the published material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly, I'll give it a re-read eventually.<br /> <br /> Yet, the main point persists: for the enraged Ravnos to kill each other to the point of only 100 (give or take) survivors, that necessarily means there was only 100 individual groups of Ravnos, with lone travelers counting as a single group and anyone with less contact than twice a week counting as a separate group.<br /> <br /> That means <b>All the Ravnos</b> being divided between 100 units at most, with an <u>average</u> of 10 vampires per group, which includes big groups to compensate for the smaller/solitary ones.<br /> <br /> If the clanbook describes this level of integration, where in 4 days they couldn't even avoid killing 9/10s of their global numbers, then by all means, <i>the clanbook is bulshit</i>. This is logistical suicide for predators.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T21:29:22-07:00","id":1552905,"title":"","content":"How about that? I got a thumbs down for one of my posts that wasn't even offensive to anyone<br /> anyone.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T21:32:40-07:00","id":1552906,"title":"","content":"One thing about the Ravnos suffering final death in such away that I couldn't accept. How would you keep such a thing secret when he fought and rampaged over a week drawing extremely powerful beings and countless collateral damage in the process from the world in general?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 08-05-2025, 12:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T22:55:29-07:00","id":1552909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552906#post1552906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing about the Ravnos suffering final death in such away that I couldn't accept. How would you keep such a thing secret when he fought and rampaged over a week drawing extremely powerful beings and countless collateral damage in the process from the world in general?</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually ppl of the west don't know much about what happens on Bangladesh and specially typhoons during its season, plus, this is the World of Darkness.Things are usually worse than here.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-05T17:22:14-07:00","id":1552936,"title":"","content":"Everything in V5 and most of Revised's metaplot changes too","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-05T20:17:40-07:00","id":1552942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552909#post1552909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Usually ppl of the west don't know much about what happens on Bangladesh and specially typhoons during its season, plus, this is the World of Darkness.Things are usually worse than here.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>By definition the Technocracy shouldn't worry only about people in the West, so even an outcry &quot;limited&quot; to the East would be relevant. More so if you consider that most of humanity is actually there.<br /> <br /> Other than that, there's a lot of posts about this above, already. But in short, it was too big a thing for the &quot;this is WoD&quot; explanation to hold any water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-05T20:57:57-07:00","id":1552944,"title":"","content":"At Saga, suspension of disbelief can only go so far in science fiction or gothic horror genre. How Ravnos suffering final death is a prime example of it as it would be impossible to cover up such a battle and sheer amount of lost lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-06T14:16:02-07:00","id":1552961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552896#post1552896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5, many but the main issue is Oblivion and the Lasombra. If the Lasombra had that since the beginning they had access to everything the Cappadocian and Giovanni had, that would change the entire Cainite history. Their curse would also be pointless since Caine cursing them for a thing that would be an issue millennia into the future is really pointless.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Oblivion is probably the discipline that is the most editorial mandate on it. Its a power which explicitly wouldn't exist either in lore or mechanics unless unique disciplines are banned.<br /> <br /> It kinda strains the internal plausibility of the setting by its existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-06-2025, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-07T00:22:53-07:00","id":1552972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552961#post1552961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oblivion is probably the discipline that is the most editorial mandate on it. Its a power which explicitly wouldn't exist either in lore or mechanics unless unique disciplines are banned.<br /> <br /> It kinda strains the internal plausibility of the setting by its existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree<br /> Obtenebration was something that was defined and refined over decades and actually made sense - and actually explained really well the Clan Flaw<br /> Purely focusing on Vampire - tho this worked with other game lines, like Demon, Werewolf, Mage, etc - the spource of Obtenebration was the Abyss, the Darkness before God decreed &quot;Let there be light,&quot;<br /> The Abyss is the Unmaking, the non-space that was never meant to exist within Creation, but always precedes and surrounds it.<br /> The <b>Abyss Mysticism</b> of Lasombra sorcerers (especially in <i>Dark Ages</i> and <i>V20</i>) explicitly ties Obtenebration to the <b>Darkness before the Light of Creation</b>.<br /> Their power comes from reaching into this darkness \u2014 which <b>precedes reality and God</b> \u2014 and thus their <b>very blood is corrupted by anti-reality</b>.<br /> The clan flaw is thus a <b>sign of metaphysical infection</b>: not a weakness, but a <i>scar of truth</i>. They are not &quot;unseen&quot; because of trickery \u2014 but because they exist in <b>partial contradiction to being</b>.<br /> The Lasombra flaw in <b>pre-V5 editions</b> \u2014 being invisible to mirrors and electronic recording \u2014 has often been brushed off as a &quot;shadowy&quot; gothic flavor but actually they were not seen because they were not really there.<br /> Their reflection isn't absent because of physics. It's absent because <b>reflections require presence</b>, and the Lasombra, being suffused with the <b>primordial, pre-Creation Void</b>, are <b>anti-presence</b>. This puts them closer to the Abyss than to Creation \u2014 closer to the absence of meaning, light and substance<br /> No mater what game line you take the Abyss - the source of Obtenebration - is something primodial or &quot;anti-reality&quot;<br /> Thus the Lasombra clan flaw was the byproduct of this, their connection to Reality was weakened, they were not &quot;real&quot;, their bodies were just an illusion like in the old Vampire legends and that why mirrors and devices did not &quot;saw&quot; them- they were just ideas, the willpower of the Vampire manifest in body that is material, and thanks to his own beliefs and the World concensus (al\u00e1 Mage) they had the vampiric weaknesess, but in truth they became something that simply\u2026 Isn't, thanks to their connection to this primodial Void.<br /> The Lasombra Don\u2019t \u201cExist\u201d \u2014 They Are Imposed Concepts<br /> The Lasombra are sustained not by physics, but by belief \u2014 a belief that is fraying. Hence their reflections fail; hence they appear as gaping holes in photos; hence they must manipulate reality politically, because they are losing the ability to exist metaphysically.<br /> They\u2019re <i>barely real</i> \u2014 and that is why they hunger so fiercely for control. The Abyss hollows them out, and power fills the hole.<br /> <br /> The Xi Dundu, the Laibon offshot of the Lasombra Clan weakness could be explained similarly. The weakness of the Xi Dundu is similar to the Lasombra weakness of casting no reflection; the Xi Dundu cast no shadow of any sort. They also have a secondary clan Flaw thanks to their own meddling - they originally hailed from the Congo until a rite gone wrong forced them from their homelands - they must not be touched by their native soil when they rest else they are greatly weakened; this is perhaps a further reflection of their original banishing; and a curious contrast to the Tzimisce weakness. But focus on the original, the lack of casted Shadow<br /> The Xi Dundu\u2019s lack of a shadow can be viewed as a cultural, metaphysical variation on the Lasombra flaw, rooted in the same Abyssal metaphysics but refracted through a different lens: one of identity, exile, and self-erasure rather than elitism and arrogance.<br /> <b>Reflection</b> is how the world shows <i>you</i> to yourself. The Lasombra have no <b>self-image</b>, no echo in light, because <b>reality rejects their presence</b>. Their connection to the Abyss <i>unravels their metaphysical existence</i>.<br /> <b>Shadow</b>, however, is <b>how you shape the world</b>: it\u2019s <b>your outline cast onto reality</b>. It\u2019s a mark of <b>presence</b>, of <b>interaction with the physical world via light</b>. The Xi Dundu <i>don\u2019t leave a trace</i> \u2014 they exist, but the world <b>doesn\u2019t respond</b>.<br /> Thus:<br /> <b>The Lasombra are unseen by the world; the Xi Dundu are untouched by it.</b><br /> They are <b>barely real</b>, but in a <b>different direction</b> \u2014 not denied self-recognition, but <b>denied impact</b>. No imprint. No echo. No resonance.<br /> <br /> This makes their lack of shadow eerier than the Lasombra\u2019s flaw \u2014 because people notice shadows missing instinctively, and it marks them as outsiders not only to society, but to the very laws of nature.<br /> Their presence doesn\u2019t alter light; light passes around them, touches them \u2014 but doesn\u2019t respond.<br /> In Mage terms, it\u2019s like they are not part of the Pattern enough to register weight or pressure. They <i>aren\u2019t convincing enough</i> to cast consequence.The Lasombra do not reflect because they are no longer seen.<br /> The Xi Dundu do not cast shadows because they no longer <i>impress</i> upon the world.<br /> Both are sustained by Abyssal willpower, not reality.<br /> \u200b\u200bBoth seek domination, control, or ritual mastery \u2014 to assert meaning where none was given.<br /> <br /> The Kiasyd should be a paradox: Born of the Abyss, Yet More &quot;Real&quot;<br /> But actually they are not a flaw in this<br /> The Dreaming is the realm of infinite potential, imagination, archetype, and myth. It is not bound by physical laws, but it is dense with meaning and identity.<br /> The Kiasyd are half-Abyss, half-Dreaming.\u200b<br /> Their Fae blood does something Lasombra blood alone cannot: it <b>anchors them in myth</b>, gives <b>form and narrative</b> to what would otherwise be <i>unstructured negation</i>.\u200b\u200b<br /> The Glamour (Faerie's creative fuel) provides the structure to give shape to the unstructured darkness of the Abyss.<br /> Marconius and his descendants do cast reflections and shadows because, despite their Abyssal origin, they are also made of Dream-stuff, which demands identity. Where the Lasombra are unraveling beings, the Kiasyd are &quot;mythic beings&quot; \u2014 strange, alien, but <i>storied</i>. The world can \u201csee\u201d them because they have <i>narrative weight</i>.\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThis refined and defined <b>peak metaphysical horror</b> in Vampire was thrown out the window\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 08-07-2025, 05:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-07T03:09:06-07:00","id":1552975,"title":"","content":"Well...<br /> <br /> Frankly, Obtenebration was just a symptom of the specialness of the most super special of the vampires, along with Abyss Mysticism, the Abyss, and everything else.<br /> <br /> V5 should have dumped all of this, given the Lasombra Obfuscate (as the writers should have done from day one) and vastly improved the clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-07T06:07:50-07:00","id":1552978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552975#post1552975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well...<br /> <br /> Frankly, Obtenebration was just a symptom of the specialness of the most super special of the vampires, along with Abyss Mysticism, the Abyss, and everything else.<br /> <br /> V5 should have dumped all of this, given the Lasombra Obfuscate (as the writers should have done from day one) and vastly improved the clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>obfuscation is a poor fit for the clan, they're hyper aggressive/domineering and their discipline line reflects that. If you were to change their lineup you'd most likely be better of going for Celerity or Presence if we're losing oblivion.<br /> <br /> Pretty much all clans have cool gimmicks linked with them. So it seems odd to single out the Keepers because they're spooky power had a lot of depth previously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-07-2025, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-07T10:56:48-07:00","id":1552981,"title":"","content":"There are also too many Clans/Bloodlines for the number of Disciplines if you start cutting all the unique ones and want to keep the spreads more unique. It's one of the reasons V5 had to unify the Hecata in order to justify one Discipline for them.<br /> <br /> It's also a bit weird to single out the Lasombra when VtM 1e gave unique Disciplines out like candy in the first place. Gangrel and Tremere both got one in the core book, all the Sabbat and Independent Clans got one, the first Bloodlines introduced all got one.<br /> <br /> There's a bunch of retcons in VtM (Abyssal Mysticism being a thing that always existed rather than a new innovation when it was added to the books for example) that were actually meant to (and had the effect of) reducing how special some of the group-specific Disciplines where. We saw a proliferation of different blood magic traditions to break the Tremere's lock on it. The earlier attempt to make a universal &quot;Clan of the Dead/associated Bloodlines&quot; power by Necromancy being redone to work like Thaumaturgy with each group just having favored paths was also part of this.<br /> <br /> We have obviously not like the totality of the end result, but if you want some place in VtM to point to some clear favoritism towards different groups... there's way better examples (some of which are edition specific, some aren't).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-07T18:59:16-07:00","id":1552996,"title":"","content":"Among Discipline changes, <b>Oblivion</b> was certainly a special case.<br /> <br /> I don't completely agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> because a lot of it is theory instead of canon, which is fine. But I can't say it's just &quot;Special Discipline of Specialness&quot; as it isn't really more special than any other gimmicky unique Discipline around. It's their gimmick, and open to be used as plot point or not like many others.<br /> <br /> But the actual point is that it isn't, by any means, <b>Necromancy</b>. However contrived the conflation of Death powers into <b>Necromancy</b>, it still made far more sense within the fiction than <b>Oblivion</b>, and it kept the Paths still somewhat distinct.<br /> <br /> The problem with <b>Oblivion</b> is that it conflates powers that have few-to-no thematic coherence, and irreconcilable metaphysical roles. Their narrative niches barely touch each other except by the very controversial one of &quot;scary power&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not my worse nitpick with V5 by far, I wouldn't particularly say I hate it, but there were better avenues to deal with this. In fact, conflating <b>Necromancy</b> within <b>Thaumaturgy</b> would have been a far better (if not really &quot;good&quot;) choice, and let <b>Obtenebration</b> be either its own thing, or a Trademarked suit of Alternate Powers to other Disciplines, like <b>Potence</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-08T01:03:32-07:00","id":1553005,"title":"","content":"I dont think the no unique discipline mandate works full stop because it provides no actual benifits to the game and actually works against how v5 wants to treat the clans.<br /> <br /> But i think Oblivion is probably one of the worst offenders since it feels almost gamey as the spooky power range, im struggling to find the words but it feels more like a game in setting when you use it. In lore its nonsensical and thematically the two powers types have no thematic glue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-08T02:12:07-07:00","id":1553006,"title":"","content":"To redirect back a bit to the thread's starting topic... one of the ongoing issues that no edition of VtM has ever really solved in a fashion that seems to suit most styles of play is how much the Disciplines represent something &quot;real&quot; in-universe or are abstractions. While some of the WoD games (ex: WtA) are very clear that such powers are in-universe elements that your characters can discuss and think about conceptually, and others are very unclear about it (ex: Mage), VtM has always kinda insisted on some balancing point between Disciplines being something vampires actually know about and can study and teach, and something more abstract.<br /> <br /> Obviously the real driver on this is that VtM drew from inspirations where vampires had specific powers, but they were vaguely defined and frequently never really named (Anne Rice's vampires with their dark gifts also set a precedent for the idea of vampires having unique powers that seemed to inform VtM's proliferation of Disciplines and the way Elder Disciplines were handled). So VtM vampires are supposed to know that there is a vampire way of mind controlling people, that is commonly called Dominate, but despite it existing mechanically in a defined predictable cluster of powers, the games never want you to say, &quot;I use the fourth power in the Discipline of Dominate,&quot; in-character.<br /> <br /> This tension has always made addressing some of the issues (if we could even all agree specifically what those are) more difficult than it needs to be otherwise, because there is some level of in-universe knowledge of the Disciplines that means you can't just make major changes to them as you could if they were purely meta-mechanics that weren't predictable enough to be classified and known by the characters.<br /> <br /> Just like how Oblivion in V5 causes issues in the lore because Disciplines are at least partially &quot;real&quot; concepts to vampires still, we saw similar issues with things like the Dominate vs. Dementation Malkavian lore weirdness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-08T03:44:26-07:00","id":1553007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553006#post1553006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So VtM vampires are supposed to know that there is a vampire way of mind controlling people, that is commonly called Dominate, but despite it existing mechanically in a defined predictable cluster of powers, the games never want you to say, &quot;I use the fourth power in the Discipline of Dominate,&quot; in-character.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true<br /> But I think this boils down to the RP part, like how a Sire teches his Child to Disciplines, for Dominate for example:<br /> <br /> &quot;My Child, as I am superior to you, you as a Cainite is superior to the Herd.<br /> We were made to lead<br /> Our kind are shepperds and rulers, the Word is ours and the Humans - and even those who are farther from the Dark Father than us - are our subjects<br /> By your Will they think or act according to your decree<br /> Like how a predator stares down a lowly prey, how a a King looks down on a peasant, your galre is the key to exert authority<br /> The eye is a window into the soul and staring in their naked, weak, pathetic soul give your Voice power!<br /> Don't worry my child, as you get older, more powerfull you Will not need such aid<br /> But now you do<br /> Like how you command a well trained dog or subject, your Word is Law. Your decree must be obeyed<br /> Give a simple one-word order and they must obey.<br /> They have to<br /> And just as they have obey one World, they have to obey your comand<br /> You give them a command and that Will affect their deeds, as it should be, from simple, precise directives to complex, highly involved ones your planted Command bend their very weak mind and soul to Obey and do what you ordered<br /> As just easly you can command to Obey, you can command them to Forget\u2026 or to what to remember.<br /> History is written by the Victors and whats happened in their past, what they remember is not different.<br /> By now my Child you see, our Mind is a powerfull weapon, our Will is absolute! It is absolute to such a degree you can shape and bend your subjects to obey you and only You; fill their heads with subtle whispers and veiled urges, thereby ensuring these mortals\u2019 loyalty\u2026 this way lose much of their passion and individuality but that is a small price to pay to have obedient subjects who are hard to manipulate by your enemies.<br /> And finally, when you mastered the art of the dominating commands your mind can utterly supplant the mind of a mortal subject, move your very consciousness into their bodies!&quot;<br /> <br /> But Vampire never really &quot;formalized&quot; how these powers are actually &quot;called&quot; or <i>used</i> in the world (tho' in Dark Ages they have fancy names, like &quot;Command&quot; is &quot;Observance of the Spoken Word&quot;)<br /> Tho' this gave a realitve freedom to sape and mold your playstlye<br /> Nontheless I am a creature of habit, and like rules and defined things, so it is a curse and blessing in my eyes and indeed never realyl liked this lack of &quot;lore&quot;<br /> ...like how in theory Vampires find lineage important yet the lore not really support this and you can find a precious little complete family trees up to Caine dow nto the 16th generation<br /> Of course you always can make up Vampires and fil lthe gaps, but to be a member of a &quot;canon&quot; line gives you that warm fuzzy feeling your character is <i>really</i> part of that World<br /> <br /> For example, you want to be an 8th generation Tzimisce from Yorak's line ,your tree is:<br /> <br /> <b>Caine</b><br /> I<br /> <b>Irad </b><i>and</i> <b>Enoch</b> (see below)<br /> I<br /> <b>The Eldest</b> (The Legend of Irad has it that, at some point in the city of Enoch, Irad the Strong sought to purge himself of all evil. Using his mastery of Protean, the ancient gathered all of his evil into a bilious mass of repugnancy and horror, and spat it out. Irad's intention was to destroy the mortal who consumed this mass of Protean, thinking that by destroying this mortal, he would destroy the evil also. But to Irad's surprise, this mortal appeared normal. Irad brought the mortal to his brother attention, who - out of Curiousity - Embraced the mortal to see what the outcome would be.<br /> According to texts in the Library of the Forgotten, Ynosh the Lawgiver was attracted to the insights of the man that he would Embrace<br /> Thus, the world was given the Tzimisce Antediluvian, whos sire is both Enoch and Irad in a sense)<br /> I<br /> <b>Yorak</b>, Voivode among Voivodes, High Priest of Clan Tzimisce, Master (or Mistress depending of Yorak's mood) of the Cathedral of Flesh (4th Generation)<br /> I<br /> <b>Kosczecsyku</b> (5th Generation) (Faked his death in 983 CE. Mighty Koldun. Even in modern nights he is the proud owner of a vozhd.) [Transylvania by Night, WTA: Rage: Warriors of the Apocalypse, Rites of the Blood]<br /> I<br /> <b>Count Vladimir Rustovich</b>, Voivode among Voivodes (6th Generation) [Transylvania by Night, WTA: Rage: Warriors of the Apocalypse]<br /> I<br /> <b>Kara Vlaszy Lupescu</b>, Fiendish Knight (7th Generation) During the Anarch Revolt, Kara joined the Sabbat alongside her sire. An unspecified amount of time later, however, she was killed by Lupines in the woods of Wallachia. [Under the Black Cross]<br /> I<br /> And Y<b>ou</b>, the 8th Generation Child of Kara<br /> \u200b<br /> Feels... a bit different isn't it?<br /> <br /> Maybe it is just me, but I always was fond of vampiric geneology and the lore supposedly should support it... yet it not really, not always","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-08T04:47:21-07:00","id":1553008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553005#post1553005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont think the no unique discipline mandate works full stop because it provides no actual benifits to the game and actually works against how v5 wants to treat the clans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's a big deal, actually, it's just another take on the rules.<br /> <br /> Whatever it means for the clans, it's easily covered within the fiction with the powers being gated behind clans and factions, even if that isn't enforced by rules. And that's the other point: this is strictly a mechanical change, not a lore one exactly.<br /> <br /> Sure, the specific execution of the idea isn't always the best, and how they let the lore be affected in official products is possibly a problem (I don't know, I don't read a lot of them), but by itself the new take on Disciplines is ok on my book, <b>Oblivion</b> not-withstanding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553006#post1553006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">one of the ongoing issues that no edition of VtM has ever really solved in a fashion that seems to suit most styles of play is how much the Disciplines represent something &quot;real&quot; in-universe or are abstractions.</div> </div> </div> </div>My own take was always that they were mostly &quot;real&quot;. From their descriptions to their names, and the flourish in the names of the specific powers, it does seem to me that Vampires think of them as distinct and classified sets of powers, and do think of them as having an expected progression, at least until level 5.<br /> <br /> On most Disciplines, the difference between levels isn't either intensity nor general understanding of principles, but the full development of an ability that wasn't previously there, each level doing something other levels just don't. There are exceptions, but this general trend remains even within V5's framework. So while the development of a new level may occur gradually within the fiction, the perception of such powers as distinct developments within the framework of a Discipline seems the most intuitive take.<br /> <br /> Physical Disciplines are an obvious exception, where they probably are seen as a single power that can be improved in a continuum that wouldn't be equated to levels, even if mechanically they have them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-08T12:39:10-07:00","id":1553013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553007#post1553007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feels... a bit different isn't it?<br /> <br /> Maybe it is just me, but I always was fond of vampiric geneology and the lore supposedly should support it... yet it not really, not always</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is this is a very high investment sort of fun.<br /> <br /> If you're a completely new to VtM player, who's just read the core book of whatever edition your group is playing, this approach means nothing. It's a bunch of names - most of which are canon NPCs your ST is never going to use - and have no meaning because your Generation and additional traits like Prestigious Sire or Mentor are going to matter far more than a genealogy will.<br /> <br /> If you're really deep into the lore of the game? Yeah, these sorts of things can be fun. It's also a cool way to help show off the differences in Clan culture by showing which Clans think your lineage is really important, which Clans do it because they have to put up with the first group, and which Clans don't really care about it on various levels.<br /> <br /> Though, that said, I have found WtA to do better at getting people into this than VtM because you don't get the ramp up in power as you go back, and your ancient ancestors are all dead anyway. There's a lot more freedom to come up with custom ancestors to suit your PC and the tone of the group, and since the Garou can actually summon ancestor spirits (well, this is a VtM thread so I'm going to not get into the W5 issues) it matters more than just the more traditionalist and formality valuing Tribes having a social value to reciting their genealogies. Being able to say, &quot;Hey, my great-great-great-great-grandma fought something that sounds awful familiar to this, lets see if the Theurges can get her advice,&quot; makes it rewarding to have those details. It makes the sting of not having ancestor-spirits readily accessible to your Tribe a lot more real when it means you have to summon up other people's ancestors and try to butter them up for the indignation of being asked to talk to someone that isn't part of their family.<br /> <br /> <br /> Requiem clearly wanted to replicate this to make genealogy more relevant to its vampires. While Requiem's setup does make deep genealogies somewhat shallow in meaning even for very dedicated players, Requiem does have a lot of ways to benefit in-game by detailing at least your sire and grandsire. By getting rid of Generation and one original vampire, Requiem also lets you have genealogical depth vary in at least social importance. You never get stuck on &quot;well, we're now automatically in the heavy hitters of the 4th Gen, and then the mythological dangers of the 3rd and 2nd Gens, and then Caine after that.&quot; You can have a game where running into a vampire that's 10 generations back from you doesn't have to mean an epic world shaking badass (it can if you want that, it just doesn't have to be). Requiem's approach clearly can't satisfy everyone - as nothing can - but IME it gives more reason to engage with vampire genealogy that will really come up in game compared to VtM which has lots of interesting canon NPCs you could descend from but most games that'll never really matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-09T02:58:31-07:00","id":1553021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553013#post1553013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is this is a very high investment sort of fun.<br /> <br /> If you're a completely new to VtM player, who's just read the core book of whatever edition your group is playing, this approach means nothing..</div> </div> </div> </div>In a sense, yes<br /> On the other? After a session or two you are not completely new and even new players face this problem from a certain point of view in the form of the Tremere who have a ritual to determine lineage, Ventrue who are built on lineage, the Traditions, that requires intorduction, and the aforementioned Flaws and Merits you mentioned about mentor and sire<br /> And the whole boons and favors-system<br /> The whole Jyhad<br /> The Vampire society is based on lineage, Sires, the enmity or alliances between those sires up to the top - and most of the time the central of the stories one way or another are rooted in them (regardless if you picked up or not any of those flaws, personal horror aside the coteries have their &quot;missions&quot; or things they investigate and rarely if ever they do those things out of their own free will) <br /> And it is completely fine not care about these things as a character or as a player - tho' after a few games you are hardly a newbie and your characters quickly learn even in an Anarch or a Sabbat game, not to mention a Camarilla, you can really entangle in this web<br /> And while there is wisdom in ignorance and safety in silence I think most of the fledgelings/Ancillae learn to... learn and be preapared.<br /> Like as you said in Werewolf it is part of the life<br /> But it is in my humble oppinion is part ot the vampires unlife too (or should/could be)<br /> <br /> My problem is not the opinion, everyone is free to ignore or add after all whatever they like to their game, but the fact, fundamentally the Game is built around this mechanic and lore wise (take the Infamous Sire Flaw, Rival Sires, Clan Enmity or simply <b>Black Sheep (5-pt. Flaw) </b>that starts with &quot;You belong to a prestigious lineage that is considered to be paragon of another sect&quot;) <i>yet it is not really supported to the point it barely scratches the surface</i><br /> <br /> Sure it not essential, just personally this part of the lore was always a bit anoying for me, because the game have its own extended universe, video games, card game, comics, books and even if you just read the core book and clan book, player guide mayhaps, you encounter these names, the clans important figures, the cities important figureas and their complicated web of interractions and connections and unavoidably, their destiny - and your character in one way or another a part of this<br /> And literally would have been nothing to write a name in those bios insted sire: &quot;unknown&quot; <br /> Or give you a little help if you after having Disgrace to the Blood (3pt. Flaw) - Your sire regards the fact that he Embraced you to be a titanic mistake and/or Sire\u2019s Resentment (1pt. Flaw) - Your sire dislikes you and wishes you ill decide you not lie on your back, but do you homework, deals, boons, favors to research your Sire maybe she is like that because she was in the same situtation and maybe worth the risk to seek out your Grandsire - my enemy's enemy-style <br /> Would helped greatly the STs and players work to have this frame that in theroy everything built up and the whole reason catalist of the Jyhad<br /> <br /> Again, not essential and the game is fine and neat without it - but I always believed it would have been better if we would had that lore","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-09T04:34:50-07:00","id":1553022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553008#post1553008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it's a big deal, actually, it's just another take on the rules.<br /> <br /> Whatever it means for the clans, it's easily covered within the fiction with the powers being gated behind clans and factions, even if that isn't enforced by rules. And that's the other point: this is strictly a mechanical change, not a lore one exactly.<br /> <br /> Sure, the specific execution of the idea isn't always the best, and how they let the lore be affected in official products is possibly a problem (I don't know, I don't read a lot of them), but by itself the new take on Disciplines is ok on my book, <b>Oblivion</b> not-withstanding.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh kinda? Nothing 5th ed does individually is a big deal but it's a death of a thousand cuts and this is one of those cuts. It's ultimately a low level negative change because it's a complete waste of time and mildly pushes against some of 5th editions (perceived) writing intents because it's an arbitrarily editorial mandate rather than an organic game design decision. It's not a deal killer which is why I didnt comment on it initially but it is a rock in my shoe when I'm a running the game.<br /> <br /> This stretches credibility in terms of lore, you can see in previous editions writing that the clan disciplines are distinct ability and you cannot do common discipline powers with them, it's something of a plot point on occasion. Most dramatically with the Ravnos and tzmisce whose powers work very differently both mechanically and lore wise in very dramatic ways. It's like If Gaelic and Welsh suddenly became one language in reality.<br /> <br /> It's pretty pointless, provides no actual benefits outside of if you're really into modular powers and is ultimately a low key negative. Oblivion is the worst offender but I can't really think of anything positive to say about any of the others. If anything it feels weird the Ministry have protean rather than either oblivion, Blood sorcery or auspex for example. Like you said not a big deal but ultimately a diet coke when I wanted full fat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-09-2025, 07:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-09T09:27:08-07:00","id":1553027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552972#post1552972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Obtenebration was something that was defined and refined... \u200b\u200b\u200bThis refined and defined <b>peak metaphysical horror</b> in Vampire was thrown out the window\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Xi Dundu and Kyasid are absent from V5, like most bloodlines, but otherwise none of this is disputed. The differences is its world of the dead is at the near edge of the Abyss and shares some sort of metaphysical property with former.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-09T12:22:15-07:00","id":1553031,"title":"","content":"Creating lineages can be fun, but in our games it didn't make much of impact unless needed and it hasn't happened yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-09T12:43:49-07:00","id":1553032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553021#post1553021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, not essential and the game is fine and neat without it - but I always believed it would have been better if we would had that lore</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem isn't the playstyle, but the need to attach it to lore.<br /> <br /> A list of names such as that wouldn't be a small thing to do, to begin with. You have to cover several Generations, for several Clans, splitting Lineages within those clans, spread them across cities, or at least regions. This is a lot of work. And the end result of this work isn't freedom, but restriction, because your list doesn't necessarily fit the needs of the people who'll actually make stories with it, be them writers working on a novel or sourcebook, STs making their cities, or even players making their characters, not to say the extra work those people must put into learning those lists.<br /> <br /> It's why <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said Requiem's setup works better to do this. On top of 2nd edition rules for lineage sympathy, the fact is that with a system where there's far less need to link your lineage back to a host of important NPCs, it becomes actually easier to make up your own lineage from scratch, dating back as far as you want, tracing it to known NPCs only if it serves you in any way.<br /> <br /> While it's true that the game was partially built with the idea of tracking lineages being a very important thing, and that doing so may improve the game experience, making out lists upon lists of such lineages won't really solve the problem, it will make for lineages that don't feel organic and puts pressure without reward for most participants.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T13:33:03-07:00","id":1553302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552742#post1552742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As you pointed out the Week if Nightmares, this one was one of its major problems... Zapathasura rampaged across India to Bangladesh for two days... then on the third day was attacked by three of the eldest Kuei-jin Bodhisattvas, the Devil-Tiger Eight Thunders Sage, the Thrashing Dragon Black Earth Boy and the Resplendent Crane Rising Majestically to the Western Sun, powerhouses on their own right<br /> Since Baba Yaga and her Armies casually swept away Spets and anything that stood in Her way the world not really seen such display of power... but Bangladesh was and is - and no offense to russia and where Baba Yaga rose and ruled - is the eighth-most populous country in the world and among the most densely populated with a population of over 171 million within an area of 148,460 square kilometres... the death toll was above the charts and after that others joined the fray - swath of territory stretching from Calcutta to Dhaka was almost entirely depopulated.<br /> From storyteller point of view the Week of Nightmares was a logistical nightmare say the least and you had to be pretty clever to explain how on earth this not broke the Masquarade to pieces and more importantly what happened to the locals? And those who played there...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You know what is funny? Until you started discussing it alongside other examples of lore/setting changes across editions, i never quite realized how <b><i>absolutely </i></b>i rejected the Week of Nightmares. I just, simply blocked any reference whatsoever to the idea without even realizing it.<br /> <br /> The event itself is a morass of over-the-top silliness, supposed to jumpstart a setting change i'm not a fan of, while hinging on lore-setting conceits i had rejected since the Ravnos clanbook and KotE came to be. So it was simply, something that never happened and was never discussed, because it had no reason to be.<br /> <br /> It's kind of curious in hindsight when contrasted with my own relation to the Wan Kuei, that started from vitriolic distaste with much of the lore and portrayal but eventually went to just retooling it all into a different kindred society, with different dynamics (the massive majority of wan kuei/gui ren/etc being something between Caitiff, &quot;ascended&quot; thin-bloods and other peculiar beings instead of embraced childer of clans or bloodlines), common regional myths and so on.<br /> <br /> I never felt anything about it. Just absentmindedly buried it, covered with a rug, forgot and went on as if nothing happened, only now realizing i even did that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-20-2025, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T13:49:36-07:00","id":1553304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552683#post1552683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">KotEK's &quot;we're the same kinda vampire, but also just a bit different,&quot; wasn't an improvement in helping make setting games in Africa easier, or handling clashes between African vampires and vampires from other places as imperialism and colonialism have faded only to be replaced by globalization. I appreciate the intent to show that vampires can have a completely functional non-Noddist mythology, it's so late in the game for such a big push to finally explore the topic in depth that too many people just react to the African myths as wrong instead of different because different wasn't represented well enough in the older books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of this is the fact that a large chunk of the audience was expecting Africa to be the place where they explored anyone other than the Followers of Set to believe in non-Noddism. The problem being that the majority of Africa is Muslim and it has a Christian branch older than the European Catholic Church or at least comparable. It's the kind of place where you could conceivably have Noddism having originated but they just sort of shuffle that off to the Middle East,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552754#post1552754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Almost 1,5 million people died in total in accordance with the official lore, most from the astounding colateral damage of the many battles raging there (Zapathasura plus a bunch of Ravnos plus a lot of stranded spirits, vs everyone else), but 110.000+ from the floods and 60.000+ from the nukes.<br /> <br /> This is more than the annual deaths in the entire country for most of the last century. In fact, unless no one else died that year, it's enough to make 1999 almost as lethal as 1971, the year of the Bangladeshi Liberation War, which was one of the biggest mass deaths events after WWII, and more lethal than the entire year of 1970, when Bangladesh was hit by the Bhola Cyclone, the most lethal storm of its history (the Bhola killed at most half a million people).</div> </div> </div> </div>For comparison, a million died during Covid in America.<br /> <br /> But yes, I agree with everyone else here that this was at the end of the line with the assumption that the apocalypse was happening so the universe didn't have to continue on much longer afterward. It's only when the line is revived that it becomes an uncomfortable statement that one of the biggest disasters of all time in terms of lives lost is sort of glossed over.<br /> <br /> To a lesser extent, the Week of Nightmares pisses me off for a couple of other reasons. The event being resolved by the Technocracy pretty much validates them as the only people actually able to fight and protect humankind in the larger World of Darkness. It's like having an alien invasion and then having the Nazis fight them off (which John Ringo actually wrote a book about, I shitzu you not). It contributed heavily, IMHO, to the belief in the &quot;clean Technocracy&quot; of Revised.<br /> <br /> Second, the Ravnos had already undergone a massive rewrite to try to make them more than stereotypes and help deal with the overall whiteness of V:TM's clans, Making the South Asian clan into the disposable one wasn't a good look even if they were the ones chosen BECAUSE of their unfortunate history.<br /> <br /> But another thing that was annoying is the Ravnos, &quot;Let's go punch Godzilla&quot; ending for the thing is the fact that it also changed the scope of the game much the same way the Clan Novels did with the Sabbat taking the East Coast. Lasombra and Tzimisce illustrate the antediluvians as subtle, careful, and manipulative beings that you can't just 'nuke.' Ravnos acts like a kaiju fighting superheroes and not with the genius of a millennia old monster. Later retcons are stating that he was a antediluvian that had succumbed to wightdom but....doesn't that make him LESS frightening?<br /> <br /> Some other retcons I'm not fond of:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Ur-Shulgi</b>: What I hate about him is primarily the fact that he's an anchor on the line. Okay, there's a 10,000 year old vampire that is destroying the Assamites. So...what do the PLAYERS do about him? Like Divis Mal, the game is set up so they're irrelevant to him. I follow the Exalted line of thinking, &quot;If the PCs can't be involved in the plot in a central way, don't do it.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2. <b>The Sabbat</b>: I don't mind the Sabbat collapsing into another Civil War. In fact, I'd argue that was inevitable. The Sabbat has ALWAYS been depicted as a dysfunctional mass of assholes at each other's throats. It's just having them abandon their cities and disappear makes less sense than just saying they lost a war. The thing is about the Sabbat is Paradox's White Wolf seemed to have an irrational hatred of them. They serve a valuable game function as cheap heat, though.<br /> &quot;A Sabbat is doing something evil in your city&quot; is one of the easiest adventure hooks.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Rocks Fall Plots</b>: The Tremere Antitribu massacre is one of the worst changes for no good reason that I can think of. Why would you do this? The same for the Ravnos to an extent but at least they left the door open for future ones. The same for the Black Hand who get destroyed by GHOST NUKES and somehow this is LESS silly than the cult of Antediluvian worshipers.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Lucita joins the Sabbat</b>: I dunno, I just really liked the character and felt it was an awful end to her story.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>Killing Jan Pieterzsoon</b>: Okay, I know EXACTLY why they did this. I just wish had it received more fanfare.<br /> <br /> 6. <b>The Gangrel and Brujah leaving the Camarilla: </b>It makes no sense in-universe as I'd argue they aren't organized enough to do so. Same for the Brujah. By contrast, I really liked the Lasombra leaving the Sabbat or at least joining the Camarilla because I felt that centered the PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-20-2025, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T20:43:49-07:00","id":1553314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553304#post1553304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of this is the fact that a large chunk of the audience was expecting Africa to be the place where they explored anyone other than the Followers of Set to believe in non-Noddism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is the problem even if it were true. It's just as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said, what held KotEK from being accepted wasn't so much if it was sensible with the source material (which it was more than KotE, as low a bar as it was), but that by that time the game was way past the point where it should have introduced a serious and well developed non-Noddist society. It's less if this made sense in Africa and more that it wouldn't have a hold with most players.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553304#post1553304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem being that the majority of Africa is Muslim and it has a Christian branch older than the European Catholic Church or at least comparable. It's the kind of place where you could conceivably have Noddism having originated but they just sort of shuffle that off to the Middle East,</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not actually true.<br /> <br /> While Islam came to Africa in the 7th century (not as early as Christianity in Europe, if still early), it's only strong in North Africa and a bit in its East Coast, which is not KotEK's focus point. Eritrea and Ethiopia have a strong and ancient Christian presence that persists today, as do a few enclaves in the north (which was dominated by early Christianity before Islamic conquest), but for most of Africa's history they weren't sizable in comparison with the continent at large. Semitic peoples, mostly Hebrew, did exist elsewhere in Africa possibly since a long time ago, like the Beta Israeli, Lemba and Yibir, but they were completely isolated from the Near East and the Mediterranean world until very recently.<br /> <br /> Even considering those parts, most of Africa was still on indigenous religions up to the end of the 19th century, and only started to convert in bulk to Christianity during the 20th century. And they did surpass Islam in the continent in general, so Muslims are not a majority outside their own countries in northern Africa. In the end we have a small Semitic presence consigned to Egypt or cut from the rest, then Christianity arriving in the 1st Century, Islam in the 7th century, but all of those only taking any hold in sub-saharan Africa in the 20th century, fairly recent for vampires.<br /> <br /> Add to that the fact that our ides of the African continent as a geographic category is fairly recent, and again isn't the focus of KotEK. North Africa had some contact with the south, sure, but it was far more linked to the Mediterranean for most of history. Egypt and Sudan (Nubia) had more contact with the Near East than with anyone else up until Macedonian arrival integrated them even more with the larger Mediterranean community. Even when smaller, the Sahara was a far more daunting barrier than the sea, so north and sub-saharan Africa are quite different areas even today. Talking about North Africa as more related to Africa at large than the Middle East and Europe doesn't really work.<br /> <br /> In this context, Noddism is thoroughly rooted in the Middle East. Only developments pertaining to early Christianity would have any big chance at happening in North Africa and even then that was a world away from sub-saharan Africa. North Africa, especially Egypt, was already plenty covered in other books as far as covering foreign regions goes for White Wolf. KotEK focused on an area that really had no reason to have a strong Noddist presence until very recently, and even then mostly through colonists and Neonates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553304#post1553304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's only when the line is revived that it becomes an uncomfortable statement that one of the biggest disasters of all time in terms of lives lost is sort of glossed over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, I still think it was uncomfortable right at the time. It's certainly worse now, but even at the time.<br /> <br /> The problem is that even if it was the beginning of the end, it was just the beginning. Precisely because it was meant to be this kickstart to a huge thing, it could have went full on &quot;WTH just happened&quot; and stay as a wound in the Masquerade without messing things up too much, but the setting still had to exist for quite some more years with this weird &quot;huge thing that never happened&quot; hanging in the background.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553304#post1553304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The event being resolved by the Technocracy pretty much validates them as the only people actually able to fight and protect humankind in the larger World of Darkness. It's like having an alien invasion and then having the Nazis fight them off (which John Ringo actually wrote a book about, I shitzu you not). It contributed heavily, IMHO, to the belief in the &quot;clean Technocracy&quot; of Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hated this more back then, although I have to agree that it's a sore point, if for other reasons. I think it leaves a bad taste to have a single faction be so important in an event that will be present to some extent in every single gameline, so even in games where the Union shouldn't be that big of a deal.<br /> <br /> That said, a lot of it is you being physically incapable of accepting that the Technocracy wasn't &quot;cleaned&quot; to say imperialist fascists are good, but to admit they were not a good stand-in (or explanation) for imperialist fascists to begin with. Dude, not cleaning the Technocracy was the same as saying that good science and competent healthcare are fascist things and should be avoided for pseudoscience and anti-vax ideas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553304#post1553304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making the South Asian clan into the disposable one wasn't a good look</div> </div> </div> </div>That was really a terrible idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553304#post1553304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Later retcons are stating that he was a antediluvian that had succumbed to wightdom but....doesn't that make him LESS frightening?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually that wasn't a late retcon, I remember that being stated, or at least considered the most likely explanation, in ToTB itself.<br /> <br /> The problem here is that the Antes as master manipulators don't really mesh with the whole idea of Gehenna. If they're subtly pushing strings from the shadows, that's about every night vampire society, not the End Times When Everyone Dies. That much was pretty clear since 1st edition, Gehenna isn't a legend about the ancients controlling things from the shadow, it's about the night when subtlety will be thrown through the window.<br /> <br /> Now, does this makes for a less frightening experience? Well, in a sense that was precisely the point: this huge destruction is the work of <i>a loser</i>. Imagine what the others will do. Compound this with the state of affairs after the 6th Maelstrom, and even if every Ante woke up as a Wight, the supernatural world wouldn't have the resources to fight them all, not even close.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553304#post1553304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the game is set up so they're irrelevant to him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worse, he's equally irrelevant to them. He may be at most a point in the background of a Banu Haqim character, but otherwise no one cares.<br /> <br /> But you're right. All the problems aside, <i>Lair of the Hidden</i> was good in the sense that it lets the PCs have meaningful interactions with and relevance for its many Methuselah (and one Ante). It shows that you don't even need to give PCs a &quot;fighting chance&quot; to have a good story with the most powerful characters in the setting, you just need those characters to care about something other than being brutes.<br /> <br /> Something that Ur-Shulgi ultimately doesn't have. His motivations aside, the end result is that if it isn't a show of brute force, he doesn't care.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553304#post1553304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is about the Sabbat is Paradox's White Wolf seemed to have an irrational hatred of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting aside that this wasn't an uncommon thing among the fanbase, yeah, that pretty much sums it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553304#post1553304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Rocks Fall Plots</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Thoroughly agree, and I have to add that the silliness doesn't matter. All of those, plus the Vienna Chantry bombings, are sore points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553304#post1553304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Lucita joins the Sabbat</b>\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Not many Lucita fans liked it. It made little sense for her story, it made little sense at all, and it didn't even added much to the Sabbat end of things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553304#post1553304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Gangrel and Brujah leaving the Camarilla</b>\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It didn't made any sense at all, except as a means to create less gimmicky &quot;neutral&quot; factions, but then you didn't really need to remove an entire clan from a sect to have a neutral faction of said clan.<br /> <br /> But I do think the same for the <b>Lasombra</b>. Not because they're not a good addition in the Camarilla, but precisely because there was no need for them to leave the Sabbat to do that. <b>Lasombra-Antitribu</b> were already a thing, and making it harder for the Sabbat faction to persecute them would be more than enough to justify a surge in their Cam numbers without removing their bulk from the Sabbat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T21:14:47-07:00","id":1553316,"title":"","content":"<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> <br /> <br /> I've long held on this and other forums that the reason the Technocracy argument exists is because it's the faction that has suffered the most lore drift, the Get of Fenris and Garou may be the other ones, but unlike the Garou changes, each version has its own fanbase. So there's no wrong answer really and attempts to align the various versions fail because it's really a case of black and white with no ability for there to be a gray.<br /> <br /> It really boils down to what you think the most important part of the Technocracy is:<br /> <br /> 1. Are they the kind of faction who sees nothing wrong with the use of pogrom and have the explicit goals of genocide.<br /> 2. Are they the people who want free health care for everyone and universal education.<br /> <br /> Because I don't believe 1 and 2 go together. I also don't think arguing about it works even Doyle-istically. Because the audiences are talking about literally entirely different versions of the organization that might as well be comparing Superman to Ultraman.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually that wasn't a late retcon, I remember that being stated, or at least considered the most likely explanation, in ToTB itself.<br /> <br /> The problem here is that the Antes as master manipulators don't really mesh with the whole idea of Gehenna. If they're subtly pushing strings from the shadows, that's about every night vampire society, not the End Times When Everyone Dies. That much was pretty clear since 1st edition, Gehenna isn't a legend about the ancients controlling things from the shadow, it's about the night when subtlety will be thrown through the window.<br /> <br /> Now, does this makes for a less frightening experience? Well, in a sense that was precisely the point: this huge destruction is the work of <i>a loser</i>. Imagine what the others will do. Compound this with the state of affairs after the 6th Maelstrom, and even if every Ante woke up as a Wight, the supernatural world wouldn't have the resources to fight them all, not even close. </div> </div> </div>I think as early as 1st Edition, I was always interested in the idea of the Cyclical Gehenna that only got brought up by OPP in Beckett's Jyhad Diary. Basically, that the Antediluvians would wake up once every 1000 years or so, devour a bunch of their childer's childer and then embrace a whole new bunch of 4th generations. Which we know they've done plenty of times. Of course, part of the issue is that Gehenna seems to be based on Akasha from QUEEN OF THE DAMNED and she only woke up once.<br /> <br /> Basically, the game doesn't seem to have done enough to establish THIS TIME will be different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Worse, he's equally irrelevant to them. He may be at most a point in the background of a Banu Haqim character, but otherwise no one cares. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's why I liked the idea of the US bombing him thanks to Ventrue manipulators. Mind you, I would have used an existing faction of Hunters for the death of Ravnos. It didn't have to be the Technocracy or US (because US centrism is terrible) but should have been humanity if they wanted to illustrate how mankind has become a threat to the undead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But you're right. All the problems aside, <i>Lair of the Hidden</i> was good in the sense that it lets the PCs have meaningful interactions with and relevance for its many Methuselah (and one Ante). It shows that you don't even need to give PCs a &quot;fighting chance&quot; to have a good story with the most powerful characters in the setting, you just need those characters to care about something other than being brutes. </div> </div> </div>Agreed, at some point, they remembered that V:TM is best when you TALK to your enemies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Something that Ur-Shulgi ultimately doesn't have. His motivations aside, the end result is that if it isn't a show of brute force, he doesn't care.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>His motive is also pretty esoteric for the majority of people, &quot;Convert or die.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I do think the same for the <b>Lasombra</b>. Not because they're not a good addition in the Camarilla, but precisely because there was no need for them to leave the Sabbat to do that. <b>Lasombra-Antitribu</b> were already a thing, and making it harder for the Sabbat faction to persecute them would be more than enough to justify a surge in their Cam numbers without removing their bulk from the Sabbat.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Before the actual supplement came out, I actually had my home game in 5th Edition with the numbers of vampires in the world remembered. Basically, that there's only about 2000 vampires of each clan in the world anyway. It didn't take that much to turn the Lasomba Antis from a Bloodline into a full clan in terms of defections and Embraces or the deaths of Sabbat.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat being weakened in the setting because of the Second Inquisition given their....habits...would have made a far more understandable situation.<br /> <br /> Mind you, the Second Inquisition is an idea I both like and hate as a retcon. To me, it's War on Terror critique....a decade or more too late.<br /> <br /> It's also kind of objectively terrible for a game called Vampire: The Masquerade. Unless they have a REASON not to blow the whistle on everything...why don't they?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T11:39:13-07:00","id":1553331,"title":"","content":"I know many people hated the addition of having Uri Shugi into the lore and has no real personality and was meant to be a disposable character in a game setting that was ending. Now that the game is back and he is still around and serves no purpose at all <br /> <br /> I personally would replace him with Issm Ur Baal as the clan threat and caused the fracturing of Banu Haqium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T12:49:52-07:00","id":1553339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553316#post1553316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there's no wrong answer really and attempts to align the various versions fail because it's really a case of black and white with no ability for there to be a gray.</div> </div> </div> </div>So there's no wrong answer, except there is a wrong answer, because while the faction was made to be both things at once, it can't be both things at once and it has to be nazis.<br /> <br /> I don't think here's the place to argue that further, nor do I think you're objectively wrong in your opinion about the Technocracy. I just think you demonstrates exactly what I said, but this isn't a problem <i>per se</i>.<br /> <br /> A real problem would be if anyone here were <i>really</i> trying to use the Union as an argument to defend fascism. No one should defend fascism, and I don't think this should be a right, so lets keep it at that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553316#post1553316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think as early as 1st Edition, I was always interested in the idea of the Cyclical Gehenna</div> </div> </div> </div>But that changes nothing in the end.<br /> <br /> Cyclical or not, Gehenna is an apocalyptic event, it's about cataclysmic portents announcing the rise of powerful dead gods who'll walk among the living to turn a race of super predators into their prey.<br /> <br /> This isn't something that thematically happens within the confinements of subtle manipulation. It's the climax of those manipulations, but this climax isn't subtle, at least not from the POV of those in the know, even if it doesn't necessarily leave proof for humanity of what transpired.<br /> <br /> However you see Gehenna, it's thematically a foil for the Jyhad, giving it closure and meaning, but through stark contrast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553316#post1553316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's why I liked the idea of the US bombing him thanks to Ventrue manipulators. Mind you, I would have used an existing faction of Hunters for the death of Ravnos. It didn't have to be the Technocracy or US (because US centrism is terrible) but should have been humanity if they wanted to illustrate how mankind has become a threat to the undead.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree on both accounts. Bombing Ur-Shulgi instead of Vienna would have been a far better way of showing the threat of the Second Inquisition. If I ever run a chronicle with them, I'll definitely do that. Vienna could fall or lose its power in a number of more thematically appropriate way to explain the schism of the Tremere (which isn't a bad ide by itself, it's just the execution that's bad).<br /> <br /> Hunters killing Zapathasura would have been far better for the setting as a whole. Humanity as a threat would have been proven and wouldn't put any setting faction above others, while making them all understand the need for secrecy (with maybe an exception for Changelings, because they're crazy anyways). And if push comes to shove, an actual Nuke could have been used for this, which would actually reduce the need for a lot of Masquerade covering as nukes aren't supernatural.<br /> <br /> What about the chaos and instability that would engender? Heck, it wasn't the kickstart of the End Times? EMBRACE THE FUCKING CHAOS, the setting would be better off with this event being in full view (if not full understanding), and it wouldn't really affect the games of people that don't want it to be more than noticeable news.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553316#post1553316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, the Second Inquisition is an idea I both like and hate as a retcon. To me, it's War on Terror critique....a decade or more too late.<br /> <br /> It's also kind of objectively terrible for a game called Vampire: The Masquerade. Unless they have a REASON not to blow the whistle on everything...why don't they?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes very little sense in the way it was run. It's not that the idea can't be saved, it may be used to critique other things, more modern problems, and in the way pick up an actual explanation on why there are no whistle blowers, or why they can't convince people.<br /> <br /> But as it was made... yeah. It's basically late WoT with a lot of inconsistencies that don't really play along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T12:57:09-07:00","id":1553340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553331#post1553331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know many people hated the addition of having Uri Shugi into the lore and has no real personality and was meant to be a disposable character in a game setting that was ending. Now that the game is back and he is still around and serves no purpose at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I respectfully disagree<br /> Not the many people hated Ur-Shulgi but the personality and uselessness-part<br /> When he was introduced in around 2000 I think, in the Revised Assamite Clanbook we already have a plathora of Elders and Ancients with way less personality. Baba Yaga, Mithras, Kemintiri, Odin, Montano, the big names not really had any meaningfull personality just their background and a few plothooks and to be fair it was up to the storyteller how he would introduce and present them to their players and what encounter they will have<br /> Ur-Shulgi was a bit different, because he was more of an eldrich monstorsity akin to the aforementioned Cthulhu, older than most if not all the relegions and this was his main personality trait: he was old and not really the big fan of relegion, upstart gods and was a loyal &quot;son&quot;.<br /> To that point the Assamite was... lets say not really kindly portryed, tho' like the Ravnos they tired to polish them, make them more than murderer muslim cannibals - it hurts even to write it down, but lets face it they were in a sense a worse stereotype than the Gypsy Vampires who at least had some background - the mullo, a type of undead revenant in Romani folklore that is believed to return from the dead to commit malicious acts and drink human blood, often that of a relative. If you squinted enough you coudl see why they were added and of course Dracula and Stradh all added to the lore mix and we ended up with... well I wouldn't say offensive per see, because back then it wasn't <i>that</i> offensive, not more than the biker Brujah...<br /> To that setting addig Ur-Shulgi who was so old he not really recognized any relegion he predated and started some house cleaning was so strange it cought people offguard and lets face it, the Tremere were fan favorites and out of nowhere Ur-Shulgi handed their collective ass to the Clan and undone their gratest achivement and showed they are the new kids in the block<br /> All of these rubbed many the wrong way, but Ur-Shulgi had a personality - still have and if you add the later additions about the whole Baali thing, re-embrace and all paints a very deep and intriguing story and plot hooks your palyers can interract with, stats or no stats - even confronting him - in that sense he is no different than any other 4th generation vampire<br /> And he served a purpose, several actually (funny you mentioned Izhim wafi abd'Azrael ur-Baal, he revealed in the <i>Dark Ages Anthology</i> to be an agent of Namtaru, the Baali\u2019s patron, and he actually joined the Black Shepherd as his right hand. Furthermore, Ur-Shulgi\u2019s hostility toward religions aligns well with the Baali Clan weakness.. )\u200b<br /> <br /> Arguably offing Baba Yaga with Vasilisa was worse &quot;lore-offense&quot; than Ur-Shulgi and if you really want a blank monster without any personality or use, well Vasilisa is the one<br /> This of course don't realyl changes the fact Ur-Shulgi is widely disliked or outright hated, but I don't think because of the lack of personality - he do have one - or lack of purpose - ha have several (and later editions up to <i>Beckett\u2019s Jyhad Diary</i>\u200b kind of polished him and fleshed him out quite nicely)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 08-21-2025, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T13:01:27-07:00","id":1553341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553339#post1553339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there's no wrong answer, except there is a wrong answer, because while the faction was made to be both things at once, it can't be both things at once and it has to be nazis.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify:<br /> <br /> * I prefer the Technocracy as fascist critique of Western imperialism, capitalism, and the surveillance state.<br /> * Other people prefer them as stalwart defenders of humanity or heavily flawed idealists.<br /> * I don't think you can do them as Nazis and the Federation of United Planets.<br /> * I think trying to make Nazi Federation doesn't work.<br /> <br /> Which is different from the above, I believe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A real problem would be if anyone here were <i>really</i> trying to use the Union as an argument to defend fascism. No one should defend fascism, and I don't think this should be a right, so lets keep it at that. </div> </div> </div>I think I've seen plenty of arguments that the Technocracy is the only force actively advancing humanity and fighting for humanity. Which is a different argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cyclical or not, Gehenna is an apocalyptic event, it's about cataclysmic portents announcing the rise of powerful dead gods who'll walk among the living to turn a race of super predators into their prey. </div> </div> </div>I mean, it depends if it apocalyptic for humanity or vampires. Imagine for example in 2004, the Antediluvians summon all of their childer and eat them.<br /> <br /> Would humanity even notice?<br /> <br /> Wormwood also is a Gehenna scenario that happens like a thief in the night.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Agree on both accounts. Bombing Ur-Shulgi instead of Vienna would have been a far better way of showing the threat of the Second Inquisition. If I ever run a chronicle with them, I'll definitely do that. Vienna could fall or lose its power in a number of more thematically appropriate way to explain the schism of the Tremere (which isn't a bad ide by itself, it's just the execution that's bad). </div> </div> </div>The Transylvania Chronicles also showed the Tremere civil war with Tremere in Goratrix vs. whatever stole his body (Kupala/Tzimisce/Saulot or whatever).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hunters killing Zapathasura would have been far better for the setting as a whole. Humanity as a threat would have been proven and wouldn't put any setting faction above others, while making them all understand the need for secrecy (with maybe an exception for Changelings, because they're crazy anyways). And if push comes to shove, an actual Nuke could have been used for this, which would actually reduce the need for a lot of Masquerade covering as nukes aren't supernatural. </div> </div> </div>Hell, make the Indian government who nuked Ravnos and doing the cover up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It makes very little sense in the way it was run. It's not that the idea can't be saved, it may be used to critique other things, more modern problems, and in the way pick up an actual explanation on why there are no whistle blowers, or why they can't convince people. </div> </div> </div>Very true.<br /> <br /> I think the SI is a good idea but it needed to be established with limits like the fact that it has corruption, a limit on its resources, and maybe you could allude to the other gamelines tht they'd be detsroyed if they worked too to exposing the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T15:43:47-07:00","id":1553353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553340#post1553340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I respectfully disagree<br /> Not the many people hated Ur-Shulgi but the personality and uselessness-part</div> </div> </div> </div>Personality isn't background, or motivation. Usefulness, neither.<br /> <br /> The problem with Ur-Shulgi isn't that he was the worse at being like that, but that he was the worse means to cause the impact he caused in the setting.<br /> <br /> Most of those vampires you mentioned are blank slates. It's not that they don't have personalities, but that the game didn't make one for them, it's up to the ST. Which isn't a very good thing to do, by the way, but is still usable.<br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi is personality-less by design. He's described as not caring about anything beyond his life's mission. He has no quirks, no interests, he doesn't talk a lot, even his political views are simple to an extreme, without complexity or nuance, or even much reason beyond &quot;Haqim said so&quot;. His motivations aren't absent, they're instead geared towards justifying him being like that and never straying from it. It's indeed incorrect to say that he has no personality, but the problem is that his personality is to be obstinately shallow and boring, even if with a convoluted story behind it.<br /> <br /> Worse, and what really makes it bad, is that his power level is also constructed and justified to make things without a story. He has a huge impact on the setting, but the way it plays out is boring. He does everything without any effort, preparation or actual plot. His doing <b>is</b> the plot, all of it. He isn't either a villain that makes things through an interesting story, nor an apocalyptic event people have to prepare for or navigate. He's the meteor that falls, everyone dies, the end.<br /> <br /> And he's useless because while you can investigate his ancient backstory and have to live with the consequences of his actions, nothing really changes with that. Learning his story doesn't change what he is, and don't actually shed new light upon his actions, they're still <b>exactly</b> as it says on the tin. His followers can't be reasoned with, and he can't be reasoned with. The only thing that changes the outcome of an encounter with any of those people is if you'll convert to their cause or not, and that's binary: if you do, no deviation is allowed, if you don't, they try to kill you, the end. If Ur-Shulgi himself is present, you die, no roll allowed and that's it.<br /> <br /> He doesn't really impact the setting at large, either. Yes, his followers are around killing people, so what? They don't gather meaningful resources, they don't conquer land, they don't command nothing, they have no political agenda or interaction with any faction living or dead, they don't stop to meaningfully talk, they don't care about anything at all outside a very simple and strict mission of genocide through frontal engagement. They're otherwise just there in Allamut waiting for the next mission of wanton murder.<br /> <br /> On the purposes he served, few people actually deny, but that's not the point. At the end of the day, Ur-Shulgi was a literary device, a tool to achieve those purposes in the setting. But he was a bad tool. The purposes themselves were valid and needed, but they could all have been achieved through other means. Ur-Shulgi was the straightest and most boring tool for the job.<br /> <br /> So the point isn't that Ur-Shulgi literally had no personality or purpose, but that he was overall a very bad execution, and one deliberately designed to be exactly what it is with no room for innovation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553341#post1553341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is different from the above, I believe.</div> </div> </div> </div>More or less. And to be clear: your personal position in the matter is perfectly ok.<br /> <br /> What I want you to consider is that people disagree with some of your points.<br /> <br /> This disagreement comes from a few things:<br /> <br /> 1- The Technocracy was made to be both fascists and defenders of actual science and modern society. Our opinions on this depiction do not change the depiction itself;<br /> 2- First Edition Mage was quite luddite (in the derogatory sense, yes), so it did thought actual science and modern society were inherently corrupt and unsalvageable things;<br /> 3- You can't change those aspects of the game without changing it too much. Mage was fated to forever have a faction that's anti-fascist, but harbors science deniers, and a faction that's fascist, but promotes actual science, with each being respectively against or in favor of modern society with everything it has, good or bad;<br /> 4- Mage is a game about individuality, so both faction need nuance by the very nature of the game, we like it or not.<br /> <br /> So the movement you're very adamantly against of them being the Nazi Federation is basically the only option for anyone that want to recognize, within the premises of the game, that modern society and actual science have something good about them.<br /> <br /> Is that the real world? No. In the real world fascists are usually science-deniers and traditionalists that reject modernity in any way that isn't convenient for them. IRL fascists wouldn't ever be the Technocracy. But Mage isn't real life, for better or worse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553341#post1553341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I've seen plenty of arguments that the Technocracy is the only force actively advancing humanity and fighting for humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, because this is the WoD and most forces aren't doing it. The only other faction that could actually do it are the Traditions.<br /> <br /> Second, because nowadays people usually think the best things for humanity are good science and affordable healthcare.<br /> <br /> Third, outside Mages most game factions are inherently inimical to humanity, even if particular individuals may be exceptions, and the Union fights them. So they're literally, like it or not, one of the few factions actively hunting for a lot of threats to humanity, on a daily basis. This simply isn't a thing in <u>most</u> of the rest of the game (with a few exceptions).<br /> <br /> And fourth, because people have bias, just like we do. Anyone who thinks this is objectively wrong, because there are other forces in the WoD working to actively advance and protect humanity. But you need to have some broad knowledge of the game to know this, and even then you have to understand a lot of nuance, both to understand how others contribute and how the Union has serious limitations. So those people are defending a faction <b>you</b> think are unavoidably fascists, but not because they think this faction is right on being fascists.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's actually a fifth: some people are fascists. But at least among WoD fans they're still embarrassed enough to not try to defend fascism, so they don't actually argue that the Union is evidence in favor of fascism even if they secretly think so.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553341#post1553341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it depends if it apocalyptic for humanity or vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but the game is written from the point of view of vampires.<br /> <br /> However subtle Gehenna is to Humanity, it can't be subtle for the vampires, and so it can't be subtle for the players.<br /> <br /> From the Kindred POV there are portents and a very unsubtle showdown. Also, there are world-shattering events, even if they only shatter the undeads' world.<br /> <br /> So that's my point: however blind (or not) humanity would remain to the events, from the perspective of players Gehenna is by necessity an unsubtle plot. It can be hidden from humans, but it can't be just secret manipulations all the time. It can't be Jyhad-as-usual.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553341#post1553341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, make the Indian government who nuked Ravnos and doing the cover up.</div> </div> </div> </div>And maybe add a lot of behind-the-scenes espionage and conflict as governments struggle over the use of a nuke, because the overall population not knowing doesn't mean a lot of potentially interesting secret chaos can't be happening.<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition itself could be linked to this conflict, and one of the reasons they keep quiet about the supernatural is a very real fear of nuclear war if the truth transpires, a war that would be <b>objectively</b> worse than anything the supernatural has to throw at us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T19:24:20-07:00","id":1553361,"title":"","content":"I just want to point out that in Mage, there is no such thing as Science (as we know it in the real world,) just a differing form of Magick. Technology are magical devices that work because the consensus shifted enough to make their effects seem mundane and no longer wonderous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-22T04:15:15-07:00","id":1553369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553361#post1553361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to point out that in Mage, there is no such thing as Science (as we know it in the real world,) just a differing form of Magick. Technology are magical devices that work because the consensus shifted enough to make their effects seem mundane and no longer wonderous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which gets back to the larger issue of Mage being a different game to everyone else.<br /> <br /> People fully believe the Traditions want to restore the Dark Ages or make a world where there's no science, only magic.<br /> <br /> And then they get CONFUSED if you believe they are perfectly fine with science.<br /> <br /> Becuase different books say different things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-22T08:20:22-07:00","id":1553372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553353#post1553353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the purposes he served, few people actually deny, but that's not the point. At the end of the day, Ur-Shulgi was a literary device, a tool to achieve those purposes in the setting. But he was a bad tool. The purposes themselves were valid and needed, but they could all have been achieved through other means. Ur-Shulgi was the straightest and most boring tool for the job.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the basic view that if you're going to make a giant change like Ur-Shulgi, you need to weave it into the characters' motivations. DEADLANDS made the greatest course corrections in the history of RPGs by making the Adventure Modules about taking down the Four Horsemen of the Reckoners that had previously been Villain Sues for decades.<br /> <br /> The Transylvania Chronicles had a lot of railroading and invincible creatures but you were mostly at least there when dealing with things like Kupala and the Tzimisce Antediluvian.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is that the real world? No. In the real world fascists are usually science-deniers and traditionalists that reject modernity in any way that isn't convenient for them. IRL fascists wouldn't ever be the Technocracy. But Mage isn't real life, for better or worse. </div> </div> </div>Amusingly, my First Edition Mage character was a Science Revolutionary for the Sons of Ether who believed the Technocracy was the enemy of science and a Luddite faction because obviously denying how physics in the world worked (i.e. magic) was suppression of learning. Back then, the Etherites steampunk shit was trappings but serious science. No actual scientist would side with the Technocracy because everything they promoted was made up edited state-mandated bullshit like Lysenko-ism. Only later did the Traditions get depicted as science deniers and not the actual scientists...and then they went away from that to. It was very much my interpretation but the vibe I'd gotten was, &quot;free knowledge from the people controlling it.&quot;<br /> <br /> But my argument isn't &quot;The Technocracy is fascist=bad&quot; but my argument is, &quot;The books depict the Union very differently. I like one more than others but that's not my argument.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, because nowadays people usually think the best things for humanity are good science and affordable healthcare. </div> </div> </div>Part of why I have the choice of the Technocrats being Big Pharma against free health care is because, &quot;Why would the World of Darkness look like this if the people in charge of reality were flawed idealists instead of like Pentex?&quot;<br /> <br /> But again, my point is that I think the <u>argument</u> needs to be attacked. That these are all valid depictions of one group. Every time someone gets drawn into it, I feel like I've lost because my point is it should be accepted that people ignore the premise is broken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So those people are defending a faction <b>you</b> think are unavoidably fascists, but not because they think this faction is right on being fascists. </div> </div> </div>To reiterate, I don't think they're fascists at all. My point is that there is no consistent Technocracy and that people who argue there is one are wrong. I also feel that I have utterly failed every time I get drawn into arguing whether they're fascists or not because my point is not they're fascists. My point is that there are irreconciable depictions of them.<br /> <br /> My point being, to use another faction, is that I have two arguments, &quot;The Get of Fenris are not fascists and I prefer them not being fascists. I don't like people trying to combine the idea of them being fascists and not fascists. It's retcons that don't make sense together as one universe.&quot; I use the Technos as bad guys because they're The ManTM and I'm an anarchist in RL. But that's not my argument. My argument is that 1st Edition Union, 3rd Edition Union, and M20 are three different beasts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So that's my point: however blind (or not) humanity would remain to the events, from the perspective of players Gehenna is by necessity an unsubtle plot. It can be hidden from humans, but it can't be just secret manipulations all the time. It can't be Jyhad-as-usual. </div> </div> </div>I was hoping the Gehenna Wars were meant to be actually Gehenna. The summoning being done in the background but the whole, &quot;Elders fighting&quot; thing was silly. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And maybe add a lot of behind-the-scenes espionage and conflict as governments struggle over the use of a nuke, because the overall population not knowing doesn't mean a lot of potentially interesting secret chaos can't be happening.<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition itself could be linked to this conflict, and one of the reasons they keep quiet about the supernatural is a very real fear of nuclear war if the truth transpires, a war that would be <b>objectively</b> worse than anything the supernatural has to throw at us. </div> </div> </div>That would have been much better, yes.<br /> <br /> In my &quot;Esoterrorism&quot; book, the anti-magic faction kept the existence of vampires and other monsters secret because they believed that if the governments revealed that immortality was real and magic that the collapse of human civilization into chaos would happen with at least a large chunk of humanity siding with the monsters or worshiping them as gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-22-2025, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-22T10:29:20-07:00","id":1553377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553341#post1553341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the SI is a good idea but it needed to be established with limits like the fact that it has corruption, a limit on its resources, and maybe you could allude to the other gamelines tht they'd be detsroyed if they worked too to exposing the world</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Most emphatically.<br /> <br /> That being said, if the SI it's doing anything like Vienna, Alamut it's the perfect place. On the grounds that it doesn't exist (because Assamites obfuscated the place). It's the perfect crime.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-22T13:33:56-07:00","id":1553383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553361#post1553361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to point out that in Mage, there is no such thing as Science (as we know it in the real world,) just a differing form of Magick. Technology are magical devices that work because the consensus shifted enough to make their effects seem mundane and no longer wonderous.</div> </div> </div> </div>A couple things are important here:<br /> <br /> 1- That's not exactly true. Especially as editions went on, not every scientific exploration and discovery in the Setting comes from the Technocracy. There <b>are</b> objectively real laws of nature, what is now called <i>Earthly Foundations</i>. There are also laws of nature that derive from the Consensus without being directly established by it. The books do state that the Union doesn't have a finger on every research going on and that this research does have results. How far it goes is by design unclear, it may either be a niche thing, or actually the bulk of how reality works and science is made;<br /> <br /> 2- However similar this science is to real science, what's important is what it means as a metaphor and to the setting at large. In-character, it is about establishing a method of development that is safe and replicable, accessible to the masses, whose benefits come to all. Out-of-Character, it's still a stand-in for actual science and technology. And it's science, not Science. Science with upper-case S in Mage refers to Magic, and the point is science as an idea, not as an effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553369#post1553369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which gets back to the larger issue of Mage being a different game to everyone else.<br /> <br /> People fully believe the Traditions want to restore the Dark Ages or make a world where there's no science, only magic.<br /> <br /> And then they get CONFUSED if you believe they are perfectly fine with science.<br /> <br /> Becuase different books say different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage is a game about nuance. The very idea that a faction can only have one opinion is against the themes of the game.<br /> <br /> There <b>are</b> people in the Traditions that want to restore the Dark Ages, full stop. There's a big faction within it that's not fine with science by any means.<br /> <br /> And the proportion changed with time. By the early 90s the anti-science faction was <b>objectively</b> in power, with the <b>Virtual Adepts</b> as the sole exception.<br /> <br /> Never was that a black and white thing, there was always Mages, especially young Mages, that were fine with science or even embraced it, and their numbers and political power increased with time. After the Avatar Storm they finally mostly got the upper hand, as the Horizon Realms were also the main seats of power of the luddites within the Traditions, including the many Archmages.<br /> <br /> It's the other point about the Technocracy: you may be against the notion of making fascists a nuanced faction, but Mage doesn't do black-and-white.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553372#post1553372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;free knowledge from the people controlling it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, 1st Edition was predicated on the idea that Academia works with Doctors for Big Pharma to hide from everyone that you can cure cancer with Chromotherapy. It's literally a proponent of the idea that modern academia (A.K.A. <i>actual science</i>) control knowledge to keep people away from it.<br /> <br /> The Sons of Ether were literally fringe theories and pseudosciences being taken seriously.<br /> <br /> You're mistaking the in-game fact that Magic is real for what those game elements symbolize in the real world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553372#post1553372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That these are all valid depictions of one group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are all valid depictions of a <i>fictional</i> group that stands-in for a lot of things, in a game about the folly of thinking in absolutes (and where <i>everyone</i> thinks in absolutes).<br /> <br /> At no point the argument is that this is a valid depiction of actual fascists, and in general it is repeatedly stated that their fascism is a bad thing. Every book about the Technocracy after the first batch of Convention Books (which were horrible) has been adamant about how their fascist tendencies are exactly the problems you're expected to fight from within.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553372#post1553372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To reiterate, I don't think they're fascists at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I'm confused, for real.<br /> <br /> And by the way, they are.<br /> <br /> Or at least, they're everything about imperialism, including fascism.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553372#post1553372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My argument is that 1st Edition Union, 3rd Edition Union, and M20 are three different beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>When we get into this argument, what we're usually trying to say (me and other people that talk about the Technocracy) is that there's a reason for later Technocracy being as it is.<br /> <br /> And this isn't completely true, either. 2nd, 3rd and 4th edition Technocracies are distinct, but not a lot more than every other faction is also different between editions.<br /> <br /> But 1st edition Technocracy, that thing <b>is, indeed</b>, a different beast. And a beast that most people think didn't worked, and needed to be changed into its later depictions. Because they depicted mainstream science and modern technology as inherently bad.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553372#post1553372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was hoping the Gehenna Wars were meant to be actually Gehenna.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did they even defined something at all to be Gehenna?<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1553377#post1553377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said, if the SI it's doing anything like Vienna, Alamut it's the perfect place. On the grounds that it doesn't exist (because Assamites obfuscated the place). It's the perfect crime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to say that it is manned by people with far less contact with the modern world (as in, they don't live in a modern metropolis and have regular contact with modern society, politics, etc), and is located in the middle of nowhere, where it actually does make sense for no one to notice a bombardment.<br /> <br /> And piercing the veiling magics of such a place is an impressive feat, but one that makes more sense when the caster a single person and someone who doesn't know what a satellite is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-12T04:04:26-08:00","id":1555396,"title":"","content":"Speaking of lore changes, i'm of the view that the &quot;civil disturbances&quot; that served as cover for the anarch revolt that toppled the elders and lead to the formation of the Anarch Free States could be a reference to the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zoot_Suit_Riots\" target=\"_blank\">Zoot Suit riots</a>. What means we need an image of Jeremy MacNeil, Salvador Garcia, Crispus Attucks, Marguerite Foccart &amp; Smiling Jack like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cknW0WToLsw\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. ASAP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby