?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the problem of defining any place in the setting really.<br /> <br /> Mexico City was defined as effectively Mordor with the Nephandi, Pentex's headquarters, Sabbat, and a bunch of Baali underneath it.<br /> <br /> Which is unpleasant in that 1st Edition Shadowrun sort of way (which I love but was deeply problematic in many ways). However, it becomes a PROBLEM when you're an international corporation and brand and it turns out Mexico City is full of Vampire: The Masquerade gamers who are paying customers.<br /> <br /> And don't want to play a bunch of Satanic psychos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T20:37:53-08:00","id":1555452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555396#post1555396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of lore changes, i'm of the view that the &quot;civil disturbances&quot; that served as cover for the anarch revolt that toppled the elders and lead to the formation of the Anarch Free States could be a reference to the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zoot_Suit_Riots\" target=\"_blank\">Zoot Suit riots</a>. What means we need an image of Jeremy MacNeil, Salvador Garcia, Crispus Attucks, Marguerite Foccart &amp; Smiling Jack like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cknW0WToLsw\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. ASAP.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree! I always assumed that the Zoot Suit Riots were a cover for the collapse of Don Sebastian\u2019s Princedom and the fall of Los Angeles to the Anarchs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-14T03:15:22-08:00","id":1555468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555451#post1555451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the problem of defining any place in the setting really.<br /> <br /> Mexico City was defined as effectively Mordor with the Nephandi, Pentex's headquarters, Sabbat, and a bunch of Baali underneath it.<br /> <br /> Which is unpleasant in that 1st Edition Shadowrun sort of way (which I love but was deeply problematic in many ways). However, it becomes a PROBLEM when you're an international corporation and brand and it turns out Mexico City is full of Vampire: The Masquerade gamers who are paying customers.<br /> <br /> And don't want to play a bunch of Satanic psychos.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the issue with having any placed be ruled by &quot;outsider sects&quot; like the Sabbat or the Wan Kuei as a whole, i guess. Though to be fair it's possibly more of a matter of throw away lines or vibe ideas becoming lore-defining points that spark a narrative, incidental or not. Metaplot or vibe concepts over referencing actual knowledge of a place's history and peculiarities as inspiration.<br /> <br /> Also one of the reasons i prefer to stick to the &quot;historical novel&quot; or what i call &quot;Chicago school&quot; of citybook writing - look into major events, disasters and struggles in the history of a city, think of how one or two individuals of each clan embraced into that era would be like and what those events could tell us about the struggles the monsters hiding under the rug of society, be it opportunistically using them as cover for their crimes and disputes or inadvertently sparking things they did not mean to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-14-2025, 06:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-14T03:28:48-08:00","id":1555469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555468#post1555468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's the issue with having any placed be ruled by &quot;outsider sects&quot; like the Sabbat or the Wan Kuei as a whole, i guess. Though to be fair it's possibly more of a matter of throw away lines or vibe ideas becoming lore-defining points that spark a narrative, incidental or not. Metaplot or vibe concepts over referencing actual knowledge of a place's history and peculiarities as inspiration.<br /> <br /> Also one of the reasons i prefer to stick to the &quot;historical novel&quot; or what i call &quot;Chicago school&quot; of citybook writing - look into major events, disasters and struggles in the history of a city, think of how one or two individuals of each clan embraced into that era would be like and what those events could tell us about the struggles the monsters hiding under the rug of society, be it opportunistically using them as cover for their crimes and disputes or inadvertently sparking things they did not mean to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect you can draw a direct line from Point A (defining things with city books and supplements) to Point B in the Chronicles of Darkness where it's a toolbox rather than anything actually being defined.<br /> <br /> And yes, even Outstar hates some of it because she is Polish and doesn't like the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> Both sides have their adherents but the reason I love V:TM is its lore and NPCs but I understand that it limits your ability to define your home area or area you'd like to game.<br /> <br /> The perils of gaming in the &quot;real world.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-14T11:26:06-08:00","id":1555474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555469#post1555469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The perils of gaming in the &quot;real world.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>At the end this was and is a major problem with WoD, even when done sensibly.<br /> <br /> Requiem's take also has the advantage of, by going into a little less detail on each city, having the word count to do more cities, which means more places and more ideas on how they can organize in different ways.<br /> <br /> But then, there's something about the hard lore take of VtM that simply has an undeniable charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-14T12:17:08-08:00","id":1555476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555474#post1555474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At the end this was and is a major problem with WoD, even when done sensibly.<br /> <br /> Requiem's take also has the advantage of, by going into a little less detail on each city, having the word count to do more cities, which means more places and more ideas on how they can organize in different ways.<br /> <br /> But then, there's something about the hard lore take of VtM that simply has an undeniable charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>The larger issue is that Requiem never appealed to me because you can't detail a society like Chicago that way and Chicago was what drew me to the game with the complicated relationships, histories, romances, and rivalries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-14T14:22:17-08:00","id":1555478,"title":"","content":"Yes, the Chronicles of Darkness approach, that thing that's completely incapable of doing a 400+ page book on a single city to give it lots of specific details and lore...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/3073/world-of-darkness-chicago\" target=\"_blank\">Oh. Wait. Right...</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-14T14:47:21-08:00","id":1555479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555478#post1555478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the Chronicles of Darkness approach, that thing that's completely incapable of doing a 400+ page book on a single city to give it lots of specific details and lore...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/3073/world-of-darkness-chicago\" target=\"_blank\">Oh. Wait. Right...</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Yep and it's the only one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-14T15:09:48-08:00","id":1555480,"title":"","content":"Beyond the length making your post true in the most trivial technical way, not it is not the only detailed setting book in the CofD. How about you stop warring between the WoD and CofD with straight up falsehoods, and go back to the actual point of the thread?<br /> <br /> You made a demonstrably untrue statement, and when offered proof you doubled down instead of backing off. I'm not surprised, because you're you, and spare me any apologies because they're meaningless garbage after the first few of them, dozens later they just piss me off more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-14T15:22:53-08:00","id":1555481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555480#post1555480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beyond the length making your post true in the most trivial technical way, not it is not the only detailed setting book in the CofD. How about you stop warring between the WoD and CofD with straight up falsehoods, and go back to the actual point of the thread?<br /> <br /> You made a demonstrably untrue statement, and when offered proof you doubled down instead of backing off. I'm not surprised, because you're you, and spare me any apologies because they're meaningless garbage after the first few of them, dozens later they just piss me off more.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you say so. I'm not arguing because I don't consider this anything other than a matter of opinion. I reject the premise there's a &quot;true&quot; at all. Especially since I own the World of Darkness: Chicago book.<br /> <br /> I don't think of it as an Edition War either because I think they both have their benefits and both have their fans for reasons I'm trying to articulate. If you disagree, again, I don't have any problem with that but I consider it a matter of opinion.<br /> <br /> There's not a wrong or right to which you prefer. It's what you enjoy more. There's lore and NPCs in Chronicles and there's exceptional world building and rules in WOD. It's like comparing DC and Marvel. Both have their icons and down to Earth but you can compare/contrast them on which is emphasized.<br /> <br /> But I don't want to argue or belabor the point so yes, absolutely, I was in the wrong. Chronicles can and does have worldbuilding worth commenting on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-14T16:24:46-08:00","id":1555482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552692#post1552692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That line went anywhere?<br /> I kinda lost notice after in their clanbook story about Caine himself talking with their Antediluvian and more or less giving him the imperative of stopping the Secret Masters, after he had witnessed the coming of great destruction for mankind from their hands. What he revealed scared Vaddertha so much he turned his palace in to a Fortress and gathered artifacts like Fenris's fang, the Rainbow Birdge, the Tapestry of Blood ,etc... but that plot line never went anywhere right?<br /> And never truly it was relvelaed who the hell were the Secret Masters?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe in the theory of Alien: the Abduction, the game that never got to be. Probably the real thing behind Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-14T18:51:09-08:00","id":1555486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555478#post1555478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the Chronicles of Darkness approach, that thing that's completely incapable of doing a 400+ page book on a single city to give it lots of specific details and lore...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/3073/world-of-darkness-chicago\" target=\"_blank\">Oh. Wait. Right...</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I rest corrected.<br /> <br /> Maybe I didn't remember because I'm not a fan of city books to begin with, but thanks for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-16T23:06:24-08:00","id":1555515,"title":"","content":"With regard to the Ventrue's secret enemies, I've always read into that story that, if it's a story that the Ventrue have been passing from sire to childe for a long time, then it probably goes back to some ancient prince noticing that his control was opposed by the trading guilds that were the spiritual ancestors of the Technocracy and/or other High Clans predisposed toward having a lot of influence in the mortal world. The most important takeaway from the Aeons is that the unreliable storyteller characters narrating the clanbook were both paranoid and narcissistic enough to paint their rule as benevolent, and that this is held up by the authors as an example of the clan's culture.<br /> <br /> A lot of the off-camera shakeups to the status quo that have heralded the arrival of each new edition of the game have already been covered here, so I'll try not to belabor the point too much. It does leave a little bit of a sour taste that everything that changes the world happens to the branded NPC's, when those incidents could easily be the stuff of memorable published Chronicle-type adventures with a little reworking. V20 stands out as a favorite for me because it's such an inclusive setting construction kit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-16T23:32:20-08:00","id":1555517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555515#post1555515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With regard to the Ventrue's secret enemies, I've always read into that story that, if it's a story that the Ventrue have been passing from sire to childe for a long time, then it probably goes back to some ancient prince noticing that his control was opposed by the trading guilds that were the spiritual ancestors of the Technocracy and/or other High Clans predisposed toward having a lot of influence in the mortal world. The most important takeaway from the Aeons is that the unreliable storyteller characters narrating the clanbook were both paranoid and narcissistic enough to paint their rule as benevolent, and that this is held up by the authors as an example of the clan's culture.<br /> <br /> A lot of the off-camera shakeups to the status quo that have heralded the arrival of each new edition of the game have already been covered here, so I'll try not to belabor the point too much. It does leave a little bit of a sour taste that everything that changes the world happens to the branded NPC's, when those incidents could easily be the stuff of memorable published Chronicle-type adventures with a little reworking. V20 stands out as a favorite for me because it's such an inclusive setting construction kit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never thought it was actually a secret, ironically.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Secret masters&quot; was just the Ventrue commenting on the Jyhad on a greater level than just the common Elders. It's the Antediluvians, Wyrm, Mage Lords, and everyone else competing for dominance over the world.<br /> <br /> Ironically, like Project: Twilight, the only freedom mortals have is because so many people are competing with each other that they often cancel each other out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T09:53:34-08:00","id":1555537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555517#post1555517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never thought it was actually a secret, ironically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because exclusively from a lore perspective and taking into account the whole game, it isn't hard to picture what it is. You must read it from the limited perspective of the character, and how it is intended to inform a chronicle.<br /> <br /> The point here is threefold. First, it is to show the in-character perspective, how much in control the Ventrue perceive they are and how baffling whatever that lies above them is, and yet they keep at the game as a group, capable of antagonizing whatever it is.<br /> <br /> Second it is a nod to the ST to fill the gaps with whatever they want, not with everything the setting has. It may be any of those things, or it can be something else, it is what you need it to be. I know you're a sucker for lore, but you must remember that the game isn't meant to be played assuming all the lore from all the books from all the lines to be true at any given chronicle. Even if it has some very interesting characters and lore bits, it's still a tool for telling stories, not a story itself.<br /> <br /> And third and interacting with the other two points, this is also about what's implied: if the characters talk like that about an unknown quantity, what it says about <i>known quantities</i><i>?</i> You can assume this character knows about any of those things you want. Lets say the Union exists in your chronicle. Sure, you can have them be this strange force that vies for power with the Camarilla and clan Ventrue. But you can just as easily assume Elders, or even Ancilla, know about it and what it does, because Kindred are top spies after all. Then what this is saying is that the Ventrue <i><b>does not</b></i> see this Technocracy as mysterious or as an equal. Sure, they may be wrong. But they may also be manipulating the Union.<br /> <br /> You can interpret this kind of passage in many ways to build and color your chronicle, keeping in mind that it is a Vampire chronicle and it's perfectly valid in it to have Vampires be the real top dogs of the world at the end of the day (or night).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T10:07:37-08:00","id":1555538,"title":"","content":"The secret masters of second edition is clearly the Tal'Mahe'Ra. Its referenced in dirty secrets of the black hand.<br /> <br /> ok...as clearly as white wolf gets about that kind of stuff. One can always choose for it to be something else for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-26T12:22:04-08:00","id":1555889,"title":"","content":"Rereading Mexico City By Night today, and I can't help wishing the Revised era's disdain for Second Edition's goofiness hadn't prevented the book from being a direct sequel to Chaos Factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-26T13:56:35-08:00","id":1555892,"title":"","content":"The new baali write up seems really silly as those could have been a cool new thing and kept the baali.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-26T15:23:41-08:00","id":1555893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555889#post1555889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rereading Mexico City By Night today, and I can't help wishing the Revised era's disdain for Second Edition's goofiness hadn't prevented the book from being a direct sequel to Chaos Factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotta agree on that one. Besides Chaos Factor being really goofy, it was fun to have that book around. Any ST can adjust such goofiness.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-26T20:05:17-08:00","id":1555898,"title":"","content":"Bringing here what was said in the sister thread, I really, really think the Gangrel leaving the Camarilla made absolutely no sense at all.<br /> <br /> Neither the clan nor the Cam have an actual organization that gives meaning to it.<br /> <br /> In which sense you're a member to an organization that works just like a contact bridge between Princes to begin with? How do you talk in the name of a whole clan that isn't organized in the first place? How any of this actually work?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555826#post1555826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing here was because the Camarilla denied the Antediluvians and Xaviar, being the Justicar at that time, fought what he believed was an Antediluvian (again, this was a yes and no situation). He was so pissed off that the elders disregarded his claims that he took the entire clan out, and his political position allowed him to back up his claim. Many left, out of respect for the elder, but many remained. All this background is on Clan Novel Gangrel, it's really good.</div> </div> </div> </div>The backstory of it I know, that's not the point.<br /> <br /> Xaviar left the Camarilla. Ok. What does that means, he went to live alone in the woods? It seems to be the case, so it makes sense <i>for him</i>, but isn't a big deal.<br /> <br /> How did he took the entire clan out? Only the Tremere has a centralized organization within which this even makes sense. His political position allowed what and how, if the clan barely pays heed to elders more than a stone throw away? Why the clan most given to self sufficiency followed him at all, even if they respected him? And to where, the same grove in the woods? What does a clan independence from a Sect even looks like? And why didn't the Camarilla simply chose a new Gangrel Justicar right away?<br /> <br /> A Justicar isn't a member of the Inner Council or something. One of them leaving just means the position was vacated. Where's the Camarilla law that says if a Justicar steps down you can't replace them with the people who stay and call it a day? It isn't a good background. It may be a good story, as I already said the <i>Week of Nightmares</i> also is, but the result of it being depicted as <i>Clan Gangrel left the Camarilla</i> doesn't make any sense in any way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555847#post1555847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, the Clan Gangrel doing a walk-out from the Camarilla would work best if it were contextualised as the Clan making it plain that they work <i>with</i> the Camarilla, they do not work <i>for</i> the Ivory Tower: this being not necessarily intended as a permenant state of affairs but as a Power Move to demonstrate Gangrel self-sufficiency and demonstrate that the Camarilla is useful, but not so overwhelmingly essential that it can simply dictate terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe problem is that this is not how the Camarilla work.<br /> <br /> You could say that this is like treating the Camarilla as a government when it is the UN.<br /> <br /> What the Camarilla does isn't to control cities. Technically it doesn't control any territory at all. Instead, it is an understanding between Princes/Primogen. Whomever controls a Domain because they have the power and age to do so, accepts the Traditions and a couple other rules, namely Conclaves and Justicars, even then only to a certain degree. Otherwise they just keep in touch. Beyond that decisions are non-binding: no Prince is under any obligation to do whatever they don't want to. Other Princes may decide they'll take care of a troublesome colleague if they need, but that's less Camarilla Law and more people in contact self-organizing.<br /> <br /> Belonging to the Camarilla just means you accept the Traditions are a good idea and everyone should follow them. Even recognizing Conclaves and Justicars is completely optional (although probably healthy). Actually, not even that, it just means you live in an area where the local powers do that. Just as you can't personally leave the UN without physically leaving UN-abiding countries, leaving the Camarilla, from a personal level, isn't a thing except as self-exile.<br /> <br /> Camarilla's power before V5 isn't about dictating terms and has never been. It's about influence. The Inner Circle isn't a real institution, it's a conspiracy of sorts of the most influential Princes in the sect. That's all. They get things done because they have influence, not because anyone is required by some law to follow them. The Conclave is non-biding, it's just that paying heed to the collective will of lots of vampires is usually good policy. <i>Usually</i>. Justicars have authority in any city only when they're accepted by the local Prince, and they <i>have</i> been denied or expelled many times, even if letting them in is usually a good idea.<br /> <br /> So <i>not belonging</i> to the Camarilla in a non-V5 context is a weird thing to even say. By their reconing, everyone is a member in the sense that everyone is bound to follow the Traditions. The Sabbat is not Camarilla because it disregards the Traditions and actively try to control territory where they'll implement their beliefs. The Inconnu are not Camarilla because they do, actually, live alone in the woods or whatever. The Anarchs aren't even not Camarilla most of the time, that's the case only when they manage to control territories where they ban at least one Tradition.<br /> <br /> Most vampires don't even know the Camarilla exists, it's a concept, not a government. If you live within a Domain and by the Traditions, whether or not it's by choice, then whatever you call yourself means nothing, you're Camarilla for all intents and purposes that matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555850#post1555850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THE CAMARILLA covered it with essentially the Inner Council expelling the Brujah after so many high ranking members helped Theo Bell escape (which apparently he hadn't planned on). It also introduced the Hellenes as those Brujah who were allowed to remain without a representative.<br /> <br /> It's implied something happened to the Brujah Inner Councilwoman too (not the Beckoning) but I honestly forget what.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe Brujah leaving the Camarilla doesn't make a lot more sense than the Gangrel. A bit, maybe, but not a lot more. All previous observations apply.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's before the changes brought to the Camarilla itself by V5. As a more defined entity, the NuCam has, indeed, the power to also define membership.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-26T20:44:27-08:00","id":1555901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555893#post1555893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gotta agree on that one. Besides Chaos Factor being really goofy, it was fun to have that book around. Any ST can adjust such goofiness.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>I have held this opinion for about thirty years but it's one that I think I am about the only person who holds this. Basically, I feel like the Sabbat lost one of its most interesting plotlines when they got rid of infernalism, The Path of Evil Revelations, and the role of demonology in the sect. I know it's &quot;cheap heat&quot; that the organization that is **already** irredeemably evil and openly so has an even more depraved inner sect BUT I think it worked very well. The only reason the Sabbat hate the Path of Evil Revelations and demon worship is because they know demons enslace them and are better at this than the Sabbat. The Sabbat are for freedom and demon worship just enslaves you.<br /> <br /> And...it's not a very persuasive argument.<br /> <br /> It exposes the hypocrisy of the Sabbat and confronts them with a conundrum. &quot;Why DO I not embrace black magic and sell my soul if it gives me power? If I don't care about freedom in the slightest but allying with the biggest dog on the block?&quot;<br /> <br /> It exposes how low vampires are on the totem pole and how much the Sabbat's own philosophy doesn't stand up under scrutiny","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-26T20:52:31-08:00","id":1555902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555898#post1555898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Brujah leaving the Camarilla doesn't make a lot more sense than the Gangrel. A bit, maybe, but not a lot more. All previous observations apply.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's before the changes brought to the Camarilla itself by V5. As a more defined entity, the NuCam has, indeed, the power to also define membership.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the idea of what they were going for with the Camarilla. The circumstances in the world have changed and the Masquerade is semi-broken. So they're attempting to isolate from the people they blame (believing their own lies it was the Anarchs and not the Camarilla who broke the Masquerade). They want to throw the Brujah to the Second Inquisition in hopes of distracting their enemies. It was the same strategy that absolutely didn't work during the first Inquisition but fits with the vampires having very little species-wide loyalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T00:59:19-08:00","id":1555903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555898#post1555898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Brujah leaving the Camarilla doesn't make a lot more sense than the Gangrel. A bit, maybe, but not a lot more. All previous observations apply.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's before the changes brought to the Camarilla itself by V5. As a more defined entity, the NuCam has, indeed, the power to also define membership.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>True<br /> But at least the Brujah had <i>some </i>background why they did it from the quasi-historical beef with the Ventrue what sparked the numerous Brujah Wars (starting with Greece when they nested in several domains especially Athen while Artemis Orthia ruled Sparta, attracting many Ventrue to her cause and forming the Peloponnesian League with other local Ventrue Princes and wages war against the Brujah-ruled Athens then several more conflicts in Antiquity) that peeked in the Punic Wars where Malkavians and Ventrue of Rome crushed eventually Carthage of the Brujah (aaaand Baali, but we don't talk about that)<br /> And the effect/memory of the Brujah Wars echoed in the Dark Ages trying to remember and recapture the glory of Athen and Carthage while gave them a very strong view and opinion against Sparta and Rome and her heirs...<br /> Later they eagerly embraced Marxism, collectivism, syndicalism, and even Darwinism and engaged in various revolutionary groups to topple the rising pauperization during the Industrial Revolution and the Victorian Age - things that positioned them fiercly against the Ventrue and their ideals and views<br /> Even later the only notabvle Brujah &quot;movement&quot; was the <b>Brujah Council</b>, or the <b>Soviet Brujah</b>\u200b (eventually they formally abandoned the ideal of open coexistence with mortals... nuff' said)<br /> While the Brujah had 0, literaly 0 Clan structure compared even to the Gangrel who at leats had their own little system, they deep down always at least hated the Venture and everything and their allies did or created with passion<br /> And of course the Brujah always were &quot;closet-Anarachs&quot; ... or openly proto-Anarachs then full fledged supporters of the Anarachs<br /> <br /> The Brujah departure - especialy after the Lasombra joined, who in their eyes are Ventrue Light/Tesco Ventrue at best just with nastier tricks - is somewhat understandable tho' as you pointed it previous observations apply, especially the individual level-part<br /> <br /> What I never really understood, why the Tzimisce ended up Anarchs isted of Camarilla in V5<br /> <br /> From the logical point of view, the Tzimisce should be Camarilla!<br /> The Tremere are in ruins (the Salubri are back - and any self respecting Dragon should own a precious Unicorn) and the Nosferatu while like the Gangrel were seen interlopers on their lands, more often than not, a Nosferatu if introduced itself and accepted the Tzimisce lordship was treated like... just anyone else. Same with the Gangrel. In the Dark Ages this was something no other High Clan did and I belive this carried over in to the modern nights, not to mention both Clans were the victims of the Tremere Gargoyle experiments. While the Gangrel left, the Tzimisce basically age old allies are there - not to mention the Lasombra who jumped ship...<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce - overfond of traditions - logically should find the neofeudalism of the Camarilla attractive while the Anarch standpoint repulsive\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> Anyhow, this is just my two coppers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T04:00:15-08:00","id":1555906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555901#post1555901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, I feel like the Sabbat lost one of its most interesting plotlines when they got rid of infernalism, The Path of Evil Revelations, and the role of demonology in the sect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it fits more with the Sabbat as it was. To me the PoER very much feels like a symptom of the rot setting in as the Sabbat movement ideologically grinds to a halt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T04:11:45-08:00","id":1555909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555906#post1555906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it fits more with the Sabbat as it was. To me the PoER very much feels like a symptom of the rot setting in as the Sabbat movement ideologically grinds to a halt.</div> </div> </div> </div>While they were intended as the &quot;badder than the bad&quot;, I also was interested in revisiting them with DEMON: THE FALLEN and DARK AGES as the role of demons isn't necessarily the one-dimensional &quot;I want to destroy and debase the world&quot; that so much of the early treatment of them was. The Path of the Devil being one about freedom at all costs and so many of the demons ARE nihilistic Nephandi types but that's because of their pain and insanity while others have their own vision of building a better tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T04:26:19-08:00","id":1555910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555909#post1555909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While they were intended as the &quot;badder than the bad&quot;, I also was interested in revisiting them with DEMON: THE FALLEN and DARK AGES as the role of demons isn't necessarily the one-dimensional &quot;I want to destroy and debase the world&quot; that so much of the early treatment of them was. The Path of the Devil being one about freedom at all costs and so many of the demons ARE nihilistic Nephandi types but that's because of their pain and insanity while others have their own vision of building a better tomorrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I maybe misremembering, but I thought the more positive demons were basically solely the result of incarnating in humans. Like, demons need some space between themselves and the horrors of their pasts to allow them that perspective. And anything you summon from the Abyss directly is going to be absolutely the one-dimensional demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T11:05:12-08:00","id":1555914,"title":"","content":"I don't like V5<br /> Theo Bell's revolt doesn't make sense; nothing in his &quot;background&quot; indicates that he would plan the assassination of Hardestadt and Pieterzoon, as if the Inner Circle didn't have at least a coterie of archons or alastors to protect him during a Conclave.<br /> <br /> Based on the novels, Theo Bell, Don Cerro (with his drive for justice), and Helissente wouldn't have a powerful enough motive to induce Theo to commit murder in front of several witnesses without a solid motivation.<br /> <br /> Theo being accepted among the Anarchs also doesn't make sense; he eliminated Anarchs and Sabbats, and was known as Killa B.<br /> More likely, even if he miraculously had enough personal power to eliminate a 6th and 7th generation vampire (Theo being a 9th generation), the Anarchs probably wouldn't shelter or protect him. They would likely take advantage of the situation to avenge sires, allies, and progeny killed by Theo, rather than welcoming him as a symbol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T12:50:57-08:00","id":1555916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555914#post1555914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like V5<br /> Theo Bell's revolt doesn't make sense; nothing in his &quot;background&quot; indicates that he would plan the assassination of Hardestadt and Pieterzoon, as if the Inner Circle didn't have at least a coterie of archons or alastors to protect him during a Conclavel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to undercut you here but this is the one area that V5 has no blame as Theo Bell killed Hardestadt for betraying vampirekind in the Gehenna novel and metaplot of 2004.<br /> <br /> It was always meant to be the capstone of the character.<br /> <br /> Theo didn't kill Jan either and denied it. Jan just was presumed to have been killed during the Conclave when the Brujah representatives moved to protect Theo Bell, probably because Hardestadt demands for fealty offended them all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Theo being accepted among the Anarchs also doesn't make sense; he eliminated Anarchs and Sabbats, and was known as Killa B.<br /> More likely, even if he miraculously had enough personal power to eliminate a 6th and 7th generation vampire (Theo being a 9th generation), the Anarchs probably wouldn't shelter or protect him. They would likely take advantage of the situation to avenge sires, allies, and progeny killed by Theo, rather than welcoming him as a symbol. </div> </div> </div>I'm confused at, &quot;A 9th generation vampire can't kill a 6th&quot; because one of the reason the Storyteller system works is that it doesn't work like Dungeons and Dragons. It is possible and in fact very frequent to kill much more powerful beings than yourself because the difference is Disciplines not really an existential one. <br /> <br /> Besides, Theo Bell has defeated Karsh and Marcus Vitel before.<br /> <br /> It's kind of his thing to punch above his weight class.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T13:22:11-08:00","id":1555918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555914#post1555914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like V5<br /> Theo Bell's revolt doesn't make sense; nothing in his &quot;background&quot; indicates that he would plan the assassination of Hardestadt and Pieterzoon, as if the Inner Circle didn't have at least a coterie of archons or alastors to protect him during a Conclave.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not completly true<br /> Bell was always &quot;Cerro's colored progeny&quot; and Cerro fanned his feelings by showing him the decadence and debauchery of Europe's Elysiums as he wanted him to experience the Camarilla at its best and worst and as Cerro's influence in the sect rose, he had to shouldering burdensome responsibilities for his sire's sake.<br /> Cerro raised and the Inner Circle appointed him Justicar partially because they knew his Progeny would become Archon - and Bell was well aware, and resentful, of the politics behind his appointment; as well, he harbored no small amount of sympathy for the anarchs.<br /> He did his job nontheless, so good when Jaroslav Pascek became Justicar, he kept Bell even though the two Kindred despised each other.<br /> The truth is - and many miss this - he had to serve the whims of Hardestadt and Jan Pieterzoon for years and the Justicars had forced Bell to remain in Washington, D.C after the whole Vitel incident<br /> Bell always had that &quot;Brujah flame&quot; , despised the plotical plays and never really liked the idea to be a Ventrue pawn (maybe because Helissente was probably a Carthaginian Brujah, tho' that is not confirmed) - maybe, and this is specualtion from my part, when his Sire was killed by Karsh, the right-hand man of Hardestadt and the Inner Circle it gave him that last push he always needed, after all, Bell and Cerro was close - as close as father and son and Family was always a very important part of Theo's charatcer back from his slave days<br /> So after Hardestadt's lackey killed the man who was his Father in a sense, who gave him porpuse and power to destroy his slave master...?<br /> I think it is reasonable he made a suicide run (he had nothing to lose at that point, kept in a short leash, lost everything, chained to DC, etc) ; Bell probably never expected to survive the attack - also, offing older kindred as a younger not unheard of , the whole Anarch Revolt based on that idea... and freedom - but he did. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T16:27:31-08:00","id":1555929,"title":"","content":"In Gehenna, Bell killed Hardestadt because of the massive number of Thin Bloods that Hardestadt was diablerizing to hold back the Withering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T16:59:46-08:00","id":1555930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555903#post1555903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True<br /> But at least the Brujah had <i>some </i>background why they did it from the quasi-historical beef with the Ventrue what sparked the numerous Brujah Wars (starting with Greece when they nested in several domains especially Athen while Artemis Orthia ruled Sparta, attracting many Ventrue to her cause and forming the Peloponnesian League with other local Ventrue Princes and wages war against the Brujah-ruled Athens then several more conflicts in Antiquity) that peeked in the Punic Wars where Malkavians and Ventrue of Rome crushed eventually Carthage of the Brujah (aaaand Baali, but we don't talk about that)<br /> And the effect/memory of the Brujah Wars echoed in the Dark Ages trying to remember and recapture the glory of Athen and Carthage while gave them a very strong view and opinion against Sparta and Rome and her heirs...<br /> Later they eagerly embraced Marxism, collectivism, syndicalism, and even Darwinism and engaged in various revolutionary groups to topple the rising pauperization during the Industrial Revolution and the Victorian Age - things that positioned them fiercly against the Ventrue and their ideals and views<br /> Even later the only notabvle Brujah &quot;movement&quot; was the <b>Brujah Council</b>, or the <b>Soviet Brujah</b> (eventually they formally abandoned the ideal of open coexistence with mortals... nuff' said)<br /> While the Brujah had 0, literaly 0 Clan structure compared even to the Gangrel who at leats had their own little system, they deep down always at least hated the Venture and everything and their allies did or created with passion<br /> And of course the Brujah always were &quot;closet-Anarachs&quot; ... or openly proto-Anarachs then full fledged supporters of the Anarachs<br /> <br /> The Brujah departure - especialy after the Lasombra joined, who in their eyes are Ventrue Light/Tesco Ventrue at best just with nastier tricks - is somewhat understandable tho' as you pointed it previous observations apply, especially the individual level-part<br /> <br /> What I never really understood, why the Tzimisce ended up Anarchs isted of Camarilla in V5<br /> <br /> From the logical point of view, the Tzimisce should be Camarilla!<br /> The Tremere are in ruins (the Salubri are back - and any self respecting Dragon should own a precious Unicorn) and the Nosferatu while like the Gangrel were seen interlopers on their lands, more often than not, a Nosferatu if introduced itself and accepted the Tzimisce lordship was treated like... just anyone else. Same with the Gangrel. In the Dark Ages this was something no other High Clan did and I belive this carried over in to the modern nights, not to mention both Clans were the victims of the Tremere Gargoyle experiments. While the Gangrel left, the Tzimisce basically age old allies are there - not to mention the Lasombra who jumped ship...<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce - overfond of traditions - logically should find the neofeudalism of the Camarilla attractive while the Anarch standpoint repulsive\u200b<br /> <br /> Anyhow, this is just my two coppers</div> </div> </div> </div>The Brujah also had New Lacadaemonia (greek island from Ashen Thief), It was also supposed to be featured on Brujah Chronicles but the book never got published. This place was intended to be a recreation of Carthage (Baali included). It's fate is unknown after the Dark Ages.<br /> <br /> Sheriff Devon from Indianapolis has access to the Brujah history and those involved in the sack of Carthage. That's how they traced Marcus Vitel before his supposed death against Bell (this happened during the Clan Novel Brujah).<br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555910#post1555910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I maybe misremembering, but I thought the more positive demons were basically solely the result of incarnating in humans. Like, demons need some space between themselves and the horrors of their pasts to allow them that perspective. And anything you summon from the Abyss directly is going to be absolutely the one-dimensional demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> On the Abyss entities, some of them are the emotions held during their appearance like the thing that attacked the Lasombra during the clan novel trilogy. It was a fragment of [Lasombra] himself summoned by Abyss mystics until Montano neutralized the situation. Then [Lasombra] himself re-emerged from the Abyss rift made by Moncada's Leviathan back in Gehenna: The Final Night. I believe they're different things to demons and though they appear to behave like them, it's more on who has the strongest emotion when being summoned and used what gives them shape.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","user":"Saga","date":". 11-27-2025, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T17:09:39-08:00","id":1555931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555930#post1555930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Abyss entities, some of them are the emotions held during their appearance like the thing that attacked the Lasombra during the clan novel trilogy. It was a fragment of [Lasombra] himself summoned by Abyss mystics until Montano neutralized the situation. Then [Lasombra] himself re-emerged from the Abyss rift made by Moncada's Leviathan back in Gehenna: The Final Night. I believe they're different things to demons and though they appear to behave like them, it's more on who has the strongest emotion when being summoned and used what gives them shape.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Weirdly, I always felt Obtenebration was a weaksauce Discipline and combining it with Necromancy was a good idea because the Abyss was already tied to the Underworld as well as the popular conception of Hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T20:43:02-08:00","id":1555932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555931#post1555931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weirdly, I always felt Obtenebration was a weaksauce Discipline and combining it with Necromancy was a good idea because the Abyss was already tied to the Underworld as well as the popular conception of Hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was just the power over shadows of the classic vampires but since controlling just shadows would be weak, adding substance to it made it &quot;cool&quot; back in the day, specially since those masters of the discipline we're the Lasombra, the &quot;evil&quot; Ventrue. It got OP during Dark Ages (Dark Steel...) and then expanded better into the Revised era, it took a while to get the highly demanded Abyss Mysticism that appeared for the first time on Players Guide to the High Clans (I remember &quot;Nephilim&quot; promoting his ideas on the forums before the book launch) and Mexico City by Night<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-28T00:24:50-08:00","id":1555934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555902#post1555902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the idea of what they were going for with the Camarilla. The circumstances in the world have changed and the Masquerade is semi-broken. So they're attempting to isolate from the people they blame (believing their own lies it was the Anarchs and not the Camarilla who broke the Masquerade). They want to throw the Brujah to the Second Inquisition in hopes of distracting their enemies. It was the same strategy that absolutely didn't work during the first Inquisition but fits with the vampires having very little species-wide loyalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what about their embrace of Antedeluvian cults? I don't really buy any of that <b><i>IF</i></b> we assume the old Camarilla. This strategy seems really weird overall for them, and it isn't really as much isolation as it is a complete change on what they do.<br /> <br /> V5 Camarilla may be a continuation in lore, but it has actually very little to do with the original beyond the most superficial level. It's a completely new entity with distinct goals and strategies.<br /> <br /> That said, I can buy it on its own terms. It isn't uninteresting or anything like that, and it can make for some very fun styles of game, as far as you see it as a distinct thing with a background that just resembles the original. Overall V5 is far more palatable when I take it as its own setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555903#post1555903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But at least the Brujah had <i>some </i>background why they did it from the quasi-historical beef with the Ventrue</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's for sure.<br /> <br /> Even on the organization side, while they have none whatsoever, they are far more prone to coordinate if they have a reason to.<br /> <br /> If leaving the Camarilla were <i>a thing</i>, they'd be far more likely to do so as a clan than the Gangrel. Or to be expelled.<br /> <br /> As philosophers, especially political philosophers, though, I see the Brujah fighting tooth and nails for the <i>ideal</i> of the Camarilla. Many of them despise it, most have at least some criticism, but any &quot;typical&quot; Brujah who endorses it does so with gusto, because it isn't just about politics, it is about everything this system represents to them despite its flaws. In fact I think for V5 it makes little sense for the NuCam to have expelled them because of Theo Bell, but instead because of their resistance to its change. I totally see the Brujah being absolutely repulsed by what the NuCam became.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555909#post1555909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While they were intended as the &quot;badder than the bad&quot;, I also was interested in revisiting them with DEMON: THE FALLEN and DARK AGES as the role of demons isn't necessarily the one-dimensional &quot;I want to destroy and debase the world&quot; that so much of the early treatment of them was. The Path of the Devil being one about freedom at all costs and so many of the demons ARE nihilistic Nephandi types but that's because of their pain and insanity while others have their own vision of building a better tomorrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>For starters, I think the presence of infernalists among the Sabbat is an interesting plot point, but I strongly disagree with your stance on them only hating enslavement. I think it's interesting precisely because it plays with the notion that as monstrous as the Sabbat's morality is, it's still pretty much there, and so there are things they consider too abhorrent. It only gets better with the idea that some of those entities may be actually less monstrous than the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> But one thing to understand here, and that's important about any and all plots about infernalism, is that they're more about the people doing it than the entities contacted. As well-meaning as a Fallen may be (assuming we're talking about them), the person who contacts a demon doesn't know or expect it. This person has all the reasons in the world to expect the worse from this entity and assume any kindness as a lie. This is a person that's either deeply selfish, delusional or desperate, to the point of walking the irredeemable path. That, more than the entity itself, is why infernalism is always bad news.<br /> <br /> So, in a crossover with DtF sure, a sympathetic Fallen may be a great addition to the game's cast. But as far as the plot of infernalism itself goes, this is always about upper-case Evil to a degree even the Sabbat would shy from. If not as a fact, at least as a very concrete potential.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555910#post1555910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I maybe misremembering, but I thought the more positive demons were basically solely the result of incarnating in humans. Like, demons need some space between themselves and the horrors of their pasts to allow them that perspective. And anything you summon from the Abyss directly is going to be absolutely the one-dimensional demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly.<br /> <br /> Torment is always huge for virtually all Demons who didn't went through any process that could reduce it, but it isn't a goal-definer. Most Fallen will fit your description to <i>some</i> degree, but there are plenty exceptions.<br /> <br /> First of all, while they're likely to be extremely violent and full of prejudice, full-Torment Fallen can still ascribe to any of their factions for some reason. Sure, a greater number will be Raveners and very few will be Reconcilers, but it's still their suffering and their own free will to decide how to deal with it.<br /> <br /> Second, once out of the Abyss they're all able to find ways to deal with Torment and possibly reduce it. In fact, <i>leaving the Abyss does that</i> to some degree, they're out and back to a world where they may have experiences that placate their pain. They are objectively in a better situation than at the Abyss, and will remain so as long as they don't go back. Nothing really stops a T10 Fallen NPC from coming down to more manageable, and even actually low, levels of Torment.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, what makes Torment quite different from most mechanics for supernatural beings, and even from Humanity as the Kindred experience it, is that Torment is actually just old regular PTSD. It's an unimaginably huge chain of traumas, but still mundane in nature. So much so that besides the not-so-high XP price for reducing it, the rules don't require any extraordinary conditions for doing so, they're more lenient than any other similar trait. So the Fallen only actually have to process their emotions to change their minds, even if that's still easier said than done.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555903#post1555903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I never really understood, why the Tzimisce ended up Anarchs isted of Camarilla in V5</div> </div> </div> </div>No other reason than they wanted to &quot;balance&quot; the sects. Most movements actually happened just because Paradox was hyper-focused on the idea that clans as a whole ascribe to a single sect, so you have to distribute them between NuCam and DumbAnarchs.<br /> <br /> Once we got the description of Old Clan and pre-Revolt Tzimisce, no clan has more of a Camarilla vibe than them. They are the most attached to Domains and Traditions, to Hospitality rules and Embrace rules, they're literally the archetypal Kindred according to Camarilla law. It's bizarre that they somehow became Anarchs to &quot;be left alone&quot; instead of becoming NuCam to have their own turf respected exactly in the way they like it. Switching Tzimisce and Lasombra in V5 story would still be a bad idea, but at least would make way more sense.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555931#post1555931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weirdly, I always felt Obtenebration was a weaksauce Discipline and combining it with Necromancy was a good idea because the Abyss was already tied to the Underworld as well as the popular conception of Hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's first important to remember that &quot;Abyss&quot; means at least four not-necessarily-linked things in WoD.<br /> <br /> We can theorize about it a lot, but for any meaningful conversation on canon the Abyss from DtF has no relation or contact point with the Abyss of Obtenebration (at least none is known).<br /> <br /> And it definitely has no implied relation with the Underworld. That's one of the reasons a lot of people who played either Necromancers, Lasombra or both disliked the combination, as it merges unrelated themes and rules, and powers that don't really have much in common when you know them well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-28T01:09:33-08:00","id":1555935,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m inclined to say that more options are generally better. So I like the idea of Brujah, Gangrel, Lasombra, and Tzimisce all being in the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> As others have said, I think it make a lot of sense to have Camarilla Tzimisce, especially if we go with the Old Clan or similar ideas. <br /> <br /> I also think that it doesn\u2019t make that much sense for the Gangrel to leave the Camarilla. In large part, because leaving takes a degree of organization that the Gangrel don\u2019t have. Also, there isn\u2019t really a down side to being in the Camarilla for the Gangrel. If you\u2019re a Gangrel in a Camarilla city, it can he the respect and privileges associated with being a Camarilla Clan. If you don\u2019t want the associated responsibilities, you leave the city and you\u2019re essentially free. <br /> <br /> It does make a bit more sense for the Brujah to leave the Camarilla, as they essentially are the Anarch Clan.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I think that there is a problem with how the Anarchs are handled. I like the idea of shifting focus to the Camarilla vs Anarch conflict. The problem is, the Anarchs shouldn\u2019t be a bunch of full fledged Clans with elders and hierarchy and everything. The elders are hierarchy are for the Camarilla, the Anarchs should represent the interests of the young within each Clan. In that way, all Clans should have some degree of Anarch representation in opposition to elders - presumably in the Camarilla hierarchy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-28T15:00:00-08:00","id":1555945,"title":"","content":"Imo the tzmisce are very very sabbat on pretty much every level and the other sects are at best mixed fits.<br /> <br /> Thats said it would have made more sense to have them go independant ala the heceta if you're insistant on them not being sabbat and going back to the old voivode model.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-28T17:32:33-08:00","id":1555946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555945#post1555945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imo the tzmisce are very very sabbat on pretty much every level and the other sects are at best mixed fits.<br /> <br /> Thats said it would have made more sense to have them go independant ala the heceta if you're insistant on them not being sabbat and going back to the old voivode model.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on how you're defining the Sabbat and which Tzimisce you're using.<br /> <br /> If the Tzimisce are a bunch of randomly inhuman &quot;body modification is EVILLLlllll&quot; then yes they fit into the Sabbat that are just a bunch of random psychopaths.<br /> <br /> If your Tzimisce are obsessive controlling types that rule over a single apartment building as a neo-feudal lord then the Camarilla or Anarchs both fit them just as well and they probably are a poor fit for the Sabbat because they would not share with their packs in the more leveled collectivist Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Also, did they ever say the Tzimisce joined the Anarchs or are there just Tzimisce members?<br /> <br /> I can understand the latter as the Tzimisce defecting to the Camarilla would be far more difficult than the Lasombra, assuming that (untrue or not), the Tzimisce's reputation is far worse than the latter in terms of them being alien Masquerade-breaking monsters. The Anarchs, by contrast, will take anyone and you're far more likely to get an inconsistent level of response than a Camarilla-wide reaction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-28T23:53:38-08:00","id":1555948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555946#post1555946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends on how you're defining the Sabbat and which Tzimisce you're using.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their are infinate interpretations of both the moment they hit the table, even the idea of dracula vs pinhead is a false binary and frankly, lazy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the Tzimisce are a bunch of randomly inhuman &quot;body modification is EVILLLlllll&quot; then yes they fit into the Sabbat that are just a bunch of random psychopaths. </div> </div> </div>That's such a lazy and reductive interpretation of both and their aspects. I'm genuinely surprised to hear this coming from someone so well read on lore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If your Tzimisce are obsessive controlling types that rule over a single apartment building as a neo-feudal lord then the Camarilla or Anarchs both fit them just as well and they probably are a poor fit for the Sabbat because they would not share with their packs in the more leveled collectivist Sabbat. </div> </div> </div>This is largely an interpretation of 5th and isn't particularly well fleshed out (if you'll excuse the pun) as it is far shallower than the post human monsters (which paradox doesnt like) with some low level reflections of dark age tzmisce. But such a mindset is going to be incredibly disruptive in the other two sects for a number of reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, did they ever say the Tzimisce joined the Anarchs or are there just Tzimisce members? </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much the only way to justify it, If you ask a Tzmisce, (or a lasombra) to go Anarch the Sabbat is effectively what you get. Their's very little the sect has to offer from a clan perspective so it has to be individual.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can understand the latter as the Tzimisce defecting to the Camarilla would be far more difficult than the Lasombra, assuming that (untrue or not), the Tzimisce's reputation is far worse than the latter in terms of them being alien Masquerade-breaking monsters. The Anarchs, by contrast, will take anyone and you're far more likely to get an inconsistent level of response than a Camarilla-wide reaction. </div> </div> </div>I'd probably argue the Tzmisce are probably a better fit than the Lasombra even if both are bad fit, the anarch will take anyone but their isnt actually much to appeal to the Tzmisce's tzmisce their unless they're just looking to carve out a vovoide and need to pretend to be in a sect for various reasons.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-29T00:28:34-08:00","id":1555949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555946#post1555946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can understand the latter as the Tzimisce defecting to the Camarilla would be far more difficult than the Lasombra, assuming that (untrue or not), the Tzimisce's reputation is far worse than the latter in terms of them being alien Masquerade-breaking monsters. The Anarchs, by contrast, will take anyone and you're far more likely to get an inconsistent level of response than a Camarilla-wide reaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know<br /> Even a Sabbat monster at the end of the day crave for two things: solitude to do whatever he wants and a few underlings to command them around<br /> You probbaly not even would notice a Sabbat Tzimisce moved in the neighborhood; one of the buildings - probably abandoned to be begin with - staring to have some stories on the streets, it is haunted, people go in, never come out, homeless people start to dissapear, strange sightings...<br /> ...nothing you would not experience already; I mean a TONS of rural legends are about these places you can chalk up as &quot; <b>Urban Cryptids&quot; ; </b>from the Jersey Devil, and Mothman, alongside others such as the Skunk Ape, Chupacabra, and regional legends like the Rougarou of the Louisiana bayou and the Nain Rouge of Detroit to the Hodag, the fearsome-looking beast from Rhinelander, Wisconsin, with horns, spikes, and claws.<br /> Even seasoned Camarilla would not autmatically think, yeah there is a Tzimsice<br /> I think there was a story of a Tzimisce in the clanbook mayhaps, who filled the inner core of a sykscraper with his native soil and used the vents to time to time feed and drag inside someone...<br /> And this is the most hardcore, nonhuman monsters who care little about the Masquarade<br /> But even the Sabbat in his prime had the Grimaldi , rivaling in influence the Giovanni and the Ventrue and Toreador , tutored in private schools to guarantee the best possible education and hide the slow aging process and blood-borne quirks and ultimately served the Sabbat as deep-cover agents, who handled the unpopular affair of dealing with mortal agencies, preserving and maintaining the Masquerade and supplying the sect with money.<br /> Their job was literally to clean up (sometimes hand in hand with the Zantosa) and keep the Masquerade for their masters<br /> <br /> A Metamorphosist just wants to be left alone, really and have subjects<br /> And the doctor from Mexico who actually helps anyone who comes willingly is a good example, you can be an inhuman monster while provide important service<br /> <br /> Now move away from this the bulk of the Clan or what the Tzimsice should/would/could be in V5 is different, but not that much<br /> They are &quot;dragons&quot;<br /> The Tzimisce <i>own</i>.<br /> The Tzimisce are about ownership. They don't care about results. They don't care about inspiration. They care about total control. They want you to live every waking moment knowing you exist at their whims. Their clan's obsession with manners is a mirror of exactly that. Enter a Tzimisce's home with gifts, and you will remain unharmed for three nights... because you are its guest. For those three nights, it is responsible for you. Therefore, it owns you. It doesn't matter the Tzimisce's subjects are loyal because of love, because of fear, because of ancient oaths, because of Koldunic magic, because of blood bonds, because you fleshcrafted their brain into perfect servitude, because of stockholm syndrome...it makes no difference to the Tzimisce.<br /> What metters is to <i>own</i>\u200b<br /> The Tzimisce are hoarders and bound to the land they own.<br /> <br /> They have always been the overlords ruling over peasant villages from ancient castles. We as players have known them as metamorphosists, but pretty much every book noted that there were actually rather few followers of that path, with most Tzimisce using the discipline without applying greater philosophy to it and subscribing to transhumanism only in a very general &quot;We're better than the Herd&quot; sort of way.<br /> <br /> SO the new young Anarch Tzimsice strive to redefine themselves by what they rule over.\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200bMany Anarch barons and for that matter Sabbat rulers hold the position because they feel a responsibility to the goals and well-being of the sect. Not for personal glory, nor for power over their fellow Kindred, but out of an actual sense of civic duty that most Kindred lost<br /> Now this... is not ownership.<br /> This is quite the opposite, your subjects <i>owns you<br /> <br /> What the Camarilla have, what it is all about is ownership!</i><br /> <br /> You wouldn't actually notice a Tzimsice living in the Camarilla city; just a hosue - rundown because after they got it, they not realyl care to maintain it, the improtant is to <i>own</i> it and servants, like the Grimaldi and the Zantosa to make things work for them and provide food<br /> They are actually better than the Ventrue to stay in their own ivory towers, instead micromanaging things while the blood is delivered<br /> And they are very polite, politically adept and with the Zantosa and Grimaldi connections their ties should be very tight with the Toreador, Ventrue, Lasombra maybe, and thanks to the historical ties, the Gangrel ,their everloyal &quot;warhounds&quot; lying around in the castle and the whispering shadow Nosferatu next to their throne of bones made out of their enemies<br /> <br /> In the Tzimisce' eyes the past ~600 years happened, just not really changed anything and if you look at the neofeudal byzantine system of the Camariall?<br /> Neither to the Camarilla... \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 11-29-2025, 03:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-29T03:35:25-08:00","id":1555950,"title":"","content":"On reflection id like to add the v5 tzmisce write up to bad changes. Its really shallow, 'safe' and bland<br /> <br /> Dragons dragons dragon dragons......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-29-2025, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-29T04:46:51-08:00","id":1555952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555950#post1555950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On reflection id like to add the v5 tzmisce write up to bad changes. Its really shallow, 'safe' and bland<br /> <br /> Dragons dragons dragon dragons......</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked it because the Tzimisce being &quot;alien, inhuman, and cold&quot; because of their Clan does not fit with V:TM. I also hate the body shaming that the &quot;evil corrupting discipline&quot; take of fleshcrafting comes with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-29T10:01:23-08:00","id":1555953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555952#post1555952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I liked it because the Tzimisce being &quot;alien, inhuman, and cold&quot; because of their Clan does not fit with V:TM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much all the clans have shitty personalities and toxic cultures once you get to know them v5 even leans into this with clan compulsions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also hate the body shaming that the &quot;evil corrupting discipline&quot; take of fleshcrafting comes with. </div> </div> </div>You can always make negative interpretations of anything written down but to shut down entire sections because of it is a really bad idea. Take a look at w5 for this in effect<br /> <br /> Although you did implicitly endorse my perspective here by admitting it was about staying safe and conservative on what vtm should be and this should be 'protected'.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-29T13:12:18-08:00","id":1555956,"title":"","content":"Just sharing my thoughts and I'm not shaming your like of the older versus the new. I just always think that vampires should be about corrupted humans versus beings removed from that experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-29T21:33:33-08:00","id":1555968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555946#post1555946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, did they ever say the Tzimisce joined the Anarchs or are there just Tzimisce members?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much yes.<br /> <br /> They stated directly that the clan is now evenly divided between Sabbat and Anarchs, but in the Sabbat they're officially the <i>Antitribu</i>, now. Which is either a recognition of this moniker as a Sabbat thing, or a formal moving of the clan to the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> Also, their rationale is that the young Tzimisce are Anarchs because they see Sabbat Tzimisce as hypocrites. They're not the most fervent Anarchs, but they're fully Anarchs. There are, of course, a few Cam Tzim, but they're rare.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555948#post1555948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their are infinate interpretations of both the moment they hit the table, even the idea of dracula vs pinhead is a false binary and frankly, lazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that's not here or there. Once we're talking about a clan as a whole, or its majority at least, we're talking about archetypes, about the &quot;average&quot; individual that, while it doesn't actually exists in any single member, governs a lot of how the group as a whole works.<br /> <br /> When we get to the infinite variations of actual individuals, then talking about the clan's sect becomes entirely pointless, because individuals may fit into any of them (and some on more than one).<br /> <br /> All that said, I don't think the &quot;voivode&quot; type works within the Anarchs so well. Why would they? The Camarilla is the sect that defines Domain and keep Traditions around the concept. The Anarchs expect either some level of collectivism or disposition for political experiments (a concept unfortunately little played with through the whole VtM history). I don't think those types would fit well within the Sabbat, either. The &quot;transhumanist&quot; types sure, they're Sabbat through and through, especially if you have a less simplistic view of the sect than Phipps.<br /> <br /> I actually agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Sergeant Brother</a> and go even further, I think the game should just stop classifying clans and bloodlines as belonging to faction X or Y and have everyone in the Camarilla with just the caveat that the Big Seven are the most common, nothing else. Everyone Sabbat should be called <i>Antitribu</i> not out of numbers, but as a reflection of their ideologies. And Anarchs are not an actual sect, just a phenomenon that can happen at any domain with a rigid hierarchy or something. Call LA and others as &quot;rogue cities&quot; as they don't follow the Traditions nor any formal faction (and they may be sympathetic to Anarchs and be previous Anarchs). And have groups as the Setites and Giovanni as Independent Factions, Minor Sects, Clan-Sects or something like that, recognizing that they only accept members of one clan (or not even that), but that not all members of such clans belong to those factions.<br /> <br /> The whole idea of clans belonging to one sect or another, given how VtM built those sects, is bullshit as is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555949#post1555949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You wouldn't actually notice a Tzimsice living in the Camarilla city; just a hosue - rundown because after they got it, they not realyl care to maintain it, the improtant is to <i>own</i> it and servants, like the Grimaldi and the Zantosa to make things work for them and provide food</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they would be so indifferent, this sounds kinda stupid outside specific characters, even if caring for the house isn't the priority.<br /> <br /> But what I really want to add is that a Tzimisce doesn't stand out if they don't want to. Without a lot of research or magical tampering, you can't really tell a Tzimisce from most other clans. If one wants to come in without giving away their clan, they can claim most anything, really, they'd have a better time faking it than a Lasombra hiding their lack of shadow and reflection.<br /> <br /> Also, you're severely downplaying how much Princes pay attention to the presence of unknown vampires in their cities, and the consequences. However long it takes for someone to find it out, once it happens there will be Hell to pay if you didn't present yourself as tradition states.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555950#post1555950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On reflection id like to add the v5 tzmisce write up to bad changes. Its really shallow, 'safe' and bland<br /> <br /> Dragons dragons dragon dragons......</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> They took the vanilla vampire and made it even more bland.<br /> <br /> It looks like something different from other vampires... but isn't really? It's just way more one-note.<br /> <br /> But I don't think the transhumanists are that better, really. As much as we can add nuance in the actual character, the take on them seen in books was pretty much one-note since First Edition, just <i>Necroscope</i> instead of hoarders. And I take Phipps' complain about the <i>Necroscope</i> Tzimisce, it isn't that &quot;alien, inhuman and cold&quot; give them shitty personalities and toxic cultures, it is that VtM is about exploring the human condition through the lens of the Vampire and their Humanity, and the classic Tzimisce are about... not being human to begin with and having no response to moral quandaries, nor having human failures (unless you go out of your way, and from book depiction, to purposefully explore how this is all pretense for the Edge Lord teenager beneath).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T01:20:31-08:00","id":1555971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555968#post1555968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, but that's not here or there. Once we're talking about a clan as a whole, or its majority at least, we're talking about archetypes, about the &quot;average&quot; individual that, while it doesn't actually exists in any single member, governs a lot of how the group as a whole works.<br /> <br /> When we get to the infinite variations of actual individuals, then talking about the clan's sect becomes entirely pointless, because individuals may fit into any of them (and some on more than one).<br /> <br /> All that said, I don't think the &quot;voivode&quot; type works within the Anarchs so well. Why would they? The Camarilla is the sect that defines Domain and keep Traditions around the concept. The Anarchs expect either some level of collectivism or disposition for political experiments (a concept unfortunately little played with through the whole VtM history). I don't think those types would fit well within the Sabbat, either. The &quot;transhumanist&quot; types sure, they're Sabbat through and through, especially if you have a less simplistic view of the sect than Phipps.<br /> <br /> I actually agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Sergeant Brother</a> and go even further, I think the game should just stop classifying clans and bloodlines as belonging to faction X or Y and have everyone in the Camarilla with just the caveat that the Big Seven are the most common, nothing else. Everyone Sabbat should be called <i>Antitribu</i> not out of numbers, but as a reflection of their ideologies. And Anarchs are not an actual sect, just a phenomenon that can happen at any domain with a rigid hierarchy or something. Call LA and others as &quot;rogue cities&quot; as they don't follow the Traditions nor any formal faction (and they may be sympathetic to Anarchs and be previous Anarchs). And have groups as the Setites and Giovanni as Independent Factions, Minor Sects, Clan-Sects or something like that, recognizing that they only accept members of one clan (or not even that), but that not all members of such clans belong to those factions.<br /> <br /> The whole idea of clans belonging to one sect or another, given how VtM built those sects, is bullshit as is.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>True and that's usually how a rationalize oddities in terms of sect but I would'nt really implies clan/sect dynamics as pointless as they're both an interesting plot point and a quite thematic. It's telling these arguments usually boil down to inconvenience with Sabbat and independent clans as nobody seems to care much that say the Ventrue are mostly Carmarilla and all this could have been wrapped up by third edition with about two pages commenting on all clans being present to a degree in all sects-like the revised Sabbat has ironically.<br /> <br /> I think the Tzmisce generally work most effectively in the Sabbath-especially post revolt culture, which makes sense as they're written as a Sabbat clan from day 1. Even when they're not transhumanist they're brutal, inhuman, inhumaine and elderich in a way which just gels with the sect in a way it doesn't with the Tower or the movement.<br /> <br /> I don't really see it as a binary and don't loose much sleep over who qualifies as <i>Antitribu</i> or clan. I'm okay with Lasombra and Tzmisce being Sabbat clans for a number of reasons (im my home cannon the Salubri and Ravnos are also majority Sabbat). If anything the <i>Antitribu</i> in previous editions is just a way of articulating how they differ from the mainstreme clan and in 5th a clumsy way of reducing characterization to make them less appealing to play. IMO the revised Sabbat actually had the best angle which is that pretty much all clans are present in all sects to a degree, do a write up on how this causes them to differ from the majority (or not) and leave it at that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> It looks like something different from other vampires... but isn't really? It's just way more one-note.<br /> <br /> But I don't think the transhumanists are that better, really. As much as we can add nuance in the actual character, the take on them seen in books was pretty much one-note since First Edition, just <i>Necroscope</i> instead of hoarders. And I take Phipps' complain about the <i>Necroscope</i> Tzimisce, it isn't that &quot;alien, inhuman and cold&quot; give them shitty personalities and toxic cultures, it is that VtM is about exploring the human condition through the lens of the Vampire and their Humanity, and the classic Tzimisce are about... not being human to begin with and having no response to moral quandaries, nor having human failures (unless you go out of your way, and from book depiction, to purposefully explore how this is all pretense for the Edge Lord teenager beneath). </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is, I don't really see anything which marks them out as more shallow-or more accurately, the other clans as deeper. I've never been a big fan of the mandate that vtm has to be about exploring the human condition through the lens of the Vampire and their Humanity, so i really don't have a problem with turning that on it's head with the Lasombra (reveling in vampirism) or Tzmisce (completely rejecting humanity) the clan has a pretty rich and interesting history and explains itself pretty well and I'm not expecting a the vampiric version of thus spoke zarathrustra from them anymore I'm expecting Chomsky with fangs from every Brujah.<br /> <br /> <br /> I am in agreement that the v5 write up for the clan is embarrassingly shallow even by my relaxed standards however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T12:52:22-08:00","id":1555988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555971#post1555971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True and that's usually how a rationalize oddities in terms of sect but I would'nt really implies clan/sect dynamics as pointless as they're both an interesting plot point and a quite thematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to throw this away as much as I want to have a clearer description that doesn't induce players to think in too strict standards, which is a recurring problem with the fanbase.<br /> <br /> You can say which clans are most numerous and powerful as a whole in each sect without really describing it as &quot;Sect's clan&quot;, which is the source of many problems we have with both players and writers with too narrow views. In my games I had members of every clan in every sect, I had an important Giovanni elder be actually Toreador, but she was Giovanni by birth and got back to her family, I had the Primigen of a city include a Follower of Set, I had Sabbat cities with no presence of important Lasombra or Tzimisce, only Bishops of other clans, yet at no point those were standard or the overall politics of each clan about the sects meaningfully changed or got stale.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555971#post1555971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's telling these arguments usually boil down to inconvenience with Sabbat and independent clans as nobody seems to care much that say the Ventrue are mostly Carmarilla and all this could have been wrapped up by third edition with about two pages commenting on all clans being present to a degree in all sects-like the revised Sabbat has ironically.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason my suggestion focus on identifying all clans as Camarilla is because, at the end of the day, the Camarilla is the only sect where it matters, even if they shouldn't be. The Sabbat got everything <i>Antitribu</i> to play with, and the Anarchs weren't even organized like that to begin with, they're not a sect before V5. Having members of any clan at those two groups was all too simple, it was in the Camarilla that things got unnecessarily tricky.<br /> <br /> And I thoroughly blame a lot of this on Marcus Vitel, as he was the first and archetypal canon example of a non-Cam clan in a Cam city.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555971#post1555971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Tzmisce generally work most effectively in the Sabbath-especially post revolt culture, which makes sense as they're written as a Sabbat clan from day 1. Even when they're not transhumanist they're brutal, inhuman, inhumaine and elderich in a way which just gels with the sect in a way it doesn't with the Tower or the movement.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one way to look at it, but I also think it's not the best take.<br /> <br /> First of all, distinguishing the two takes as members of each sect is more interesting to me. Sure you can have inner conflict if you have both at the same place, but with two sects you make a clearer point about how distinct they are even if they're not at all as much as they think.<br /> <br /> Second, I don't think everyone in the Cam should ascribe to Humanity, just as not every Tzimisce should be &quot;inhumane&quot;. The sect has a stance about Humanity, but it isn't really something they can or care to control as much as they want to use as propaganda. Humanity as a sect thing is something that arose in the game more as an excuse for the rules than it ever was a consequence or necessity of the game and its themes. The ST can vet or let any Path or Road, but in the fiction it doesn't make much sense for the sect to interfere so much on such personal matters as long as members follow the Traditions.<br /> <br /> If you assume Paths exist, I really don't buy that they're so rare in the Camarilla, especially after DA made them such a big part of Vampire culture and Humanity just one among many.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555971#post1555971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it is, I don't really see anything which marks them out as more shallow-or more accurately, the other clans as deeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they're shallower, precisely, but more on point that they're narrower.<br /> <br /> Other clans have archetypes that, while simple, have room for a lot of variation without breaking with it, especially the Big Seven, but not only them. The Tzimisce have maybe the harder to play with in making different characters without breaking it. Of course, this is not a problem when you plan to break it to begin with, but as a rule of thumb the result is very same-y, most Tximisce characters that follow the clan archetype are little more than it because of how little space you have to work with.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555971#post1555971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never been a big fan of the mandate that vtm has to be about exploring the human condition through the lens of the Vampire and their Humanity, so i really don't have a problem with turning that on it's head with the Lasombra (reveling in vampirism) or Tzmisce (completely rejecting humanity) the clan has a pretty rich and interesting history and explains itself pretty well and I'm not expecting a the vampiric version of thus spoke zarathrustra from them anymore I'm expecting Chomsky with fangs from every Brujah.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it has to be a mandate, and I don't think it was really a mandate for most of the game's history.<br /> <br /> The problem is less to have other themes and more to be hard to have this theme if this is what you want for your game.<br /> <br /> As it stands, the Transhumanist Tzimisce have always been the most disruptive clan in a game that isn't made to incorporate them specifically. This is a bad thing not because their themes aren't welcome, but because you can't use them on the main type of story the setting was designed to tell, and any story that includes this theme they may get in your way. The fact you can use them for great effect if you know how doesn't change that it's an extra barrier to using them at all.<br /> <br /> Other than that, what exploring Humanity means? It can be a lot of things, and people like the typical Lasombra who revel in vampirism are still doing that, it's a foil. Characters that aren't quite human, or not human at all, can still explore aspects of humanity either by augmenting them, contrasting them, or showing them in a purer form (like human greed without other human aspects that check it). Even if this isn't the goal, most &quot;inhuman&quot; characters are still quite human.<br /> <br /> When you strive to make a character as inhuman as possible, you're prone to actually end up with an individual character that's too shallow because too much energy goes on <i>not being</i> instead of <i>being</i> something, and you'll still probably miss the point as you end up with something <i>you</i> think as inhuman, but other people may seem as too much human silliness. And that's how I feel with the Transhumanist Tzimisce.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T18:06:05-08:00","id":1556024,"title":"","content":"Yeah, since they were already making some pretty radical changes, I think that letting every Clan be in every Sect might have been a good change. Then they could develop the culture, politics, and potentially even \u201cbiology\u201d of Camarilla, Sabbat, and independent versions of each Clan. <br /> <br /> For Tzimisce, we could have the twisted flesh shaping Sabbat Tzimisce, for the Camarilla we could have the hyper conservative and territorial possessive elders, the independents could have their own flavor and angle as well. The same idea could apply to each Clan.<br /> <br /> One change that happened really early on that I don\u2019t like and that I think tainted all subsequent Sect related discussions is this idea that the Camarilla is good or humane as opposed to the evil Sabbat. I don\u2019t think that the Camarilla should necessarily be any more moral than the Sabbat. They are more cautious, conservative, manipulative, political, and more strictly hierarchal. Not nicer. I personally don\u2019t like the idea that \u201cHumanity\u201d is somehow enforced by the Camarilla. In fact, Humanity is a game mechanic, not a in-game political affiliation, so I think it\u2019s silly to suggest that the Camarilla has a \u201cHumanity only\u201d policy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T18:47:39-08:00","id":1556029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556024#post1556024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, since they were already making some pretty radical changes, I think that letting every Clan be in every Sect might have been a good change. Then they could develop the culture, politics, and potentially even \u201cbiology\u201d of Camarilla, Sabbat, and independent versions of each Clan.<br /> <br /> For Tzimisce, we could have the twisted flesh shaping Sabbat Tzimisce, for the Camarilla we could have the hyper conservative and territorial possessive elders, the independents could have their own flavor and angle as well. The same idea could apply to each Clan.<br /> <br /> One change that happened really early on that I don\u2019t like and that I think tainted all subsequent Sect related discussions is this idea that the Camarilla is good or humane as opposed to the evil Sabbat. I don\u2019t think that the Camarilla should necessarily be any more moral than the Sabbat. They are more cautious, conservative, manipulative, political, and more strictly hierarchal. Not nicer. I personally don\u2019t like the idea that \u201cHumanity\u201d is somehow enforced by the Camarilla. In fact, Humanity is a game mechanic, not a in-game political affiliation, so I think it\u2019s silly to suggest that the Camarilla has a \u201cHumanity only\u201d policy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it really depends on how you view vampires.<br /> <br /> Are vampires denying their true nature and fooling themselves that the Sabbat and Paths are the true way?<br /> <br /> Or are the Sabbat a bunch of try hard edgelords that enforce alien moralities on themselves to fool themselves they're not damned monsters?<br /> <br /> I like the idea that the Camarilla is low humanity scum but Paths are fundamentally a lie Kindred tell themselves to feel like they are a part of nature or divinely inspired versus cursed.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla may not be better than the Sabbat but the Sabbat are DELUDED that the more they kill, the more they can escape their damnation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T20:05:55-08:00","id":1556041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556029#post1556029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it really depends on how you view vampires.<br /> <br /> Are vampires denying their true nature and fooling themselves that the Sabbat and Paths are the true way?<br /> <br /> Or are the Sabbat a bunch of try hard edgelords that enforce alien moralities on themselves to fool themselves they're not damned monsters?<br /> <br /> I like the idea that the Camarilla is low humanity scum but Paths are fundamentally a lie Kindred tell themselves to feel like they are a part of nature or divinely inspired versus cursed.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla may not be better than the Sabbat but the Sabbat are DELUDED that the more they kill, the more they can escape their damnation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can certainly see delusion as being a major part of the Sabbat. Not just with regards to morality. The Sabbat delude themselves that they are free, yet they blood bind themselves to the pack and subject themselves to the harsh conformity of the Sabbat. They delude themselves that they aren\u2019t controlled by elders yet Sabbat elders manipulate their pawns just as Camarilla elders do.<br /> <br /> Morally, they give themselves to the Beast while they cling to occult or philosophical constructs to make them feel in control.<br /> <br /> Mechanically speaking, Paths of Enlightenment aren\u2019t a delusion, they really are a hack that subverts the need to constrain behavior and morality. Which is kind of an issue I have with them in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T21:25:17-08:00","id":1556044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556041#post1556041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanically speaking, Paths of Enlightenment aren\u2019t a delusion, they really are a hack that subverts the need to constrain behavior and morality. Which is kind of an issue I have with them in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>While not canon, I had an interesting theory about the Sabbat's relationships to Path.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2022/12/the-judas-compact-or-how-sabbat-got.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2022/12/the-judas-compact-or-how-sabbat-got.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2022/12/the-judas-compact-or-how-sabbat-got.html\" target=\"_blank\"> https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2022/12/the-judas-compact-or-how-sabbat-got.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Basically, it goes with the theory that the Sabbat made Paths wholly distinct from the previous Roads because they needed morality systems that would be able to help them wage war against the Camarilla (and Antediluvians theoretically) but that meant bastardizing the Roads they're based on, often to the point of unrecognizability. The Road of Night went from being the Road of Batman to the Road of X-men's Apocalypse for example. It's why so few Sabbat have more than 1-5 in a Path because you have to more or less reinvent the wheel for yourself to get higher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-01T02:58:36-08:00","id":1556053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556024#post1556024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One change that happened really early on that I don\u2019t like and that I think tainted all subsequent Sect related discussions is this idea that the Camarilla is good or humane as opposed to the evil Sabbat. I don\u2019t think that the Camarilla should necessarily be any more moral than the Sabbat. They are more cautious, conservative, manipulative, political, and more strictly hierarchal. Not nicer. I personally don\u2019t like the idea that \u201cHumanity\u201d is somehow enforced by the Camarilla. In fact, Humanity is a game mechanic, not a in-game political affiliation, so I think it\u2019s silly to suggest that the Camarilla has a \u201cHumanity only\u201d policy.</div> </div> </div> </div>As silly as it is, and I think it is, after DA Humanity definitely became an in-game thing, even if most younger vampires aren't aware of that. It is a Path just as any other, only more intuitive for modern humans because of Enlightenment more than due to any innate property. Take from that what you will, but that's the canon as far as it goes.<br /> <br /> I too think the Camarilla as &quot;the good guys&quot; bis pretty silly, but it has a lot to do with early Sabbat doubling down on Camarilla Propaganda as presented in the core and going full <i>Lost Boys</i> without much nuance. The Sabbat would get way more fleshed out later, but never completely escape this narrow niche, and so the Camarilla ended up being the &quot;lesser of two evils&quot; even if it's Humanity only just as a means of making the Masquerade easier to enforce.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556029#post1556029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it really depends on how you view vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, this is semantics.<br /> <br /> What you're talking about is exploring justification. Can a monster be justified for being a monster? Does being less monstrous really excuses you? A good deed born out of selfish intentions is good at all?<br /> <br /> Those are interesting themes, but they don't change the actual reality: the Sabbat is objectively evil and the Camarilla objectively opposes it. Without adding nuance that's not within the books (it started to pour in with time, but never went far enough to change the basic premisses), the Cam are the good guys and the Sabbat are the bad guys. The Sabbat eat children and murder innocents for giggles, the Camarilla teach their members that while they won't be punished for doing bad stuff, it's healthier for them to not. And they're at war with the well-being of mortals at stake.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556044#post1556044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While not canon, I had an interesting theory about the Sabbat's relationships to Path.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it isn't canon, I think you just spelled out what the canon implied.<br /> <br /> Of course, ater DA and all that, as from a Doylist standpoint it was the opposite, Paths are older and later the authors managed a more nuanced and elaborate take as Roads.<br /> <br /> That said, what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a> said is true: delusion or not, Paths are a real game mechanic that gets the job done.<br /> <br /> And even your take on their delusion... it's more of a philosophical/theological take than anything.<br /> <br /> Damnation and Salvation are not things, they're ideas. Above all else, it's a <b>Christian</b> idea. Other religions, even other Abrahamic religions, rarely if ever think about it in the terms Christians do. A Path may be inferior to a Road in many ways, but the notion of avoiding damnation through them being a delusion requires that you buy into the idea of damnation to begin with, and that you have a way to concretely observe it in some way. So... nah, I'm good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-01T07:33:00-08:00","id":1556058,"title":"","content":"Good point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556053#post1556053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damnation and Salvation are not things, they're ideas. Above all else, it's a <b>Christian</b> idea. Other religions, even other Abrahamic religions, rarely if ever think about it in the terms Christians do. A Path may be inferior to a Road in many ways, but the notion of avoiding damnation through them being a delusion requires that you buy into the idea of damnation to begin with, and that you have a way to concretely observe it in some way. So... nah, I'm good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, though in this case it's an anti-Christian idea that regardless of good or evil you are screwed and the larger matter of ethics regardless of religion.<br /> <br /> Vampires are a fascinating challenge to Christian ideology as they fundamentally must choose to horribly treat humans or treat them less horribly based purely on their own values systems.<br /> <br /> Which the Sabbat rejects any real sympathy for on religious/racist grounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-01-2025, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-01T18:12:38-08:00","id":1556075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556058#post1556058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, though in this case it's an anti-Christian idea that regardless of good or evil you are screwed and the larger matter of ethics regardless of religion.<br /> <br /> Vampires are a fascinating challenge to Christian ideology as they fundamentally must choose to horribly treat humans or treat them less horribly based purely on their own values systems.<br /> <br /> Which the Sabbat rejects any real sympathy for on religious/racist grounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, it's not Anti-Christian. Not all Christianity abides to the idea that everyone can find salvation. Entire schisms and some heresies happened over this concept. Just remember that for most churches you need baptism to even have a chance at salvation to begin with.<br /> <br /> Vampires are fascinating in many respects, and it can't be denied that VtM was written from a Christian perspective.<br /> <br /> That said, you have to abide to the idea of spiritual corruption in some manner for <u><b>this</b></u> notion of being screwed to apply, and even them your belief system has to ascribe necessary corruption to the condition of being a Vampire. Some on the Sabbat believe that, but not everyone.<br /> <br /> Some Sabbat believe as Vampires they're bound to different rules, so they can find Salvation in their inhuman ways. Some believe in ideas about spiritual corruption that never had nothing to do with Salvation as Christians define it. Some simply have no such concept. Even the notion that Vampires are &quot;anti-natural&quot; isn't a given, who said they don't have a valid ecological niche? Those who do think they're damned, also think they're beyond Salvation, so why try the impossible when it serves no-one?<br /> <br /> As much as the Sabbat can be used as a picture of what giving-up on Salvation looks like, they're actually important in the game as a means to explore the very notion that this idea may be wrong, and there may be no such thing as Salvation or Damnation. Having this may not be for everyone, but it surely is for a lot of people, even people who won't actually play them. They are the other side of the coin of Golconda as it was in 1st edition, and is an aspect of the idea that a lot of Kindred suffering is self-inflicted. Damnation is important less because you may be screwed in the afterlife (which you don't know at all), but because the <b>idea</b> of it and the self-loathing that comes fucks with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-01T18:27:10-08:00","id":1556076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556075#post1556075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First, it's not Anti-Christian. Not all Christianity abides to the idea that everyone can find salvation. Entire schisms and some heresies happened over this concept. Just remember that for most churches you need baptism to even have a chance at salvation to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I find vampire to be a game profoundly critical of Christianity and counterculture to its themes and I'm under the impression from other posts you disagree so we're probably not going to agree on this.<br /> <br /> But I disagree on your take with the Sabbat and salvation. The Sabbat are by FAR the most religious and maltheistic of the Kindred in the setting (barring the Church of Cain). The Camarilla doesn't think of salvation and damnation and the Anarchs. The Sabbat by contrast have the view that Caine's story is real, that God exists, and they are waging war on the Almighty in Caine's name as a sort of substitute for the Devil.<br /> <br /> That's my take, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-01-2025, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-01T22:05:11-08:00","id":1556083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556076#post1556076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I find vampire to be a game profoundly critical of Christianity and counterculture to its themes and I'm under the impression from other posts you disagree so we're probably not going to agree on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you're Christian and you have a somewhat hard time looking at it through other lenses, which isn't a bad thing <i>per se</i>.<br /> <br /> Vampire is an internal criticism from the beginning (<i>especially</i> in the beginning). It <b>IS</b> profoundly critical of Christianity, but the kind of criticism a Christian would make, not a criticism from the outside. I can understand it as I had a Catholic upbringing in a majority Catholic country despite ending up not being Catholic myself.<br /> <br /> So Vampire is not an Anti-Christian message by any stretch of the word, even if it is strongly against <i>a form</i> of Christianity, probably the same Bible Belt Christianity that defined your childhood, but they're far from the only way Christianity may be.<br /> <br /> Even if VtM was Anti-Christian, I will repeat that stating that Damnation may come regardless of deeds isn't Anti-Christian because it is <b><i>objectively </i></b>the stance of a lot of denominations, and it only complicates when we take into account that this is a game about vampires, so this isn't simply a matter of theology, but theology through the lenses of a fictional monster. Is the vampire really an innocent being damned against free will? Even if your character in a game is literally that, the character and the game are just metaphors and allegories, and plenty of Christian <i>fiction</i> <i>and folklore</i> has characters that fit this bill even among denominations that don't believe it.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat being religious has nothing to do with it, because this is not about the characters believing in Salvation, it is Salvation as a literary theme. What makes Salvation and Damnation core themes to the game is Humanity as a rule, and the Sabbat does not necessarily follow Humanity, the Camarilla does. Humanity is what gives weight to the idea that this condition corrodes morality and your fate is defined by the Beast at its end. Likewise, the Sabbat presents other takes because they present the interpretation <i>and rules</i> to explore the notion that you're not struggling with Damnation, you either accepted it or it doesn't lie in being humane.<br /> <br /> And the Sabbat isn't maltheistic at least since Second Edition, if it ever was. I'll ask you please to point to any canon texts, especially from before V5, that actually say that they fight YHWH.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-02T05:50:32-08:00","id":1556095,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the explanation!<br /> <br /> Much appreciated.<br /> <br /> /sincerity mode","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-02T20:01:18-08:00","id":1556109,"title":"","content":"I always imagined that most of the Sabbat practiced a variation of Christianity, or at least a sort of Abrahamic religion, where they venerate Caine and they think that God is alright with them committing evil actions for reasons. So they think that they are serving God\u2019s will in their own way. Which is why they hate infernalists so much.<br /> <br /> With regards to Paths of Enlightenment, I think I would personally prefer if they just existed in setting as cults or ideologies among vampires and not a mechanic that subverts Humanity.<br /> <br /> Instead, I think that I would tweak Humanity rules so that we can still have functional low Humanity vampires especially if they can maintain high self control and willpower. That allows for both evil Sabbat vampires and ruthless Camarilla elders who aren\u2019t dysfunctional from low Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-03T03:34:39-08:00","id":1556119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556109#post1556109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always imagined that most of the Sabbat practiced a variation of Christianity, or at least a sort of Abrahamic religion, where they venerate Caine and they think that God is alright with them committing evil actions for reasons. So they think that they are serving God\u2019s will in their own way. Which is why they hate infernalists so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what the books I've read tell, and it's definitely Christianity, I can say after having studied other Abrahamic religions in debt.<br /> <br /> While the central figure in their theology is Caine, that's just how the central figure in Christian theology is Jesus. Caine is god-like in power, but not a god, just a messianic figure of sorts. You can say the standard version is that Caine is to the Kindred what Jesus is to the Kine, although some go even further and see them as the same entity in different moments.<br /> <br /> Of course, a lot of variations exist for several reasons. The main one is that despite being a religious organization, the Sabbat is mostly whiling to ignore deviation as long as you follow a few key points in public: accept the role of Caine and participate in the Ritae. But that's essentially religious compromise from assuming that their larger goals are more important than orthodoxy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556109#post1556109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With regards to Paths of Enlightenment, I think I would personally prefer if they just existed in setting as cults or ideologies among vampires and not a mechanic that subverts Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is mostly what they are, especially after the development of Roads in DA.<br /> <br /> The mechanics are there because Humanity doesn't work for every play style, and mostly don't for the Sabbat. Especially it isn't adequate for some themes and takes that aren't core to VtM, but should be possible.<br /> <br /> I like Humanity and how it fits in the game main proposal, but I learned that this isn't the only way to play and that it really gets in the way for some concepts. And you can simply ditch the Paths as mechanics if you want, the ideologies are, indeed, the important part.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556109#post1556109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead, I think that I would tweak Humanity rules so that we can still have functional low Humanity vampires especially if they can maintain high self control and willpower. That allows for both evil Sabbat vampires and ruthless Camarilla elders who aren\u2019t dysfunctional from low Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bVtR does that in two ways. First by rewriting a lot of &quot;sins&quot;, with a goal of making this less about being nice and more about not being an inhuman predator, second with a rule for Banes where you can substitute a sin for a supernatural Flaw. From this point on, that specific sin doesn't count for you no matter what, it'll never compromise your Humanity.<br /> <br /> But I don't think either take is the superior. VtM has its own reasons to have Humanity as it is, and Paths fill a particular narrative niche, too. They're what gives weight in the game to the Sabbat as an organization devoted to philosophy and religion, as experimenters on the Kindred (and by extension, the human) condition, and the importance of fervor, faith and loyalty. Without them they're just deluded idiots dooming themselves through ideas that objectively don't work and actively hinder their ability to function.<br /> <br /> Keeping in mind that high Humanity is still important to the Camarilla elders, not because <i><b>they're</b></i>on it, but because it gives them Neonates that can fulfill a lot of roles and execute tasks that would be harder for a low Humanity Kindred. Without Paths the Sabbat would be at a clear disadvantage by not having anyone who fills those gaps.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-03T03:48:27-08:00","id":1556121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556109#post1556109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With regards to Paths of Enlightenment, I think I would personally prefer if they just existed in setting as cults or ideologies among vampires and not a mechanic that subverts Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to think <i>Chaining the Beast</i> did more or less that. You're not really subverting Humanity, you're making yourself violently mentally ill. It 'works', in the sense that you can better control the beast, but it requires you to sacrifice much of what makes life worth living. There's even a sidebar that explicitly mentions that many path followers are profoundly unhappy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-04T21:16:44-08:00","id":1556162,"title":"","content":"I never felt the appeal of Paths of Enlightenment in VTM, but if other gamers could make it work in there campaigns and that's great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T05:09:58-08:00","id":1556233,"title":"","content":"<i>Antitribu</i>Sorry for the late retort been in bed with flu.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555988#post1555988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to throw this away as much as I want to have a clearer description that doesn't induce players to think in too strict standards, which is a recurring problem with the fanbase.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's lack of clarification and the tendancy towards railroading within the writing which causes these community issues. Previous edition tacitly discouraged non 7 members of the tower for...reasons and this could be solved with something as simple as a pie chart and an explicit statement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can say which clans are most numerous and powerful as a whole in each sect without really describing it as &quot;Sect's clan&quot;, which is the source of many problems we have with both players and writers with too narrow views. In my games I had members of every clan in every sect, I had an important Giovanni elder be actually Toreador, but she was Giovanni by birth and got back to her family, I had the Primigen of a city include a Follower of Set, I had Sabbat cities with no presence of important Lasombra or Tzimisce, only Bishops of other clans, yet at no point those were standard or the overall politics of each clan about the sects meaningfully changed or got stale. </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of specific clans being culturally associated with specific sects on a general level because it leans into the social and political aspects of VTM which is what I enjoy most as long as a caveat is diversity. I do tend to have a more relaxed attitude to sect membership although I tend to ask to be 'sold' on something if it's really exotic (I've only said no twice out of 14, tellingly one was a tower lasombra)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The reason my suggestion focus on identifying all clans as Camarilla is because, at the end of the day, the Camarilla is the only sect where it matters, even if they shouldn't be. The Sabbat got everything <i>Antitribu</i> to play with, and the Anarchs weren't even organized like that to begin with, they're not a sect before V5. Having members of any clan at those two groups was all too simple, it was in the Camarilla that things got unnecessarily tricky. </div> </div> </div>I think that's more an issue with sect writting with the camarilla being the only sect which often matters (except the Sabbat in revised and 2nd) and the other sects may as well not exist in 5th. Going forward I'd actually recommend the other 3 actually become full fledged sects (again) but this is a more an issue of sect write up being bad rather than clan representation and wouldn't really be solved by making the Sabbat all <i>Antitribu</i> if anything that digs the problem deeper.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I thoroughly blame a lot of this on Marcus Vitel, as he was the first and archetypal canon example of a non-Cam clan in a Cam city. </div> </div> </div>I tend to blame the larp community who tended to have very....odd interpretations of the Lasombra which seem to be affirmed in recent writting I suppose marcus might feed into that<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's one way to look at it, but I also think it's not the best take.<br /> <br /> First of all, distinguishing the two takes as members of each sect is more interesting to me. Sure you can have inner conflict if you have both at the same place, but with two sects you make a clearer point about how distinct they are even if they're not at all as much as they think. </div> </div> </div>The trouble is don't consider it a binary, pretty much all traits I just listed could describe the dragons and the fiends can also represent to more 'honerable/noble' traits quite well. I've noticed that a lot of the writting presumes their's a meaningful distinction between tzmisce who practice flashgrafting and those who don't historically.I reality most of what could be said about one can be said about the other. We're just talking historical trends which are in turn distinct from the somewhat sloppy 5th write up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, I don't think everyone in the Cam should ascribe to Humanity, just as not every Tzimisce should be &quot;inhumane&quot;. The sect has a stance about Humanity, but it isn't really something they can or care to control as much as they want to use as propaganda. Humanity as a sect thing is something that arose in the game more as an excuse for the rules than it ever was a consequence or necessity of the game and its themes. The ST can vet or let any Path or Road, but in the fiction it doesn't make much sense for the sect to interfere so much on such personal matters as long as members follow the Traditions. </div> </div> </div>We're kinda at an impasse with that because canon says otherwise. I agree in principle but in practice , although I do think a tzmisce who is neither inhuman nor inhumane is similar to a toreador who isnt into art or socialization which is tricky if acceptable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you assume Paths exist, I really don't buy that they're so rare in the Camarilla, especially after DA made them such a big part of Vampire culture and Humanity just one among many. </div> </div> </div>See above, the problem is more severe in 5th were the paths are even more discouraged.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think they're shallower, precisely, but more on point that they're narrower. </div> </div> </div>More focused perhaps but I'm not sure of that.<br /> <br /> [qupte]Other clans have archetypes that, while simple, have room for a lot of variation without breaking with it, especially the Big Seven, but not only them. The Tzimisce have maybe the harder to play with in making different characters without breaking it. Of course, this is not a problem when you plan to break it to begin with, but as a rule of thumb the result is very same-y, most Tximisce characters that follow the clan archetype are little more than it because of how little space you have to work with.[/quote]<br /> <br /> I actually find the tzmisce about as diverse as the big 7....which is to say I don't consider the 7 that diverse.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think it has to be a mandate, and I don't think it was really a mandate for most of the game's history. </div> </div> </div>I was speaking figuratively the community has always presumed and the writers seem generally behind this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem is less to have other themes and more to be hard to have this theme if this is what you want for your game. </div> </div> </div>I haven't really found that<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As it stands, the Transhumanist Tzimisce have always been the most disruptive clan in a game that isn't made to incorporate them specifically. This is a bad thing not because their themes aren't welcome, but because you can't use them on the main type of story the setting was designed to tell, and any story that includes this theme they may get in your way. The fact you can use them for great effect if you know how doesn't change that it's an extra barrier to using them at all. </div> </div> </div>this isnt really my experience at all, the biggest problem players I've had were Tremere and Brujah who played in according to the presumed expectations of the game and in terms of consistent bad roleplayers Carmarilla Lasombra stand out<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other than that, what exploring Humanity means? It can be a lot of things, and people like the typical Lasombra who revel in vampirism are still doing that, it's a foil. Characters that aren't quite human, or not human at all, can still explore aspects of humanity either by augmenting them, contrasting them, or showing them in a purer form (like human greed without other human aspects that check it). Even if this isn't the goal, most &quot;inhuman&quot; characters are still quite human. </div> </div> </div>Well that's one my meta criticisms of vtm it's a bit to vague on what humanity actually is and then subtly pushes back against so we're told it's flexible even when it's not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When you strive to make a character as inhuman as possible, you're prone to actually end up with an individual character that's too shallow because too much energy goes on <i>not being</i> instead of <i>being</i> something, and you'll still probably miss the point as you end up with something <i>you</i> think as inhuman, but other people may seem as too much human silliness. And that's how I feel with the Transhumanist Tzimisce.\u200b </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's really true and it doesn't match my experiences. My most memorable Garou was a lupus were I leaned hard into their alien nature for example.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T10:54:11-08:00","id":1556251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556233#post1556233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for the late retort been in bed with flu.</div> </div> </div> </div>No prob, happens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556233#post1556233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Previous edition tacitly discouraged non 7 members of the tower for...reasons and this could be solved with something as simple as a pie chart and an explicit statement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Balance.<br /> <br /> At the time we were at the height of the notion of balance as a strict necessity and quite fragile.<br /> <br /> This certainly affected a number of decisions back them that trickled down in this state of things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556233#post1556233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of specific clans being culturally associated with specific sects on a general level because it leans into the social and political aspects of VTM which is what I enjoy most as long as a caveat is diversity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the same, I just think we could tackle it the other way around: instead of emphasizing tradition and then adding diversity in the explanation, I'd first emphasize diversity and then add tradition.<br /> <br /> The end goal is about the same.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556233#post1556233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's more an issue with sect writting with the camarilla being the only sect which often matters (except the Sabbat in revised and 2nd) and the other sects may as well not exist in 5th.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Anarchs do, even if they're boring. So much so that we had this distribution of clans between NuCam and Anarchs. Sabbat is more a case of active persecution by the devs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556233#post1556233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going forward I'd actually recommend the other 3 actually become full fledged sects (again) but this is a more an issue of sect write up being bad rather than clan representation and wouldn't really be solved by making the Sabbat all <i>Antitribu</i> if anything that digs the problem deeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the concept of sect is partially the problem, but overall I agree, except I don't think the Anarchs should be a sect, I don't think they should be a formal entity.<br /> <br /> And my point with <i>Antitribu</i> is about rethinking what the word even means. As is, it presupposes a huge level of cohesion on Clan policy, so much so that you have to clearly mark a clan member that isn't following the official stance, or that opposes it directly. My idea is to resignify it as a Sabbat moniker indicating their rejection of elders and traditional distinctions, as a faction where your loyalty to your Pack is above your loyalty to your clan (as is the Sabbat philosophy even when it isn't it's practice).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556233#post1556233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to blame the larp community who tended to have very....odd interpretations of the Lasombra which seem to be affirmed in recent writting I suppose marcus might feed into that</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think the opposite, because we're not talking the same problem, I think.<br /> <br /> Marcus Vitel is a problem because he became the to go example of how a member of a non-Cam clan has to live in a Cam city: as a secret, hiding his true bloodline, pretending to be one of the Seven as only the Seven were accepted. That, more than anything else, solidified the <i>perception</i> of the Camarilla as exclusionary instead of inclusive. It's a part of a bigger trend where early <i>By Night</i> books gave too specific examples of how the setting could be, and they became the standard way it is, followed by both players and later writers.<br /> <br /> LARP may be full of bad Lasombra roleplayers, but it still helped to cement at least the idea of the Lasombra not being exclusively Sabbat.<br /> <br /> And the Sabbat got on top of that the <i>Antitribu</i> treatment, in that instead of being limited to two main clans, it became consistently filled with members of every clan and almost every bloodline through &quot;schismatic factions&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556233#post1556233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The trouble is don't consider it a binary, pretty much all traits I just listed could describe the dragons and the fiends can also represent to more 'honerable/noble' traits quite well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I don't, but trends matter.<br /> <br /> Even if they don't force individuals into conformity, they establish larger thematic proposals OoC and political positions IC.<br /> <br /> The very cultural associations of the clans are exactly that, they're trends and archetypes, even if they're not actual binaries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556233#post1556233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've noticed that a lot of the writting presumes their's a meaningful distinction between tzmisce who practice flashgrafting and those who don't historically.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's DSotBH, basically, as the take on them as voivodes was basically born out of Old Clan. I think it's a nice historical piece, but ultimately they certainly blend a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556233#post1556233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually find the tzmisce about as diverse as the big 7....which is to say I don't consider the 7 that diverse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do, at least when dealing with traditional pre-DA transhumanist Sabbat fleshcrafters.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556233#post1556233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that's one my meta criticisms of vtm it's a bit to vague on what humanity actually is and then subtly pushes back against so we're told it's flexible even when it's not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but I was talking about humanity as a focus of literary exploration rather than Humanity the Rule.<br /> <br /> Paths are also ways to explore themes of humanity, for example, both directly and as foils.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556233#post1556233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's really true and it doesn't match my experiences. My most memorable Garou was a lupus were I leaned hard into their alien nature for example.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking the difference between leaning into &quot;inhuman&quot; and trying too hard to be &quot;inhuman&quot; at any cost, all the time.<br /> <br /> What does inhuman means? For a lot of <i>Necroscope</i>-like Tzimisce IME it means shock for shock's sake and antagonizing &quot;human standards&quot; all the time without a personal drive beyond that.<br /> <br /> And because they're &quot;inhuman through antithesis&quot;, that is, try to be inhuman by being what the player thinks to be the opposite of human, they end up not only being quite samey, but also looking more like edgy teenagers trying to assert themselves, even if through extremes, which is an all-too-human behavior.<br /> <br /> But then again, our experiences may differ for many reasons, including key differences in perception, as I have a very critical take on what &quot;human&quot; means.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T12:49:30-08:00","id":1556263,"title":"","content":"I also think having the Antitribu be a moniker used by all Sabbat clans could help simplify matters and, as others have mentioned, it would certainly jive with the historical Sabbat philosophy of \u201cactually clan-loyalty above all else was Bad\u2122\ufe0f and it was used as a tool of the elders to enslave us, we should abandon it for the unity of Caine\u2019s Sabbath\u201d.<br /> <br /> That said I do think there\u2019s an interesting wrinkle that comes in from the trajectory of Sabbat history we get sketched out, with that attitude being more or less explicitly the feeling of the anarchic proto-Sabbat and their ideological descendants in the Loyalist faction. However I do think the notion of the significant chunk of Lasombra and Tzimisce elders who joined the sect in its early nights bringing a more conservative attitude that has endured adds an interesting element, where despite their lip service we see these elders not wanting to have to <i>actually </i>give up the benefits of clan power, especially if we interpret their addition as being largely due to a significant clique of Lasombra elders viewing the Tower as a Brujah-Toreador-Ventrue conspiracy.<br /> <br /> This element also has an important effect on the Pander question IMO. The Pander\u2019s whole story takes place in the strange narrative gray area where the Sabbat has just enough of its original ideology left to allow self-conscious Caitiff organization to exist and gain structural power but also enough traditionalism to have significant sections of the sect view the phenomena with extreme distrust and hostility.<br /> <br /> I do think one could square this circle though, by having Anttitribu be embraced as a pan-Sabbat moniker while noting that internally the Conservative faction (which has disproportionate influence on the College of Cardinals and the Pricii) practices many pre-Sabbat traditions and customs in secret and to maintain clan-oriented patronage and power networks within the sect (particularly among the Lasombra but also among the minority of elders who defected from other clans).<br /> <br /> Also, this may be a hot-take: I think it makes more sense to emphasis the Lasombra as the poster-child for this phenomena than the Tzimisce. The way the lore developed with the split between flesh-crafter Tzimisce and the Old Clan, it makes more sense IMO for the Tzimisce Antitribu to be true Sabbat in their ideology (given that they\u2019re probably descended from the Tzimisce who rebelled against the Old Clan\u2019s use of Dark Ages style customs and methods of domination). That said, I do like the idea of the Tzimisce being the most <i>spiritually </i>conservative clan. If we keep the idea that the Vinniculum was discovered by the Tzimisce before being spread throughout the Anarch Revolts, I think the idea of the Sabbat Tzimisce remaining significantly dedicated to the esoteric doctrines of the cults that originally developed and distributed the ritual, and that those occult doctrines should probably be emphasized as one of the major influences on the development of the Sabbat\u2019s belief system and ideology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T12:54:28-08:00","id":1556264,"title":"","content":"If I can be forgiven for doing necromancy on the Gangrel topic after the thread has moved on: while I agree that the clan doesn't have a real chain of command, I never had a problem buying the idea of a mass exodus happening from the grassroots up after word would have spread at the various Gathers that one of the oldest and most respected members of the clan still stalking the night met what seemed to be an Antediluvian in combat, was lucky to escape with his unlife after the rest of a Gather was wiped out, and was met with derision by the Ivory Tower's leadership. <br /> <br /> In an edition focused on the countdown to Gehenna, it sets the tone that the Gangrel have spread the word among their own that the Antediluvians are real and that the Cammies are either too blind to see it or are covering for the ancients.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T00:59:43-08:00","id":1556281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556264#post1556264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I can be forgiven for doing necromancy on the Gangrel topic .</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider yourself forgiven <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> My problem is this reasoning the fact, Vampires... are Humans<br /> Or at least <i>were </i>Humans, except some extreme cases of the Abominations and Maeghar, who are still Embraced kinain or changeling (tho' you can argue, they had enough &quot;Human&quot; in them)<br /> But the point is, most if not all of the Vampire at the end of the day are essentially? Humans who ended up on the busieness end of a fang and became/forced to become what they are<br /> The keyworld is human<br /> As a human, especially a loner... not really gives a shit whats happened and why<br /> Even if the Gangrel deveop some pack-like mentality, some old geezer on the other part of the world got a hissy fit - or more likely screwed by big time and got his team killed and possibly trying to save face and after a temper tantrum &quot;left&quot;.<br /> 'kay?<br /> Move on<br /> I doubt if you were a run-of-the-mill Gangrel who got bitten and left alone to care of yourself, your Sire barely if not really tought you and you have to &quot;prove&quot;' yoruself, have to survive and crave out a little place for yourself in the society... would you give that all up because Professor X got butthurt?<br /> Nope, I don't think so<br /> I certainly would not<br /> <br /> The Brujah thing is more or less understandable and reasonable but for the Gangrel and for such a reason...? Eh, not really","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T02:37:22-08:00","id":1556282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556251#post1556251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No prob, happens.<br /> <br /> <br /> Balance.<br /> <br /> At the time we were at the height of the notion of balance as a strict necessity and quite fragile.<br /> <br /> This certainly affected a number of decisions back them that trickled down in this state of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly, we don't actually know why. Balance isnt a particularity persuasive argument since it didn't even really exist. It spoke more to stagnancy to me than anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the same, I just think we could tackle it the other way around: instead of emphasizing tradition and then adding diversity in the explanation, I'd first emphasize diversity and then add tradition.<br /> <br /> The end goal is about the same. </div> </div> </div>Yes I think we're mostly in concord, the distinctions are quite low level.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Anarchs do, even if they're boring. So much so that we had this distribution of clans between NuCam and Anarchs. Sabbat is more a case of active persecution by the devs. </div> </div> </div>Kinda the Anarchs barely exist in v5 since they're more an aesthetic, de facto clan distribution and presumption of play, I'd be hesitant to call them a sect in the same sense as the camarilla or 2/3rd ed Sabbat. you're spot on about the Sabbat however.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the concept of sect is partially the problem, but overall I agree, except I don't think the Anarchs should be a sect, I don't think they should be a formal entity. </div> </div> </div>Maybe, imo the problem with the anarchs in 5th is the non-committal nature of what they did. The 5th ed anarchs book should have been something simular to revised Sabbat or Guide to the technocracy, what we got was an series of articles on vampire fashion and a podcast extract based on a social justice power fantasy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And my point with <i>Antitribu</i> is about rethinking what the word even means. As is, it presupposes a huge level of cohesion on Clan policy, so much so that you have to clearly mark a clan member that isn't following the official stance, or that opposes it directly. My idea is to re signify it as a Sabbat moniker indicating their rejection of elders and traditional distinctions, as a faction where your loyalty to your Pack is above your loyalty to your clan (as is the Sabbat philosophy even when it isn't it's practice). </div> </div> </div>I'd say it's more an implicit of clan culture than policy, clans despite the desires of 5th have cultural attitudes and outlooks. I don't really like the Sabbat no-clan ideology since the interpretation of clan through sect is typically very interesting and it's mostly just used as a way of removing personality from the individual vampires. when I run Sabbat i tend to run the sect as clan neutral were it's something a vampire can choose to engage with or not,I've always preffered to have cake and eat it, especially with the rick lore available with the clans belonging to specific sects.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I actually think the opposite, because we're not talking the same problem, I think.<br /> <br /> Marcus Vitel is a problem because he became the to go example of how a member of a non-Cam clan has to live in a Cam city: as a secret, hiding his true bloodline, pretending to be one of the Seven as only the Seven were accepted. That, more than anything else, solidified the <i>perception</i> of the Camarilla as exclusionary instead of inclusive. It's a part of a bigger trend where early <i>By Night</i> books gave too specific examples of how the setting could be, and they became the standard way it is, followed by both players and later writers. </div> </div> </div>I see your point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> LARP may be full of bad Lasombra roleplayers, but it still helped to cement at least the idea of the Lasombra not being exclusively Sabbat.<br /> <br /> And the Sabbat got on top of that the <i>Antitribu</i> treatment, in that instead of being limited to two main clans, it became consistently filled with members of every clan and almost every bloodline through &quot;schismatic factions&quot;. </div> </div> </div>True although tabletop lasombra players havnt exactly been stellar-I've encountered one good one so far.<br /> <br /> Yes and that was a nice balance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, I don't, but trends matter. </div> </div> </div>So I'm told but, to be candid these sorts of things should be addressed through good writting rather than tacitly re-enforced as in 5th..<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's DSotBH, basically, as the take on them as voivodes was basically born out of Old Clan. I think it's a nice historical piece, but ultimately they certainly blend a lot. </div> </div> </div>The trouble is it isnt really the take from DSotBH, it's made very clear in that book that the old clan are as inhuman are horrific as the mainstreme even with subtle aesthetics differences. The 5th is closer to a missremberance combined with a pop culture understanding or Dracula. Which is very v5.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do, at least when dealing with traditional pre-DA transhumanist Sabbat fleshcrafters. </div> </div> </div>Then we're at an impasse, i sincerely don't consider several of the cam clans deeper than the other 7.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, but I was talking about humanity as a focus of literary exploration rather than Humanity the Rule. </div> </div> </div>The trouble is they're intrinsically linked in the game because the mechanics are how that it's reflected on the table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Paths are also ways to explore themes of humanity, for example, both directly and as foils. </div> </div> </div>kinda, we're obviously caught in the problem we don't really have a good framework from inhuman sapience I also don't think you strictly have to do that<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm talking the difference between leaning into &quot;inhuman&quot; and trying too hard to be &quot;inhuman&quot; at any cost, all the time. </div> </div> </div>I agree the tzmisce are the most extreme end of the curve on this but that's fine to me, several other clans and paths explore inhumanity and alien natures the tzmisce (the lasombra for example revel in vamparism in an arguable more relatable way) just express it to an extreme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What does inhuman means? For a lot of <i>Necroscope</i>-like Tzimisce IME it means shock for shock's sake and antagonizing &quot;human standards&quot; all the time without a personal drive beyond that.<br /> <br /> And because they're &quot;inhuman through antithesis&quot;, that is, try to be inhuman by being what the player thinks to be the opposite of human, they end up not only being quite samey, but also looking more like edgy teenagers trying to assert themselves, even if through extremes, which is an all-too-human behavior.<br /> <br /> But then again, our experiences may differ for many reasons, including key differences in perception, as I have a very critical take on what &quot;human&quot; means.\u200b </div> </div> </div><br /> It certainly has a strong aesthetic and is quite uncomfortable but I think it works, it's horrific and repulsive but becomes trite through over use, like a Ventrue shit head prince becomes a bore after the 50th one. but it is a nice solid framework for the clan and a good jumping off point for the deeper dive. The Shorthalt Postulate works very well with the fiends even when they're badly written and I've yet to see a bad one in a long term play.<br /> <br /> <br /> I mostly struggle with vtm idealizing humanity but being a little vague on what it is, especially in 5th.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T18:11:36-08:00","id":1556323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556264#post1556264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In an edition focused on the countdown to Gehenna, it sets the tone that the Gangrel have spread the word among their own that the Antediluvians are real and that the Cammies are either too blind to see it or are covering for the ancients.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does and it was probably the reasoning behind it in <i>Revised</i>, but then what?<br /> <br /> The bigger problem here is that we're not given what they actually <b>did</b> then, or which form did this defection took.<br /> <br /> Are they all moving to the wilderness? Are they trying to take their own cities? Are they traveling and spreading the word while hiding from local authorities?<br /> <br /> Mass exodus is fine. The problem is this mass exodus having a result that makes no sense (why didn't the Cam just name a new Gangrel Justicar among those who remained and call it a day?) and being to the Land of Nowhere, with all those Gangrel just vanishing from the game.<br /> <br /> Not to say that &quot;mass exodus&quot; is a relative term. I can picture a lot of Gangrel being moved by that for a given value of &quot;a lot&quot;. I can't really buy something like an entire fifth or more of the clan doing so, because no elder is that important, the news wouldn't reach most of them, few of them even think in terms of &quot;clan&quot; and are ok as long as their own respect is intact, and so on.<br /> <br /> With an actual explanation and elaboration on what happened that gives meaning to the phrase &quot;left the Camarilla&quot; and actually makes something with the clan, it may be a good plot.<br /> <br /> But what we got was &quot;the Gangrel doesn't count as a Cam clan anymore, except all Gangrel you encounter will still be Cam as normal&quot;.<br /> <br /> You as an ST can make a lot with their movement as stated in <i>Revised</i>, but as is in the books, it's meaningless BS.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a> I intent on making a proper response later, and I agree with most of your take, it's just that this will take a lot of energy and I'm in a really bad day in this regard. Will see the Psychiatrist tomorrow, but it's probably burnout.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T17:34:44-08:00","id":1556420,"title":"","content":"One thing that makes me laugh. The Gangrel find out that the Antideluivans are real and decide that the Camarilla isn't doing enough to oppose them so they decide to leave the Camarilla. The Lasombra find out that their killing of the Lasombra Antideluvian didn't succeed so they decide to leave the Sabbat and join the Camarilla...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T01:11:16-08:00","id":1556424,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556420#post1556420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Lasombra find out that their killing of the Lasombra Antideluvian didn't succeed so they decide to leave the Sabbat and join the Camarilla...</div> </div> </div> </div>That was the official reason tho'?<br /> <br /> I was under the impression the Lasombra jumped ship because their power base and influence erroded as the Sabbat basically crumbled around them and they came to the conclusion the Camarilla was a more stable, powerful structure to survive and regain control<br /> Basically Political Pragmatism with a healthy dose of Social Darwinism fuelled by the de faco faliure of the Gehenna War, the harassment from the Second Inquisition and the fact the Sabbat own internal conflicts kinda tore the sect apart and the Lasombra's love of rigid structure never really took root<br /> <br /> At the end of the day the Sabbat was their instrument, their &quot;pet project&quot;...<br /> ...but it <i>failed </i><br /> And the one thing the Lasombra can't tolerate is <i>faliure</i><br /> <br /> Those in the Sabbat - and mind you there were tons of Lasombra all over the sects, notably the Ashirra and even in the Camarilla from day 1 - not joined the Camarilla because they were \u201cmortal enemies\u201d but just because the Camarilla seemed to be a worse option.<br /> Why join a club controlled mostly (or nominally) by Ventrue and Toreador that forces you to deny your vampiric nature when you can have your own club where you can do what ever you like?<br /> The Sabbat was simply better.<br /> Sure the Sabbat conceptually <i>can not be ruled</i>, but Lasombra are masters of manipulation and pulling the strings. They controlled the uncontrollable.<br /> Or tried to<br /> With the Gehenna War the fanatics molded the Sabbat from a comfortable \u201cdo as you like\u201d to a \u201cthose who are not with as are against as\u201d attitude. They demanded that every true Sabbat has to march with them in their war against the Antedeluvian and other old vampires - and many Lasombra in the Sabbat were old geezers themselves<br /> I thought that was the dealbreaker; any Lasombra worth their salt had actually no interest to give up their possessions and influence to die in a war they were actually not interested in.<br /> Suddenly, the the Kings and Queens of Shadows who were mostly humanity based and the end of the foodchain saw the opportunity and made a move - and the Amici Noctis (and if I recall correctly Montano never left it, he was always the member) kept them around <i>for exactly like that</i>. And to mitigate degeneration in the Clan.<br /> Just in case.<br /> They had back up plans long in place, they manipulated the entire clan on a wide scale<br /> <br /> The Camarilla was desperate for allies... and itself changed a bit, like banning technology (curiously the Lasombra had problem with Technology... and Montano always had a voice in the Camarilla... I wonder the two are related or not...) and became something the Lasombra prefer<br /> But at the end of the day? The Sabbat <i>failed</i> and any Lasombra truly supporting the Sect - most of the Lasombra never truly been Sabbat if you look closely; using it as a power base, ruling and taking power from it, but paying lip service in large part. So when suddenly the Sect degenerated basically a mindless swarm of locusts, giving up clan identity, completely turning from humanity, and went to war in full force with the same effectiveness as World War I. tactics of sending wave after wave of soldiers to attack the nigh untouchable Machine Gunners on ridges, the Amici Noctis clearly saw that now was the time to leave and anyone who stayed just proved they lack the survival instinct that defined their Clan - also <i>failed</i><br /> <br /> And io and behold! All Lasombra who joins the Camarilla are required to prove that they killed at least one non-Camarilla Lasombra to earn their way in...<br /> ...so they not even got a new cozy powerbase - providing the Camarilla some influence in the Church - but got rid of those who proved themselves to be <i>failures </i><br /> If this is not the most Lasombra thing you can think of I don't know what is","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":".  Gramar and typos 12-10-2025, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T08:23:19-08:00","id":1556428,"title":"","content":"I always assumed that Montano had a seat in the Inner Circle of the Camarilla<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T12:19:52-08:00","id":1556436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556424#post1556424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That was the official reason tho'?<br /> <br /> I was under the impression the Lasombra jumped ship because their power base and influence erroded as the Sabbat basically crumbled around them and they came to the conclusion the Camarilla was a more stable, powerful structure to survive and regain control<br /> Basically Political Pragmatism with a healthy dose of Social Darwinism fuelled by the de faco faliure of the Gehenna War, the harassment from the Second Inquisition and the fact the Sabbat own internal conflicts kinda tore the sect apart and the Lasombra's love of rigid structure never really took root<br /> <br /> At the end of the day the Sabbat was their instrument, their &quot;pet project&quot;...<br /> ...but it <i>failed </i><br /> And the one thing the Lasombra can't tolerate is <i>faliure</i><br /> <br /> Those in the Sabbat - and mind you there were tons of Lasombra all over the sects, notably the Ashirra and even in the Camarilla from day 1 - not joined the Camarilla because they were \u201cmortal enemies\u201d but just because the Camarilla seemed to be a worse option.<br /> Why join a club controlled mostly (or nominally) by Ventrue and Toreador that forces you to deny your vampiric nature when you can have your own club where you can do what ever you like?<br /> The Sabbat was simply better.<br /> Sure the Sabbat conceptually <i>can not be ruled</i>, but Lasombra are masters of manipulation and pulling the strings. They controlled the uncontrollable.<br /> Or tried to<br /> With the Gehenna War the fanatics molded the Sabbat from a comfortable \u201cdo as you like\u201d to a \u201cthose who are not with as are against as\u201d attitude. They demanded that every true Sabbat has to march with them in their war against the Antedeluvian and other old vampires - and many Lasombra in the Sabbat were old geezers themselves<br /> I thought that was the dealbreaker; any Lasombra worth their salt had actually no interest to give up their possessions and influence to die in a war they were actually not interested in.<br /> Suddenly, the the Kings and Queens of Shadows who were mostly humanity based and the end of the foodchain saw the opportunity and made a move - and the Amici Noctis (and if I recall correctly Montano never left it, he was always the member) kept them around <i>for exactly like that</i>. And to mitigate degeneration in the Clan.<br /> Just in case.<br /> They had back up plans long in place, they manipulated the entire clan on a wide scale<br /> <br /> The Camarilla was desperate for allies... and itself changed a bit, like banning technology (curiously the Lasombra had problem with Technology... and Montano always had a voice in the Camarilla... I wonder the two are related or not...) and became something the Lasombra prefer<br /> But at the end of the day? The Sabbat <i>failed</i> and any Lasombra truly supporting the Sect - most of the Lasombra never truly been Sabbat if you look closely; using it as a power base, ruling and taking power from it, but paying lip service in large part. So when suddenly the Sect degenerated basically a mindless swarm of locusts, giving up clan identity, completely turning from humanity, and went to war in full force with the same effectiveness as World War I. tactics of sending wave after wave of soldiers to attack the nigh untouchable Machine Gunners on ridges, the Amici Noctis clearly saw that now was the time to leave and anyone who stayed just proved they lack the survival instinct that defined their Clan - also <i>failed</i><br /> <br /> And io and behold! All Lasombra who joins the Camarilla are required to prove that they killed at least one non-Camarilla Lasombra to earn their way in...<br /> ...so they not even got a new cozy powerbase - providing the Camarilla some influence in the Church - but got rid of those who proved themselves to be <i>failures </i><br /> If this is not the most Lasombra thing you can think of I don't know what is</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you basically have it down here and the problem a lot of players had with the whole thing, aside from the fact it is a HUGE shift (and gamers are wonderfully tolerant of that between editions /s) is the fact that they have pretty simple reasons for what they're doing and people are accustomed to expecting something much bigger and more complex.<br /> <br /> The Gehenna War was all about the Sabbat actually living up to the promises of going after the Antediluvians or at least old as shit vampires akin to the ones in Diablerie: Mexico and Diablerie: Britain. It wasn't about fighting the Camarilla for territory and power while making vague promises that all of this was going to some day bring freedom.<br /> <br /> And the Lasombra's leadership saw that the Ancients were REAL or at least actually waking up like Ur-Shulgi and other things that remembered the days before the oceans drank Atlantis and the Rise of the Sons of Aras.<br /> <br /> So they were OUT OF THERE.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla openly embracing Gehenna Cults and dark mysticism also meant that was a lot easier. I'm not sure that 5th Edition Humanity and Paths are so different either because so much of the former is now horribly evil either.<br /> <br /> In the end, it was always, &quot;Why did the televangelist not agree to go on a Crusade where they might get killed once there was an actual Crusade?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T18:09:30-08:00","id":1556452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556436#post1556436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the problem a lot of players had with the whole thing, aside from the fact it is a HUGE shift (and gamers are wonderfully tolerant of that between editions /s) is the fact that they have pretty simple reasons for what they're doing and people are accustomed to expecting something much bigger and more complex.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one I can remember was severely against the shift, most didn't even consider this a big shift at all. You're misrepresenting all the discussions on the subject we had at this forums.<br /> <br /> What people complain about the defection is the <i>process</i>, not their reasons or that it happened. If anything their reasons are actually over-complicated, but the process even more so.<br /> <br /> Your depiction of the conditions for the defection as a master move is simply delusional. They're bad, they're the kind of thing you open up negotiations with either as a joke or anyway expecting it to be dismissed because it is obviously beyond bad.<br /> <br /> The <b>Lasombra</b> aren't super-vampires and the number of eliminated elders asked was ridiculously high. The idea of a third of the clan finishing another third in days or weeks like that and not being caught in the process is insane, not even the Assamites would manage that scale of high profile assassination. Not even if it was years, as stretching the time frame makes finding them out even more likely. There's no way of cutting it where those terms aren't insane.<br /> <br /> Same goes for the idea that the <b>Lasombra</b> kept their wealth. Most of the wealth of a vampire is like the wealth of a mafia boss, it's not a bank account in their name, it's a network of property of all kinds kept through proxies. You don't just run from the city in the middle of the night with pursuers on your heels and leaving bigger and angry bosses behind and really expect to still have access to all your things, the idea that they not only kept their things but actually took the wealth of their victims is complete nonsense. Have you ever heard of frozen or expropriated assets? Criminals fleeing the country may manage to still be rich, but they don't get to leave with everything they had and more, much less when what they have of more valuable is land/Domain.<br /> <br /> It's a plot that says the <b>Lasombra</b> are refugees yet somehow are in a stronger position than before or just as strong. That's not how refugees work at all and is even disrespectful with actual refugees. It's perfectly acceptable the idea that the clan expects this decision to pay out in the long run, but as it happened it's just bad writing all over the place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T19:51:38-08:00","id":1556458,"title":"","content":"Basically, monteparnas described my opinion on the matter. I really like the idea of the Lasombra in the Camarilla. It was they way that they entered that bugged me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T22:25:38-08:00","id":1556461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your depiction of the conditions for the defection as a master move is simply delusional. They're bad, they're the kind of thing you open up negotiations with either as a joke or anyway expecting it to be dismissed because it is obviously beyond bad. </div> </div> </div>I'm a little confused because my point was that the initial request was to open the door and they absolutely wouldn't be using those terms definitely. They just needed the initial agreement because after that everything became negotiable and I suggested how.<br /> <br /> This is also not fanon on my part but something in the text.<br /> <br /> It's like the old Winston Churchhill joke,<br /> <br /> &quot;Would you sleep with me for a million pounds?&quot;<br /> &quot;Yes.&quot; &quot;How about a hundred?&quot;<br /> &quot;What kind of girl do you think I am?&quot;<br /> &quot;We've established that, now we're negotiating price.&quot;<br /> <br /> They just needed to establish agents within the Camarilla to facilitate their egress and create precedent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T13:34:55-08:00","id":1556484,"title":"","content":"While i didnt like the process of the defection i also didnt like the defection itself. The lasombra are very very sabbat and their write up in 5th doesnt really do the clan justice on a number of levels. While i dont particulary object to any clan having a presence the lasombra defection doesnt do anything for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T17:55:40-08:00","id":1556489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556461#post1556461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little confused because my point was that the initial request was to open the door and they absolutely wouldn't be using those terms definitely.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, this is not what the books say. Quite the opposite, while conditions varied from Domain to Domain, the initial request set the tone and the standard others would use to measure their own demands.<br /> <br /> Second, the Sabbat was going to war. Time was of the essence. There is no &quot;later&quot; here, later they would be either dead or in the midst of a war zone anywhere in the world (or, initially, in the Middle East).<br /> <br /> Third, you say as if there was further negotiation. It's clearly stated that this didn't happen even there, it had nothing to do with this joke. They offered a million and then just accepted it, and everyone else was forced to accept something similar, with variance coming from the whims of other Princes and not from negotiation of any sort.<br /> <br /> And forth, the text doesn't say they did a master move of some sort, and I was very clear about what I was calling delusional in your position. It's this assumption that they did great because they're Lasombra and they can only have done great.<br /> <br /> Overall the canon in this is stupid, and we don't think it's stupid because we don't want changes, it's stupid because it was under ludicrous conditions that make no sense, neither that they accepted (much less offered), nor that they pulled it off. Your fanon that's BS is the idea that in secret they're laughing of all this because this was such a good idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556484#post1556484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While i didnt like the process of the defection i also didnt like the defection itself. The lasombra are very very sabbat and their write up in 5th doesnt really do the clan justice on a number of levels. While i dont particulary object to any clan having a presence the lasombra defection doesnt do anything for the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's far from a solely Lasombra problem, but the defection makes sense once we assume that everything else the 5th did is true.<br /> <br /> So... yeah, the Lasombra are very Sabbat <i>in the old Sabbat</i>. In V5's Sabbat? Only a lunatic would stay there, it's a lost cause.<br /> <br /> And that's why for me the defection makes sense as a refugee situation, as they need to leave and to find someone that can protect them from that bunch of mindless zealot idiots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T20:22:35-08:00","id":1556498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556436#post1556436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Lasombra's leadership saw that the Ancients were REAL or at least actually waking up like Ur-Shulgi and other things that remembered the days before the oceans drank Atlantis and the Rise of the Sons of Aras.<br /> <br /> So they were OUT OF THERE.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly what I find amusing. After centuries of fighting against the ancients, when they find out that everything they were fighting for (and against) was absolutely true, they decide to run away and join the Camarilla and hope those ancients will forgive them instead of eating them. Basically they decided to try and brush off the last 500+ years as an elaborate prank and hope that they wouldn't get in any trouble from Lasombra or other elder vampires for it. <br /> <br /> That's funny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T22:09:22-08:00","id":1556502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556489#post1556489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's far from a solely Lasombra problem, but the defection makes sense once we assume that everything else the 5th did is true.<br /> <br /> So... yeah, the Lasombra are very Sabbat <i>in the old Sabbat</i>. In V5's Sabbat? Only a lunatic would stay there, it's a lost cause.<br /> <br /> And that's why for me the defection makes sense as a refugee situation, as they need to leave and to find someone that can protect them from that bunch of mindless zealot idiots.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True but thats an the reaction to v5 writting on the sabbat in universe and doesnt really address the writting problem that the lasombra are very very sabbat. We'd still have this issue if say the carmarilla imploded so the ventrue and toreador as typically written joined the sabbat in v5 but inverted for example.<br /> <br /> <br /> ....the v5 write up for the sabbat is such a mess. ..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T22:22:13-08:00","id":1556504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556498#post1556498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is exactly what I find amusing. After centuries of fighting against the ancients, when they find out that everything they were fighting for (and against) was absolutely true, they decide to run away and join the Camarilla and hope those ancients will forgive them instead of eating them. Basically they decided to try and brush off the last 500+ years as an elaborate prank and hope that they wouldn't get in any trouble from Lasombra or other elder vampires for it.<br /> <br /> That's funny.</div> </div> </div> </div>The obvious issue is a lot of princes are going to go &quot;lol no.&quot; Because that's a really good idea, the lasombra defectors are explicitly not loyal to the tower, have resumed the internal issues which caused the 1st revolt but worse and they don't really contribute anything except maybe street muscle.<br /> <br /> if im prince at best im going to allow them in and wait for attricion to whittle them down and the minute i catch a whiff of them getting uppity im going to purge them as sabbat spies and frankly im probably not going to be that nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T08:34:46-08:00","id":1556515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1556502#post1556502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True but thats an the reaction to v5 writting on the sabbat in universe and doesnt really address the writting problem that the lasombra are very very sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>But at this point it's just throwing away all V5 lore. Which I do think is a good idea and is what I do shamelessly, but then it doesn't address the change at all.<br /> <br /> As far as analyzing the change goes, I can only look at it from the greater perspective of its own context.<br /> <br /> The bigger problem is beyond doubt what they did to the Sabbat. But once the old Sabbat isn't on the table anymore, where do the Lasombra better fit in among the actual options?<br /> <br /> Not to say I actually think it's a great change. Overall I think they're a good addition to the Cam as <i>a presence that matters</i>, but their main body should remain Sabbat. Beyond this analysis I simply don't use V5 beyond a few ideas taken as inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-19T16:28:41-08:00","id":1556847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555451#post1555451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect you can draw a direct line from Point A (defining things with city books and supplements) to Point B in the Chronicles of Darkness where it's a toolbox rather than anything actually being defined.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like both styles can be valid, zig-zagging between them depending on the occasion, often in the same chronicle - or even story arc between sessions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But when you write a citybook to describe/define a particular place you have to be extra careful with what you present in the book, <i><b>because it will be referenced</b></i> - no it will be THE starting reference point for players, STs or just afficionados reading a book for fun, for good and for ill. One bad slip of improvisation because you had no time or interest in researching the place or had terrible luck with the sources used and you end with stuff that bothers or offends present or future buyers-players in a place you as writer had little familiarity or experience with. And people will still give you crap over that mistake decades later. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also the reason i always went &quot;200% pulpy dark fantasy&quot; with the clans and their roots, with emphasis on Ravnos as wanderers, rogues, ilusionists &amp; tricksters instead of just romani (or later indian), Assamites as hashassin, zealots, political assassins &amp; vigilantes (and in the last decade, Assassins' Creed) across the ages, the Followers of Shesha in India &amp; much of Southeast Asia and so on, among other bits to blur geographic lines and confuse things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555451#post1555451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, even Outstar hates some of it because she is Polish and doesn't like the Tzimisce.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familiar with her work but would really like to hear on the perspective of a VtM developer and fan of polish origin on the Tzimisce.<br /> (While myself brazilian, my departed dear grandma on paternal side was from what today is Moldova - <b>so i nearly passed out from nonstop laughing</b> when i first saw Baba Yaga in the original A World of Darkness as a teenager back in '90s)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1555451#post1555451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both sides have their adherents but the reason I love V:TM is its lore and NPCs but I understand that it limits your ability to define your home area or area you'd like to game.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Some bits are better than others. Gratiano in S\u00e3o Paulo\u200b or superpowerful &amp; superbland Oradea-boss Hedeon Yaroslavich (in Poland, for reasons) are the kind of thing that for me always felt like more tacked-on &amp; hastily thrown disservice instead of added content. And it's not for any particular dislike of either clan, have in fact used lots of NPCs from either (though when thinking &quot;what is there on Poland in WoD for a polish gamer to hate the Tzimisce? Oh, Hedeon&quot; was the first thing to cross my mind) and every clan has some embarrassing samples of regionalization.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-31-2026, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-16T15:19:17-08:00","id":1557688,"title":"","content":"You mean besides the <b>entirety of 5th edition?</b> Like, literally, you could give me ANY subject regarding the current state of the game, and I could tear tear it apart.<br /> <br /> But for the sake of convenience regarding the question, I'll give some basic examples.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Assamites:</b> No, I am not calling them the 'Banu Haqim.' Especially when they are the furthest thing away from what Haqim actually stood for. Their new name is supposed to mean 'children of Haqim,' but they openly rejected worshiping him in order to cling to their mortal religions. Not only that, but they signed on with the Camarilla and became embroiled in vampire politics, which is completely against everything the clan was created to uphold!<br /> <br /> The Assamites were supposed to act as judges and protect mortals from the worst offenders among vampire society. NOT wage political power struggles and keep the vampires safe from mortal awareness!<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------<br /> <br /> The Anarchs are presented as being the closest thing to a &quot;good guys&quot; faction that vampire society has. Except that while the Camarilla has recruited Lasombra and Assamites, the Anarchs have recruited the Setites and Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> One clan deals in C.P distribution, and the other gave the Nazi's two thumbs up!<br /> <br /> These are supposed to be your heroes, fighting the good fight against vampire fascism!<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> Axing the Sabbat.... Fuck you, they were the only faction who were actually right about something. Camarilla denied everything, until the problem was knocking on their doorstep. The Anarch Movement was a disorganized mess of hypocrites, who were completely full of shit. And the Inconnu... well, even the writers had no idea what to do with them, so they just kind of dropped out of the story.<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> Thinbloods being able to join a clan through Diablerie, or become human by killing their sires.<br /> <br /> First of all, not all Thinbloods were Caitiff. They were still members of their clan, just very weak versions of them.<br /> <br /> Second of all, this potential to become human again has now rendered Golconda pointless. Why spend decades / centuries trying to achieve spiritual enlightenment, when you can just kill the one who made you? Preferably in their sleep, since you precious little day walkers can do that now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T06:05:49-08:00","id":1557723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1552686#post1552686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least the Hecata has Augustus being made into a sacrifice to seal the deal, which makes some sense as most of their enmity comes from him screwing everyone else. But it sure would pay off for this to be more carefully done and less effective than it seems to have been.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless I'm mistaken, it takes <b>50 years</b> of training as a mortal / ghoul, before you're approved for the embrace within Clan Giovanni.<br /> <br /> That is a hell of a long indoctrination process, for the clan of mafiosos to suddenly flip the switch and sell out their leader to a bunch of zombies they've never met.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, the Hecata weakness is another thing I ignore. The painful bite was specifically designed for the Giovanni, as punishment for their betrayal. As far as I'm concerned, all the other Clans of Death still look like animated corpses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T14:04:28-08:00","id":1557738,"title":"","content":"Like many things in the WoD the &quot;standard&quot; approval process for the Giovanni is more of a guideline than a law in practice. There's always a way to fast-track individuals that have clear potential, and slow down those that are being given a small chance to prove themself. It exists far more to keep the younger mortal members of the family in line than it has to do with any practical matters regarding training and indoctrination.<br /> <br /> Also, the Giovanni are the Clan of the Borgias (or at least the worst interpretations of their history as told by the Borgias' enemies), not just the Clan of mobsters (even if V5 didn't really help on this front). Beyond that, the history of the Italian mafia in the US shows how quickly such groups can fall apart once their &quot;code&quot; gets broken. One high-ish ranking member that knows enough and feels disrespected enough by those above them can lead to hundreds of mobsters in jail. There are a few dons that notoriously got overthrown precisely because their underlings saw far more money and power in making deals with the mobs of other ethnic groups than keeping the old school Cosa Nostra mindset about things. So that sort of move is hardly unprecedented in real world organized crime history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-19T06:50:00-08:00","id":1557757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1557723#post1557723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless I'm mistaken, it takes <b>50 years</b> of training as a mortal / ghoul, before you're approved for the embrace within Clan Giovanni.<br /> <br /> That is a hell of a long indoctrination process, for the clan of mafiosos to suddenly flip the switch and sell out their leader to a bunch of zombies they've never met.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, the Hecata weakness is another thing I ignore. The painful bite was specifically designed for the Giovanni, as punishment for their betrayal. As far as I'm concerned, all the other Clans of Death still look like animated corpses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I feel like it's understandable why Augustus' obsession with the Endless Night could eventually turn members of his inner circle against him. The Giovanni have spent an uncountable amount of power, money and souls towards it, and it's basically just a pipe dream. Best case scenario, the ritual won't work, Augustus will get angry and blame everyone but himself and then demand the family pour more souls, more power, more time.<br /> <br /> More likely the other clans will eventually find out what the Giovanni are up to and decide to wipe them all out. And in the worst case, the ritual succeeds, the Shroud between the living and dead falls and suddenly there are millions and millions of ghosts the Giovanni have spent centuries shitting on banging on the windows and breaking down the doors for a little payback. It's not too hard to imagine that if some of the capo's felt that taking out Augustus was the best option, they'd be willing to leave the doors unlocked and let some other vampires come in to take him out. Then, by the next night when everyone wakes up, Augustus is dead, there's some new guy in charge and everyone is either kissing the ring or dead. Of course if they knew what Lazarus and the Harbringers were up to, they might have preferred Augustus. <br /> <br /> The Giovanni might be a family, but at the end of the night they're vampires, and they're playing the Jyhad too, just like everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-19T10:17:43-08:00","id":1557759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1557738#post1557738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a few dons that notoriously got overthrown precisely because their underlings saw far more money and power in making deals with the mobs of other ethnic groups than keeping the old school Cosa Nostra mindset about things. So that sort of move is hardly unprecedented in real world organized crime history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is funny, because apparently the Giovanni were the wealthiest clan by far. Even more so than Ventrue and Lasombra.<br /> <br /> Not sure how you manage to pull off gaining a bigger bank account than the clan with ties to the Catholic church, but kudos to them for finding a way!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-19T10:33:10-08:00","id":1557761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1557759#post1557759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is funny, because apparently the Giovanni were the wealthiest clan by far. Even more so than Ventrue and Lasombra.<br /> <br /> Not sure how you manage to pull off gaining a bigger bank account than the clan with ties to the Catholic church, but kudos to them for finding a way!</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure?<br /> I mean while the Giovanni are masters of finance, banking, and ancient mercantile trade - they originated from the ancient Roman merchant family known as the Jovians (or Ioveanus), evolving into the Giovanni family by the Middle Ages - and they maybe rival the Ventrue in sheer liquid wealth, I don't think they are the wealthiest to be honest<br /> The Ventrue controlled finance, politics, and major industries through ancient wealth and elite mortal connections and focused their wealth on real estate and had a few thousand years of headstart<br /> <br /> The Lasombra as a Clan I don't think are super wealthy tho' , on the individual level, sure, but not as a whole clan<br /> <br /> Now the Followers of Set?<br /> They probably had deep coffers (not counting their sorcery to cheat a little) , connections and vice always sell well<br /> <br /> As a honorary mention I think the Tzimisce are suprisingly wealthy - Dragons love their Hoards you know<br /> The Grimaldi were the rivals of the Giovanni/Jovians and the Elders chose them to &quot;elevate&quot; to Ravenants because the Giovanni/Jovians were notoriously untrustworthy - they still high powered business moguls, the Zantosa are the debauched nobility and better yet, suppliers to the upper crust they drag down in their sin-filled lifestlye providing them and in the meantime securing blackmail material... a certain stein come in mind from the Ep kind who as a Zantosa is totally belivable<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-19T10:45:05-08:00","id":1557763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1557761#post1557761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you sure?<br /> I mean while the Giovanni are masters of finance, banking, and ancient mercantile trade - they originated from the ancient Roman merchant family known as the Jovians (or Ioveanus), evolving into the Giovanni family by the Middle Ages - and they maybe rival the Ventrue in sheer liquid wealth, I don't think they are the wealthiest to be honest<br /> The Ventrue controlled finance, politics, and major industries through ancient wealth and elite mortal connections and focused their wealth on real estate and had a few thousand years of headstart<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The difference with that, is the other clans don't share the same level of unity as the Giovanni. Oh, sure, they may have their internal hierarchies, but different companies are working towards different goals, with different agendas. Feudal lords were notorious for constantly picking fights with each other for any reason that mildly inconvenienced them.<br /> <br /> Giovanni, on the other hand, were an organized crime family. There may have been some competition within their ranks, but they were ultimately working towards a unified purpose. They had something to collectively focus their efforts and resources on. When one member of the clan made 250 million dollars, the entire clan made 250 million dollars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-19T19:09:58-08:00","id":1557770,"title":"","content":"Reducing the Giovanni to the &quot;crime family&quot; Clan is still going to get push back from me.<br /> <br /> But yes, the problem with the &quot;wealthiest&quot; Clan is that it's a meaningless concept. Wealth is a very complex and nebulous concept. How well a group can leverage wealth matters more than their theoretical net worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-19T20:48:23-08:00","id":1557772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1557770#post1557770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reducing the Giovanni to the &quot;crime family&quot; Clan is still going to get push back from me.<br /> <br /> But yes, the problem with the &quot;wealthiest&quot; Clan is that it's a meaningless concept. Wealth is a very complex and nebulous concept. How well a group can leverage wealth matters more than their theoretical net worth.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they were involved in anything besides criminal enterprises, please enlighten me.<br /> <br /> And to that, I mean the Giovanni clan. Not some divergent bloodline, like the Samedi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-20T02:30:28-08:00","id":1557774,"title":"","content":"The vast majority of the Clan - if one includes the mortal and ghoul members especially - are involved in legitimate trade and banking efforts. A few of the auxiliary families were explicitly brought into the fold to increase the Clan's mystic power by already being practitioners of mortal (not necessarily actual Numina) magic practices. Though all of the auxiliary families have some disturbing &quot;traditions&quot; (cannibalism, dealing in the illicit antiquities trade when they don't find actual mystic artifacts, etc.) that made them viable targets for recruitment, only one of the dozen detailed families that make up the Clan actually specializes in organized crime (rather lazily, the Sicilian one). <br /> <br /> As Shadeprowler already noted, the Giovanni started in ancient Rome as a family of merchants. For nearly two thousand years their MO has been using their abilities to control the spirits of the dead to get ahead in business. While the Clan has never shied away from bending or breaking the law when it comes to getting what they want as business folks (esp. when it comes to swaying politicians), crime has always been a tertiary endeavor after money and necromancy. Corruption and organized crime on the scale the main Clan tends to get involved with is because why not have another edge their rivals don't rather than the core focus on the Clan's enterprises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-20T07:54:00-08:00","id":1557779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1557723#post1557723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless I'm mistaken, it takes <b>50 years</b> of training as a mortal / ghoul, before you're approved for the embrace within Clan Giovanni.<br /> <br /> That is a hell of a long indoctrination process, for the clan of mafiosos to suddenly flip the switch and sell out their leader to a bunch of zombies they've never met.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, the Hecata weakness is another thing I ignore. The painful bite was specifically designed for the Giovanni, as punishment for their betrayal. As far as I'm concerned, all the other Clans of Death still look like animated corpses.</div> </div> </div> </div>The years and years before embrace/approval thing wasn't really a thing since at least Revised era, to note. The big intro story in the revised Giovanni clanbook centered around candidates for the embrace who hadn't gone through any such thing and it was not treated as abnormal that they hadn't. The idea, at least by that point, was more that embraces required anziani approval, and that such could itself take decades before they signed off if they were feeling picky about letting a clan member embrace anyone at all, meaning a given Giovanni might lose out on a desired protege or what have you to the vagaries of time, not that the embrace candidates were being groomed for 50 years or what have you. Branch/Subordinate Families like the Milliners wouldn't really even be possible to exist if that were the ongoing protocol.<br /> <br /> Obviously this is all pre 5th changes anyway, but essentially &quot;your given Giovanni pc had to have been trained for 50 years&quot; was not a conceptually required thing, certainly by that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-20T11:24:35-08:00","id":1557784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1557774#post1557774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The vast majority of the Clan - if one includes the mortal and ghoul members especially - are involved in legitimate trade and banking efforts. A few of the auxiliary families were explicitly brought into the fold to increase the Clan's mystic power by already being practitioners of mortal (not necessarily actual Numina) magic practices. Though all of the auxiliary families have some disturbing &quot;traditions&quot; (cannibalism, dealing in the illicit antiquities trade when they don't find actual mystic artifacts, etc.) that made them viable targets for recruitment, only one of the dozen detailed families that make up the Clan actually specializes in organized crime (rather lazily, the Sicilian one).<br /> <br /> As Shadeprowler already noted, the Giovanni started in ancient Rome as a family of merchants. For nearly two thousand years their MO has been using their abilities to control the spirits of the dead to get ahead in business. While the Clan has never shied away from bending or breaking the law when it comes to getting what they want as business folks (esp. when it comes to swaying politicians), crime has always been a tertiary endeavor after money and necromancy. Corruption and organized crime on the scale the main Clan tends to get involved with is because why not have another edge their rivals don't rather than the core focus on the Clan's enterprises.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One could argue those are merely fronts to hide their criminal activities. But very well, I'll cede your point.<br /> <br /> Every instance of the Giovanni I've come across in the past went with the vampire mafia aspect, so that's about the only depiction I was familiar with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-20T13:01:15-08:00","id":1557787,"title":"","content":"Yeah... so kinda getting back to the main topic of the thread... I do hate that pretty much every attempt in the books to explain the Giovanni as more than just the mafia Clan was undercut by two additions to the lore that made everything else about the Clan less unique. The good parts of their lore have always been there, but also get downplayed a lot because the mafia stuff is more iconic and distinctive.<br /> <br /> I do always wonder if the Giovanni lore would have been better presented if we'd seen things like Assassin's Creed Brotherhood, or the 2011 <i>The Borgias</i> show closer to when VtM was big. I know for myself the Clan didn't make much sense until I was reading about the Medici vs. Borgia feud for something else back in the 90s (also I was biased against the Giovanni at first because I started as a Dark Ages player and the Cappadocians were my favorite DA Clan so... finding out what they got replaced with didn't make for a happy younger me).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-21T08:18:01-08:00","id":1557804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1557787#post1557787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do always wonder if the Giovanni lore would have been better presented if we'd seen things like Assassin's Creed Brotherhood, or the 2011 <i>The Borgias</i> show closer to when VtM was big. I know for myself the Clan didn't make much sense until I was reading about the Medici vs. Borgia feud for something else back in the 90s .</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good question<br /> I think that was a bit of a filled niche so to speak<br /> Not counting the Danava with the addition of Persia from Mithras's line and the possible Egypt and Summer &quot;breed&quot; from Nefer-meri-Isis and Arakur of Ur... the Ventrue settled in the region and lived relatively quietly while it was ruled by the Etruscans. With a little side fiefdom with Artemis in Sparta, but after Sparta's fall, the rise of Rome was the Clan's time to shine<br /> Paired with a little hickup; Medon, untill his death was called &quot;God-King of the Aegean&quot; and ruled an island openly as God and treated his subject so poorly the mortals rebelled and destroyed him around 200 BC forcing his Clan to rethink they unlife<br /> Back to Rome, recognizing the mortals of Rome to be a proud and superstitious, Collat did not seek to rule the Romans directly or make himself a deity as vampires in the past had done, but influenced events from behind the scenes by collecting favors from the city's citizens. This system would later be refined by Camilla, childe of Collat, who replaced his sire and set about establishing political connections with the patrician families of Rome<br /> <br /> Then came the Dark Ages<br /> <br /> When Rome fell, most of the Ventrue elite abandoned the ruined city to establish new centers of power elsewhere.<br /> During the rise of the Merovingian dynasty, the Ventrue began infiltrating existing government as feudal lords, thus taking credit for the creation and expansion of the medieval feudal system.<br /> When the Holy Roman Empire was dispersed, the Ventrue tried to move their center of power to Italy again<br /> However, Rome was dominated by the Lasombra (as was much of the Church) so they had to establish centers of power elsewhere in Italy, in Venice, Milan, Genoa, and Firenze.<br /> Here, the Ventrue constantly opposed the Lasombra (and their proxies in the church and in Rome) in their quest for power, as their own early efforts had not succeeded.<br /> Posing as <b>kings and merchant princes,</b> the Ventrue expanded their influence across the Mediterranean through trade routes and crusades, thus becoming again a force to be reckoned with. During these times, many Ventrue were influenced by the laws of chivalry and personal honor.<br /> <br /> I think the Ventrue and the Lasombra already filled the Medici vs. Borgia feud (and everything you can throw in) and simply the Giovanni not had a place in that powerstruggle without becoming either or both parties pawns and bitches<br /> <br /> If you look this from the historical perspective, of course - putting aside, the Giovanni were designed to be two dimensional necromancer mafia members and only later editions expanded their history - they easly could be major players<br /> <br /> The Borgias' allies included powerful families like the Sforza and Colonna, foreign powers like Spain, and figures such as Niccol\u00f2 Machiavelli, who advised Cesare; their influence also extended through papal connections, notably Pope Callixtus III and Pope Alexander VI, - they were basically Team Lasombra<br /> The Medici family had many allies, crucial for their rise and rule in Florence, often secured through strategic marriages (like to the Cybo family), financial power (owing money to guild leaders), and political maneuvering (forming the Italic League with states like Milan) and they formed pacts with prominent families (Bardi, Altoviti, Tornabuoni, etc.) - they were technically Team Ventrue<br /> <br /> Vampire easly could have include the Givoanni Family as a Major player, rivaling the Borgias and the Medici - and possibly could have ended in a &quot;triumvirate&quot; of sort, and the area could have been rulled by the Borgia (Lasombra) - Medici (Venture)-Giovanni alliance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-22T14:51:26-08:00","id":1557841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1557723#post1557723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of, the Hecata weakness is another thing I ignore. The painful bite was specifically designed for the Giovanni, as punishment for their betrayal. As far as I'm concerned, all the other Clans of Death still look like animated corpses.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Giovanni weakness with the Cappadocian Discipline spread is particularly crippling. The Giovanni have Dominate along with great wealth and influence that allows them to overcome their painful bite.<br /> <br /> The Cappadocians didn\u2019t have any social Disciplines, which almost all Clans have. No Dominate, Presence, or Animalism. At least they had the Kiss and could hire a prostitute and bite her middle of intimacy and the next day she\u2019d just think that the orgasm was so great that she still feels weak a day after. The Hecata have no such option, it\u2019s harder for them to control minds and they have no Kiss to aid in feeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-22T16:40:32-08:00","id":1557843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1557804#post1557804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire easly could have include the Givoanni Family as a Major player, rivaling the Borgias and the Medici - and possibly could have ended in a &quot;triumvirate&quot; of sort, and the area could have been rulled by the Borgia (Lasombra) - Medici (Venture)-Giovanni alliance</div> </div> </div> </div>The original Clanbook: Giovanni was excellent in many ways, but it really screwed up popular understanding of the clan. Their original description in the Players Handbook made it very clear they were a rich merchant family from Venice, the Most Serene Republic, and one of the classic maritime republics of Italy. They were northern Italians who had a lot of inspiration from the legends of the Borgias (who were in fact Spanish nobles and not originally from Italy). &quot;Modern Day Borgias&quot; (as said by someone on this board once) is a cool concept.<br /> <br /> The clanbook, however, depicted them as mainly a southern Italian organized crime family. There was no real understanding of Italian history, and how the different families would fit into that. Huge fail. It really needed a different main narrator who didn't sound like he was a casting call reject from Goodfellas, and instead used him as a secondary narrator reflecting the perspective of the Putanesca family instead. It's OK if they sound like a goomba from New Jersey. No Venetian patrician family member is going to sound like that.<br /> <br /> There are huge differences between northern and southern Italians. Between the Venetian Republic and the rest of Italy. Between rich merchant families and crime families that come from humble origins.<br /> <br /> It's not that Clan Giovanni doesn't have some ties to organized crime. It does - that is what the Putanesca family is for. It's just that the vast majority of mortal stock is from &quot;respectable&quot; society (with lots of scandalous skeletons in the closet).<br /> <br /> In the chronicles I run, I have the &quot;Putanesca crime family&quot; be one of the Five Families of New York, and they are responsible for handling anything illegal that the Clan needs done. However, they are looked down upon by all the other families in the clan.<br /> <br /> Each of the mortal families of Clan Giovanni obviously served some kind of purpose. The Giovanni themselves were obviously an important family of Venetian patricians. They were rich and powerful within the Republic, but as Venetians they could only have limited influence outside of the Republic. The Rossellini were an aristocratic family of the Papal States like the Orisini, Collona, Borghese, and Conti. They were papal nobility and were influential in electing the popes. They obviously provided Clan Giovanni with a different kind of influence than the Giovanni mortal family could do. The Della Passaglia and Ghiberti provided the means for the clan to spread west and east during the Age of Discovery (and were probably families from other Italian cities) just like bringing in the non-Italian minor families allowed the Clan to expand away from the Mediterranean. The Putanesca probably weren't even important enough to embrace until the late 19th century after Italy was united, and a lot of previously brought in mortal families were no longer as useful as they had been when Italy was divided. They may have been long term pawns for a while, but probably weren't brought into the clan as vampires until relatively late. There's a lot less difference between most of the Italian families of Clan Giovanni now than there would have been before Italian Unification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-23T13:41:00-08:00","id":1557866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1557843#post1557843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The clanbook, however, depicted them as mainly a southern Italian organized crime family.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't really get that impression. There's a lot more about decadent nobility and legitimate business interests. The only real mentions of crime are the grave robing and murder which go with being vampire-necromancers. Plus, it's very much emphasised that this is a literal family rather than a gang that calls itself a family. I'm not saying there's nothing there, but it seems pretty limited, maybe there are references I'm not getting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There was no real understanding of Italian history, and how the different families would fit into that. Huge fail. It really needed a different main narrator who didn't sound like he was a casting call reject from Goodfellas, and instead used him as a secondary narrator reflecting the perspective of the Putanesca family instead. It's OK if they sound like a goomba from New Jersey. No Venetian patrician family member is going to sound like that. </div> </div> </div>I didn't think the narrator sounded that much like a mafioso, he just sounds like a tiresome '90s guy, not a 200 year old vampire. Personally, he kinda brought to mind Patrick Bateman from <i>American Psycho</i>. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Between rich merchant families and crime families that come from humble origins. </div> </div> </div>I suspect the issue is somewhat that there are some similarities in the kinds of personalised patronage networks the two ran. They can certainly sound similar.<br /> <br /> I do also wonder about the influence of <i>The Godfather</i> on this. The presentation of the Corleones feels a lot closer to patrician-nobility than it does to any actual mafia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-24T22:16:01-08:00","id":1557888,"title":"","content":"I really liked the 1st Edition Giovanni Clanbook, but I do agree that it leaned very heavily into Mafia flavor and stereotypes. Which I think is a valid aspect of the Clan, but I do think that the Clan is also so much more than just a Mafia family.<br /> <br /> Among the original independent Clans, they were all problematic in their own ways. I always thought that the Giovanni were the best of the independent Clans. The one that was the most original and creative and least dependent on an ethnic stereotype. I also think that the concept made more sense as a bloodline than an entire Clan. Maybe people involved with V5 thought the same thing and decided to make the entire Clan the Hecata and have the Giovanni be a bloodline within that Clan. Unfortunately, I don\u2019t think that the way they did it was very good and they missed out on a lot of interesting potential with not only the Giovanni but with other Cappadocian based bloodlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-25T08:51:23-08:00","id":1557899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1557888#post1557888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really liked the 1st Edition Giovanni Clanbook, but I do agree that it leaned very heavily into Mafia flavor and stereotypes. Which I think is a valid aspect of the Clan, but I do think that the Clan is also so much more than just a Mafia family.<br /> <br /> Among the original independent Clans, they were all problematic in their own ways. I always thought that the Giovanni were the best of the independent Clans. The one that was the most original and creative and least dependent on an ethnic stereotype. I also think that the concept made more sense as a bloodline than an entire Clan. Maybe people involved with V5 thought the same thing and decided to make the entire Clan the Hecata and have the Giovanni be a bloodline within that Clan. Unfortunately, I don\u2019t think that the way they did it was very good and they missed out on a lot of interesting potential with not only the Giovanni but with other Cappadocian based bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps that was the pitch of the sale back then. They had to follow the original 1st ed simple concept up to a point, but I admit the flair that the first Giovanni Clanbook has was extremely appealing. The Cappadocian were introduced two years earlier on '95 and recently been expanded on Vampire the Dark Ages on '96, a year before this Clanbook was released.<br /> <br /> Remember that when it came out, internet was just starting, we where recently getting to know music beyond what we could afford to buy or assist to live shows through Napster (or cassette bootleg trading if you were into that). The Godfather was THE mafia movie to see. Good Fellas, Casino also were there, even Innocent Blood, but one of the favorite was The Last Don (no very popular). This was the time when Buffy the Vampire Slayer TV (because our main reference was the '92 movie) recently came out (Spike didn0t existed yet). No Wikipedia, no Sopranos, no Breaking Bad, no Blade, no facebook, no social media, just emails every now and then (the &quot;@&quot; concept was beginning to integrate into us). Blockbuster was the main place to get anything beyond what was on TV. No Lord of the Rings. On historical research, Gobekli Tepe wasn't made public yet, and Catalhoyuk was known perhaps only to those who made a career in archaeology or history.<br /> <br /> Every time I read the old white-wolf books I have the follwing impression: &quot;they did an amazing job considering that there was NO internet when the game came out&quot; their research on history was VERY good. I always wanted to know the research process on how they got to write the books.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-25T10:44:44-08:00","id":1557901,"title":"","content":"I tend to work on the Assumption the Cappadocians were Carrion eaters in terms of feeding ecology, they even had a level 1 mortis ritual to make this easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-27T17:48:40-08:00","id":1557954,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the Hecata would make any attempts to replenish their ranks?<br /> <br /> From what I understand, Cappadocious was handing the embrace out like candy to anybody who was even vaguely interested in studying the mysteries of death. By the time he sealed them away, the Cappadocians were over 1,000 strong.<br /> <br /> As the only clan in 5th edition who has chosen to remain independent, they don't exactly have many allies they can draw upon in times of crisis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-27T22:58:55-08:00","id":1557960,"title":"","content":"They are not <i>really</i> a Clan if you think about it, more like a seperate Sect; coalition of Clans and bloodlines who practice necromancy and study death - and they will &quot;reproduce&quot; accordingily their origin<br /> The Giovanni and the satelite families I belive keep their individual traditions when it comes to Embrace, be it a Giovanni, a Dunsirn, Della Passaglia or Ghiberti or whatever they absorbed along the line or since the re-formation<br /> The Premascines of the Giovanni maybe start to finally boost their numbers?<br /> The Samedi the same; the Nasyon san an follow the Baron's orders<br /> The Lamia I belive not so different; there is <i>always</i> a Lamia, the head priestess who commands the Gorgons<br /> The Pisanob are almost became extinct , so refilling the ranks of the Children of Tenochtitlan probably a very priority to them<br /> To be honest I'm not sure the the Impundulu and the Mla Watu or Unhudo Drwoned Legacy are members, but if they are? They never been numerous and trying to survive probably in the night<br /> The Harbringers were always an oddball, the Sabbat Harbringers of Skulls not embraced a single new vampire since their arrival in the Skinlands , probably because Lazarus/Capuchin forbid it untill the last Harbringer is freed... but the Tal'mahe'Ra kin, however, have not felt so disinclined, and this faction's numbers, though small, have been growing quickly since the seal was broken. Such progeny, however, is seen as second rate unless it has spent several years in the Shadowlands.<br /> The few Cappadocian remnant - who joined - are another good question<br /> The Nagaraja again, if you take two versions are interesting, one part fled to Korea and was granted protection by the Green Court, provided that they would never sire. Another joined the Hecata - I don't thin kthey changed their strict selectiing method when it comes to Embrace<br /> <br /> So the real question is as you asked, would they even make any atempt to replenish the ranks (especially since their number are not necesarily growing, but shrinking since the Harbringers of Ashur have this habit of hunting other Hecata and quite good at it - The Lazerene Mask: The Harbinger incurs no Stains for killing another Hecata member, or anyone that serves the clan )<br /> <br /> I think they will not - or at least not any more than normally would Embrace<br /> The Hecata, as an &quot;organization&quot; don't really need allies if you think about it. The past ~500 years since the Camarilla and Sabbat formed these bloodlines stood alone, independent and <i>survived</i><br /> Now the Sabbat crumbled and the Camarilla become desperate enough to try the Ashirra merge (and I'm sure they eventually would try to reach ot for the Laibon) and the Anarchs are a joke as they always were - but if there is one constant it is Death<br /> I don't think any &quot;times of crisis&quot; would justify a waves of Embrace - even the Second Inquisition is not a porblem to them as Roger de Camden demonstrated you can play them like a fidle<br /> They have their local/regional or personal connenctions, boons and favors, ghosts and servants, influence and that is for them I think is enough<br /> Here and there could be a population boom, in secured cities like Venice or where the Hecata rules with bony fist but where the Camarilla have a strong presence or the Anarchs (or even Sabbat)? They don't need them. As long as they leave them alone I don't think the Hecata feel the urge to suddenly show why they are called the Clans of Death<br /> ...or untill the Caputchin trio decides it is time to show some teeth<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-28T19:41:45-08:00","id":1557974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1557954#post1557954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if the Hecata would make any attempts to replenish their ranks?<br /> <br /> From what I understand, Cappadocious was handing the embrace out like candy to anybody who was even vaguely interested in studying the mysteries of death. By the time he sealed them away, the Cappadocians were over 1,000 strong.<br /> <br /> As the only clan in 5th edition who has chosen to remain independent, they don't exactly have many allies they can draw upon in times of crisis.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's this thing with Cappadocius.<br /> <br /> On 1st and 2nd ed he was the big bad. Embracing Shaitan the main Baali (Moloch didn't existed yet) since Chaos Factor and Dark Ages Companion,.and Lazarus being Lameth in the Red Death trilogy. Then it got retconned in the Dark Ages Clanbook into something else, Revised changed things into Saulot being the progenitor of the Baali to retcon the Kuejin lore (my preferred one). I understand that there is no way to the Hecata to happen, no matter how well written BJD is. Yet, it happened, i'll go with the flow on this one.<br /> <br /> The thing with the Cappadocians have a before and after.<br /> Beofre, yes. After no. Ashur/Cappadocius/&quot;Sargon&quot;/Laodice sired only 6 childer: Caias, Japeth, Lazarus, Humuusa, Byzar and Augustus. He spoke with Zoroaster, Buddha, Nebuchadnezzar and Alexander the barbarian. The Feast of Folly (8th century aprox) changed everything. Since his first revelation during mythic Christ times, he was full death things, but then he changed, he was &quot;baptized&quot; by the angels and turned towards the Road of Heaven. Any mortal mind would assume he wasn't right in his mind.<br /> <br /> V5 made the gruesome mistake of handling Oblivion to Lasombra too, therefore creating an alternate timeline of everything white-wolf published during their golden age. Whatever they come up to, must explain the Lasombra under the same perspective of the Cappadocians of old.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-29T15:54:55-08:00","id":1557999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1557954#post1557954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if the Hecata would make any attempts to replenish their ranks?<br /> <br /> From what I understand, Cappadocious was handing the embrace out like candy to anybody who was even vaguely interested in studying the mysteries of death. By the time he sealed them away, the Cappadocians were over 1,000 strong.<br /> <br /> As the only clan in 5th edition who has chosen to remain independent, they don't exactly have many allies they can draw upon in times of crisis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also not to mention that the Feast Of Folly was Cappadiocous choice to cull the clan as they overtaxed the mortals residing in there fiefdom and was shocked by the number of people in his clan and how poorly chosen they were for the embrace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-29T21:18:50-08:00","id":1558010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1557999#post1557999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also not to mention that the Feast Of Folly was Cappadiocous choice to cull the clan as they overtaxed the mortals residing in there fiefdom and was shocked by the number of people in his clan and how poorly chosen they were for the embrace.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of his fault, for being so obsessed with his work that he effectively disregarded the screening process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-29T22:51:06-08:00","id":1558012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1558010#post1558010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's kind of his fault, for being so obsessed with his work that he effectively disregarded the screening process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Respectfully disagree<br /> I mean the only, the really only reason he only lifted a finger because the humans who lived with Cappadocians in Kaymakli complained and after he cheked it out, he found anemic humans, disease spread by the constant presence of corpses, and a society on the brink<br /> But was that really his or his child fault?<br /> I mean if you look closely, a Clan of Death should not be bothered by these things, more so would be interested, how Lamia was fascineted by a bloated corpse and studied it, the sloy decay, etc<br /> The presence of corpses only a problem - especially in an udnerground city with darn well water system and ventillation - if the humans constantly poking the said corpses<br /> The Cappadoican not just let them lying orund on the ground...<br /> Also Humans staying healthy and having a functional society usually are the &quot;job&quot; of the Humans - even of the Cappadoican were numerous, they literally had the basic ability to feed on dead blood, tho' probably their presence been taxing on the long run when it come to feed, but they were just scholars and prefered their little quarters where they studied the said corpses<br /> A whole &quot;Vampire&quot; part of the town - if the servants got sick, basic human survival instinck should have kicked in like in every society and simply quarantined them - we have historical record, in those times, while there were some outbreaks like Antonine Plague (165\u2013180 AD) what was likely caused by smallpox or measles, this outbreak devastated the Roman Empire, killing over 5 million people, including Emperor Marcus Aurelius or the Plague of Cyprian (c. 249\u2013262 AD), a severe pandemic, potentially smallpox or viral hemorrhagic fever, that caused widespread mortality and social disruption across the Roman Empire the humans were suprisingly healthy - evidence suggests that early medieval people (roughly 500-1000 AD) were often healthier, with stronger bones and better nutrition, than those in later, more crowded periods. While average lifespans were lower, thats true, around 60 years<br /> <br /> Beside, the Vampires have their own screenin process when it comes to progeny, that may differ from their sires, but usually they have a reason and select carefully - especically i na scholary clan and the traits of the Harbringers proves, they were not fools, or anything like that, not unworthy to the Blood<br /> Cappadocius had some strick points:<br /> <br /> Who among you cannot read or write? - this one is the only sane one, because you have to take notes, then again, recording ghosts and servants exist...<br /> Who among you has not helped build a church? - Scholars, not engineers, besides, not everyone are wealthy to help...<br /> Who among you does not follow the Via Caeli? - other Roads exist, even Cappadocius was a newbie on this one<br /> Who among you does not pursuit the answer to the great enigma? - What was the Great Enigma in HIS eyes, again?<br /> <br /> To be fair, the Feats of Foly not really made sense to begin with<br /> I mean the reasons and explanations<br /> <br /> And I think in this one we can't blame Cappadocius or any Cappadocian for the numbers; Embrace always have a reason, even if it is a fit of rage or passion or accident (but that is usually cleaned up, or ends up as a caitiff in somewhere else)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-11T22:45:18-08:00","id":1558252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1557738#post1557738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One high-ish ranking member that knows enough and feels disrespected enough by those above them can lead to hundreds of mobsters in jail. There are a few dons that notoriously got overthrown precisely because their underlings saw far more money and power in making deals with the mobs of other ethnic groups than keeping the old school Cosa Nostra mindset about things. So that sort of move is hardly unprecedented in real world organized crime history.</div> </div> </div> </div>And those other mobs are fools to place any degree of trust within those traitors.<br /> <br /> If they're willing to sell out their own families in order to secure more wealth and power, then they are guaranteed to sell you out as well, the moment a better deal comes along.<br /> <br /> They should have been disposed of the moment they were no longer useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-11T22:49:45-08:00","id":1558253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1558012#post1558012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless I'm mistaken, it was the Nosferatu who discovered the correlation between poor hygienic practices, and the spreading of disease. They even learned to weaponize it against their enemies.<br /> <br /> We're talking about the Dark Ages, when people thought illnesses were the work of evil spirits, and that the Black Plague was a punishment sent down by God.<br /> <br /> Or, if you want to get closer to the modern era, the belief in the four bodily humors. Which has been debunked since 1850.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-11T22:59:15-08:00","id":1558254,"title":"","content":"If you were driven by cold hard logic combined with a perfect ability of when to drop assets went they're no longer useful, and wanted to make maximum money at minimum risk, you'd work for a Wall Street firm, not be a mobster.<br /> <br /> Things like &quot;family,&quot; &quot;codes,&quot; &quot;loyalty,&quot; and whatever have always failed in organized crime compared to ambition, brutality, greed, and self-preservation. <br /> <br /> You can say what &quot;should&quot; have been done all you want to. That doesn't change what has happened in history with actual mobsters. The image that organized criminals want the public to get of them is rarely how things actually work on the ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-12T01:08:06-08:00","id":1558255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1558253#post1558253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless I'm mistaken, it was the Nosferatu who discovered the correlation between poor hygienic practices, and the spreading of disease. They even learned to weaponize it against their enemies.<br /> <br /> We're talking about the Dark Ages, when people thought illnesses were the work of evil spirits, and that the Black Plague was a punishment sent down by God.<br /> <br /> Or, if you want to get closer to the modern era, the belief in the four bodily humors. Which has been debunked since 1850.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes... and no<br /> It is a bit wonky and complicated<br /> What you wrote is true - but a bit later edition of the game<br /> Originally - when the Feast first popped up - it was the Clan of Death and the Baali who had the intimate knowledge of the plagues and diseases<br /> The <i>original</i> Mortis had a the Lvl 5 power called: <b>Black Death</b> - Infects its target with a virulent plague that kills mortals or puts vampires into torpor and a Lv8 variant, celled <b>Plague Wind</b> - Summon a deadly wind that steals the life from everything in the area (it was in form of a plague)<br /> The Lamia's bite carried disease, and developed their own Discipline, Deimos (based on the four humors) what was replaced with a Mortis path (the Path of the Four Humours) in the Dark Ages Storyteller Companion.<br /> <br /> The Baali, historically were famous for spreading disease and plagues - they had a few nice tricks for that and of course while Namtaru never awakened from his slumber, it is said he interact with the world through each of the 36 of his aspects, beings that are collectively known as Decani, the 36 demons of plague<br /> Actually while invoking the Decani, Nergal/Shaitan's childe, Hay-Tau, unleashed the black plague upon Europe... (and it was the aid of the Decani that it made possible for the Baali to place the Clan curse on the Banu Haqim)<br /> <br /> Back then it was a bit of a coin flip who the Baali prognitor was, and since it was comonly known as &quot;Ashur&quot; \u200ba name Cappadocius used (or others used to call him that) he was a very good candidate and this was a little nod to that - ultimately abandoned in favor of Saulot with a little side tangents<br /> <br /> So what you are saying is true, the Nosferatu indeed became expert of such underhanded tactics and defiled the water sources of a village if a local Cainite lord became too arrogant<br /> <br /> But in relation of the Feats of Folly and its reasons it is a bit irrelevant; Kaymakli and Derinkuyu were designed specifically as, and effectively functioning as, secure, self-contained refuges from plagues, invaders, and persecutions for centuries. While they were not necessarily free of the environmental hazards of living underground (such as mildew or dampness), they were highly advanced in sanitation and protection to keep inhabitants safe during long-term confinement.<br /> <br /> There is no exact date when the Feast of Folly\u200b happened, but occurred roughly in the early-to-mid Medieval period, generally cited as taking place before the embrace of Augustus Giovanni in 1005 CE. While some sources place it vaguely around the 7th century or during the plague of Justinian in 541 CE, it is widely accepted to have occurred prior to 711 CE. - it happened sometime between the 4th-century Christianization of the region and the 11th-century rise of the Giovanni, with many pointing to the 7th century as a likely, albeit unconfirmed, period.<br /> <br /> While around that time the prevailing belief across both Christian and Islamic worlds was that plague was a punishment from God for sins the leading medical theory, inherited from Greek and Roman medicine (Galen), was that plague was caused by &quot;miasma&quot;\u2014poisonous air or &quot;vapours&quot; created by rotting, stagnant water, or the corruption of the atmosphere.<br /> Despite not knowing about bacteria, people did observe that the disease moved along trade routes and, in some cases, accompanied the movement of rats on ships, particularly grain ships from Egypt and Nubia or from &quot;East&quot;<br /> Sure back then the biological source of the plagues was not understood in any scientific sense but the people knew not to poke rotting corpses, stay away from them don't drink, if it possible, contaminated water, etc<br /> <br /> My point is, the Cappadocian's presence and their studies couldn't be the cause of that culling (eg. people complained they became sick because of the many undead around)\u200b\u200b - logically<br /> Thematically? Eh, a bit shaky, but probably would hold<br /> <br /> That is why I said - <i>in my opinion</i> - the Feast of Foly not really made sense to begin with nor the reasons and explanation <i>why</i> Cappadocius culled his Clan\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-17T18:04:36-08:00","id":1558369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552676-what-lore-changes-did-you-hate-that-was-added-to-vtm?p=1557759#post1557759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is funny, because apparently the Giovanni were the wealthiest clan by far. Even more so than Ventrue and Lasombra.<br /> <br /> Not sure how you manage to pull off gaining a bigger bank account than the clan with ties to the Catholic church, but kudos to them for finding a way!</div> </div> </div> </div>Might be a reference to novel Dracula. Novel Dracula is called a necromancer, and does things like finding gold by watching for, irrc, mystic signs. Perhaps the necromancer clan is assumed to be the best at having ghosts lead them to buried treasure those ghosts will never need again. Just a guess.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}